{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick","id":966290,"title":"How technomancers see magick?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T09:55:02-07:00","id":966290,"title":"How technomancers see magick?","content":"So, technomancers don't believe in magick. They always have a good scientific explanation for everything. But they know that other traditions can make effects and they often look like magic, even though in the technomancers mind, it's just a trick.<br /> <br /> Also, almost all technomancer build and use devices to cast effects. How coule they explain a device working for them and not for a sleeper?<br /> If a technomancer builds a laser gun that all he habe to do is pull a trigger, how could it not work if a sleeper pull it? You know, a lot of devices don't require an &quot;enlightened mind&quot; specially those that were build with a sinple trigger. We do this all the time in real life, we don't have to know how electricity works to turn a switch and light the light bulb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:12:02-07:00","id":966299,"title":"","content":"Depends what kind of Technomancer they are.<br /> <br /> If they're an &quot;incorporating tech into my mystic stuff&quot; kind of technomancer, like a Hermetic mage that uses a calculator to make their charts an calculations. A Dreamspeaker that uses a flashlight to search for rifts in the gauntlet, or even a Cultist who uses elctrostimulation to give them the high they seek, then their paradigm is pretty much as it always was, they just have a few tech foci. Some of the more conservative members may think this is a bit perverse, but on the whole it's still mystic magic, just updated a little.<br /> <br /> If it's a &quot;Build my effects like a machine&quot; kind of technomancer, like your of-the-shelf Etherite and Virtual Adept, then it's not that they don't beleive in magic. Some may consider mystic magic as outdated, inefficient, and actually quite messy (especially with those Verbena people bleeding on everything, Yuck). Others might actually really admire mystics for doing magic they way that they do, but they themselves don't know how to invoke the same effects, so instead they build their effects the way they do understand it.<br /> <br /> The fundamental point combines all mages is that, at the end of the day, they are all will workers, even the Technocrats. They are all using their own force of will to shape the universe into what they see as &quot;correct&quot; or &quot;obvious&quot;. The only difference between the Technocracy and the Traditions is that the Technocracy found a way to do it so well that even sleepers can start to mess around with it.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Techomancer's foci, (tools if you're an M20 reader), the only reason their machines work is because they believe that they do. Anyone else who tries to use them would only be able to work them if they shared the same beliefs as the creator.<br /> <br /> How might a technomancer react if they see their machines used by someone else and simply not working? Simple, they'd say they're not doing it right, they haven't got the settings properly, the safety is on, the power's not plugged in properly, you're jamming it. Here let me do it!<br /> <br /> If the device was a Wonder, especially a Talisman, then that would be different, even Sleepers who understand the lore/science behind talismans can use them without need of being awakened.<br /> <br /> Technocrats have Enlightened Science which functions in the same way as magic. Some will be aware of how malleable reality is, so they will know that not everyone will be able to pull of their procedures without proper &quot;training&quot; first. Others would just consider these procedures too experimental to deliver consistent results, and thus require further development. There may come a point where these procedures become a part of the consensus, at which time they are no longer magic, but mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:20:35-07:00","id":966303,"title":"","content":"Are you saying that technomancers believe in magick?<br /> <br /> Also, let's day an etherite builds a laser gun to use his Forces sphere. It's just like a normal gun, pull the trigger and it shoots. But desdly laser instead of bullets. A sleeper takes his gun and pull the trigger. Nothing happens. What would the etherite thinks, since he doesn't know that it's his will that is making the effect and that's why the sleeper can't shoot. Considering the gun doesn't habe any &quot;setting&quot; to adjust, he just pull a trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:27:15-07:00","id":966311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966303#post966303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying that technomancers believe in magick?<br /> <br /> Also, let's day an etherite builds a laser gun to use his Forces sphere. It's just like a normal gun, pull the trigger and it shoots. But desdly laser instead of bullets. A sleeper takes his gun and pull the trigger. Nothing happens. What would the etherite thinks, since he doesn't know that it's his will that is making the effect and that's why the sleeper can't shoot. Considering the gun doesn't habe any &quot;setting&quot; to adjust, he just pull a trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some Etherites believe in magick, and will fully admit what they are doing is the next stage in magical development. Others may consider what they are doing to be True science, not that stuffy conservative stuff the Technocracy is trying to shove down everyone's throats, but rather the stuff that dreams are built on. Real Science with a sense of wonder, discovery, and awe! there are many competing theories within the Scientific community of Etherites, and while many debates are made over the subject with publishing in papers encouraged, there have been a number of duels started on such disagreements.<br /> <br /> As for this particular Etherite you mention, obviously the sleeper is an idiot! Either that or the gun's out of power or needs time to recharge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:33:52-07:00","id":966315,"title":"","content":"How can someone fail to pull a trigger? Also, the etherite would see that nothing wrong with the gun as soon as he gets it back. Maybe the etherite wouldn't know why it didn't work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:37:00-07:00","id":966316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966315#post966315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can someone fail to pull a trigger? Also, the etherite would see that nothing wrong with the gun as soon as he gets it back. Maybe the etherite wouldn't know why it didn't work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly! What kind of moron doesn't know how to use a Lightning gun!<br /> <br /> If, however, the Etherite was skilled enough with Prime, they'd be able to make the gun into a Talisman, then any Sleeper would be able to use it (and with much more success than the same Talisman that was a wand since more people would believe in a Lightning gun working than a Lightning wand).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-09-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:50:39-07:00","id":966327,"title":"","content":"It depends a lot on which faction the Technomancer belongs to, their Paradigm, and who they are surrounded by. Tradition technomancers have a party line to tow, that being that Reality is flexible and everyone's magick (or Science!) works. Many Etherites and Virtual Adepts likely just shrug, and assume their mystic colleagues are just weird, or exploiting weird facets of Science(!) that don't require the normal tools and techniques.<br /> <br /> Other Trad technos may incorporate this flexibility into their own personal Paradigms. Virtual Adepts believe that Reality is a system that can be hacked. One of them might assume, logically, that the mystic is simply using a different kind of method for hacking that same Reality. A different programming language, if you will.<br /> <br /> Etherites, by contrast, are prone to championing some pretty bizarre deviations from normal scientific thought. They are also known for being pulp-style adventurers, and the pulps didn't shy away from mixing science(!), mysticism, and raw grit and skill. Back in the pulp days, an adventurer might have trained with exotic mystics, especially in things like Yoga or Martial Arts. Others carry magical artifacts (amulets, statues, rings) that pulse with a mysterious energy. In both cases, an Etherite would likely assume there was some scientific explanation for why breathing exercises enhanced their physicality, why psychedelic drugs give them insight, or why the amulet is linked to some form of energy. These things are mysterious, but that's fine. A True Scientist sees mysteries as opportunities. Perhaps, once they've advanced their experiments sufficiently, they'll be able to develop a working theory explaining all the mumbo jumbo.<br /> <br /> Certain mystic groups have also given rise to technomancers. Hermetic House Thig, Dreamspeaker Ghost Wheel Society (and other Technoshamans), Chorister Alexandrian Society, Euthanatos Lhaksmists, etc. These groups are easily able to reconcile the miraculous with the scientific, as their practices freely mix the two. For them, what they do and what their more conservative colleagues do is merely two methods of interacting with the same fundamental magical theories.<br /> <br /> Technocrats have the hardest time of it, simply because their ethos brooks no superstitionist ideas. What the Technocracy does is not magic. There is no such thing. Inevitably, therefore, it causes some cognitive dissonance when a Technocrat agent faces off directly with a mystic mage, who proceeds to do the impossible with no apparent apparatus. When this happens, there are usually two outcomes (aside from conversion to Tradition thinking, of course). The first is that the agent starts asking their superiors and colleagues too many questions. This can be corrected quite easily by reminding the agent that superstitionist flights of fancy are Unmutual, and continued thoughts along those lines will necessitate reporting to Room 101 for correction. Sometimes, the Union will just skip the threats, and report them directly to Room 101. The conflict of ideas is no longer a problem, because the agent no longer remembers there being any inexplicable phenomenon.<br /> <br /> The other outcome is that the Technocrat does what humans (including you and I) do when confronted with cognitive dissonance: rationalize and deny. The mystics are obviously exploiting quirks in the physical laws that they don't understand, but have managed to &quot;master&quot; through centuries of trial and error. The Technocracy, meanwhile, has the benefit of the scientific method, so are able to understand and iterate on developments faster and more completely than the mystic (who, again, doesn't really know what they're doing). Alternatively, the Technocrat might assume that the mystic is a charlatan, using hidden tools of science to affect the image of a wizard. This, indeed, is a gratifying idea to Technocrats, who can feel a smug sense of superiority in the face of obvious hypocrites and liars. And that only the Etherites and the Virtual Adepts - former Technocrats themselves - are even slightly honest about what they're doing (not that they aren't still doing it wrong).<br /> <br /> Or the mystics could just be tapping into psionic potential. Which, while annoying in its vagueness, can cover a whole hell of a lot of what mystics do, in the eyes of the technomancer.<br /> <br /> As a Technocrat grows more experienced and familiar with their primary Enlightened competition, they either become more and more sure of their rationalizations, or begin to realize the truth. By then, however, they've spent their lives working loyally for the Union. They've long since tied their egos and values to the Union, and everything it stands for. So when the Technocrat finally realizes that Reality is mutable, and dependent on belief, they are able to rationalize further...as to why the Union (and its deceptions) are necessary. They've seen what the mystics do, recklessly imposing an unpalatable and dangerous Paradigm (or sets of Paradigms) onto everyone and everything they can get away with. Humanity needs to believe in a rational, rigid scientific world view. It's for their own good. Just as it's for their own good that the agents beneath them need to be kept in the dark about the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:49:15-07:00","id":966356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966315#post966315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can someone fail to pull a trigger? Also, the etherite would see that nothing wrong with the gun as soon as he gets it back. Maybe the etherite wouldn't know why it didn't work?</div> </div> </div> </div>How can my mother fail to keep her VCR from flashing &quot;12:00&quot;?<br /> <br /> Even &quot;hard science&quot; technomantic devices are the focus of extremely advanced scientific theories - so advanced that they are revolutionary to common thought, as far outside the realm of common human knowledge as mystic sigils and fireballs.<br /> <br /> I think it's a non-starter hypothetical: It's entirely feasible that you can't <i>make </i>a lightning gun so simple that it's really just a matter of pulling a trigger. There's configuration concerns and dials and gauges; enough complexity that it's not surprising that an unAwakened mind can't juggle all of them at once. It's no different than why <i>most </i>Sleepers can't unlock their chakras or use their latent psychic powers: it's intuitive once you know how to do it, even effortless, but getting someone to that point is quite difficult. If you had streamlined the science and simplified the interface to the point a Sleeper could understand it, it wouldn't be dynamic magic anymore - it'd be an Extraordinary Device or just, y'know, an object.<br /> <br /> Think of giving a normal rifle - a relatively straightforward device - to a caveman. Intuitively that's a point-and-click device, but you're neglecting that we're from a culture where mechanical objects are common and guns are known qualities. Could Thog intuit that the device was a weapon? Would he grasp it correctly? Could you explain to him why he needs to hold it just so? Simple concepts like ammunition (and that it can run out, and that Thog can't just put more metal rocks in the gun's &quot;mouth&quot;), that it's a tool and not an entity, etc. etc. all hinge on a fair amount of unacknowledged &quot;cultural&quot; knowledge about the world and its contents that Thog just doesn't have.<br /> <br /> Have you ever tried to walk a grandparent through using an internet browser, pointing out <i>exactly </i>what to do, and met with limited success, despite hands-on, explicit instruction? That's us, with the Ethertie's lightning gun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:00:31-07:00","id":966361,"title":"","content":"Bluecho, great post!<br /> <br /> Five Eyes, you failed to see my issue here. The sleeper operating the gun doesn't have to know how it works. Thog the caveman will firebthe rifle if he pullbthe trigger, even if accidentally. <br /> <br /> I agree that you could argue that no laser gun would be so simple as to pull a trigger and shoot. But the etherite could make this way. Even though there is a very complicated mechanism inside it, the trigger is enough to shoot, as the etherite do.<br /> Trying to answer my question, i believe the etherite would believe something failed in the gun inside mechanisms, even though he did shot right after the sleeper tried, leaving both with a big &quot;?&quot; face","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:12:13-07:00","id":966369,"title":"","content":"You don't even have to go as far as &quot;Give a Sleeper a simple Magick laser gun to try to fire.&quot; It is already very problematic for an Etherite when he considers that his laser guns malfunctions more often when Sleepers notice it's effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:17:41-07:00","id":966372,"title":"","content":"Charles Babbage was once asked by a Member of Parliament whether his engine would, if provided with <i>incorrect numbers, </i>provide the <i>right</i> answer.<br /> <br /> This is an obviously ludicrous question - to us. But why would a Member of Parliament in 1864 intuit that the device was performing math on provided figures and was not an &quot;answer-providing engine&quot;? When dealing with unfamiliar technology, there are actually an untold number of foundational assumptions that the creator and his or her ingroup have internalized - <i>paradigmatic </i>knowledge, in fact - that a naive user doesn't have and that a skilled user wouldn't immediately recognize as genuine knowledge.<br /> <br /> My point in saying &quot;It's entirely feasible that you can't <i>make </i>a lightning gun so simple that it's really just a matter of pulling a trigger.&quot;<br /> <br /> is that you <i>can't make a lightning gun so simple that it's really just a matter of pulling a trigger</i>. So when you say &quot;the Etherite <i>could</i> make it that way&quot; - well, no, see, that's not what &quot;can't&quot; means.<br /> <br /> It may <i>seem </i>that simple to a skilled operator, but that's because they're forgetting several preliminary steps, much as we might forget that Thog doesn't know that the firestick needs to be <i>loaded </i>first, or why your grandmother might be mystified as to why a typo in an email address causes the whole process to mysteriously fail.<br /> <br /> So the Sleeper pulls the trigger, produces nothing perhaps maybe a few measly sparks or a mechanical whine because, oops, they forgot to depress <i>this </i>or need to adjust for <i>that </i>or they fat-fingered safety button C over <i>here </i>and by they time you've corrected for those three errors they either have stumbled on operator errors four through six or, if they're anything like a grandparent with an email window, they'll keep doing one or the other because the process is actually more complex than a skilled user realizes and they haven't internalized all the correct behaviors.<br /> <br /> Seriously this is not a different concern than an Akashic having to deal with the fact that normal Sleepers can't meditate hard enough to heal their injuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 09-09-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:16:48-07:00","id":966430,"title":"","content":"Under the Technoparadigm, which includes the Virtual Adepts and some but hardly all Etherites...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick#post966290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, technomancers don't believe in magick. They always have a good scientific explanation for everything. But they know that other traditions can make effects and they often look like magic, even though in the technomancers mind, it's just a trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or deluded misapplication of genuine principles, or actual application of genuine principles which is being given further mystical 'significance' (see: hyperpsych versus Akashic self-discipline).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, almost all technomancer build and use devices to cast effects. How coule they explain a device working for them and not for a sleeper? </div> </div> </div>Non-Device technomagical foci have <i>incredibly shitty</i> user interface design or extreme personalization, you have to be an expert with super-intuition to use them.<br /> <br /> If you put in the time, effort, and resources to actually make it have not-shitty UI, well, then you have a Device and yeah a properly trained Sleeper can use it.<br /> <br /> Or it requires further things, like a psi-amp that... obviously won't work at all for anyone who isn't actively psychic or properly trained.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a technomancer builds a laser gun that all he habe to do is pull a trigger, how could it not work if a sleeper pull it? You know, a lot of devices don't require an &quot;enlightened mind&quot; specially those that were build with a sinple trigger. We do this all the time in real life, we don't have to know how electricity works to turn a switch and light the light bulb. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's <i>after</i> all the work to get the interfacing right and make the sleepertech &quot;just work&quot;. And how much of the stuff is behind-the-scenes, like the power grid needed to make the light bulb not burn out from current fluctuations constantly?<br /> <br /> Again, if a mechanism is sufficiently simple and intuitive to use that any Joe on the street could use it, it's either individually gone through the needed effort to make it a proper Device (like the laser gun which requires no Enlightened maintenance, intuition, nor configuration)... or it's Consensual.<br /> <br /> If your laser gun genuinely only requires a pull of the trigger, and not fiddly adjustments beforehand (which the Mage could admittedly do to give the gun a very temporary 'charge' of 'able to shoot things' under the right paradigms), then you have just described a Device. If you then assert that no, it's just a thing the Etherite made... well, then you're just being silly and deliberately positing a self-contradictory situation. If it should be usable by Sleepers, you need to actually use the systems for &quot;make this thing usable by Sleepers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:44:29-07:00","id":966500,"title":"","content":"One issue that a Technomancer will face is that their tools have to be specially calibrated before each time that they are used (Devices are sufficiently forgiving that they do not require calibration with each use). Now, that being said, there is no reason why a properly calibrated tool could not be used by a Sleeper, as the Technomancer is casting the spell for the Sleeper, even though the Sleeper is that one pulling the trigger (a highly skilled Technomancer could use a Time effect to maintain calibration for an extended amount of time, allowing a Sleeper the benefits of their tools).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:47:27-07:00","id":966521,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6072_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6072\" data-vbnamecard=\"6072\">Quantumboost</a> Excellent explanation. I was begining to think that devices would be required.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a> Yes, I guess this would happen with any Tradition, but it's easier for the Akashic to explain &quot;He's not clearing his mind properly&quot; than technomancer/technocrats that have their instruments external.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:09:44-07:00","id":966550,"title":"","content":"The sad thing is that in the end none of you are actually answering the question. This is a major logical problem in mage and especially with the purple paradigm where all mages are really doing is using there will to shape reality. The problem is that mage has moved beyond that in a number of respects. The purple paradigm is far too biased to thought processes like OoH. When it comes to technomancers who view science and technology as how the world works and they build something that only needs the push of a button to work then it should work regardless of who presses that button. So when it doesn't work when a sleeper presses the button then that should start raising questions for the technomancer in question. It is especially the case with something where the technomancer would want it to have the simplest interface as possible such as a laser gun for when combat happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 09-10-2016, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:54:11-07:00","id":966570,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that not all technomancer machines are single-function. That lightning gun might have variable power levels, range modifiers, adjustable spread, etc. If the scientist wanted to set off an EMP burst to short out local electronics, he needs buttons or knobs for that. Need to charge a piece of metal into a magnet? That requires further fiddling with controls. And if you wanted to stick wires on it and use it as a portable generator, all the more functions need to be applied for.<br /> <br /> The lightning gun having just a point and trigger interface presumes that the gun only has the one thing it can do: shoot a bolt of lightning as hard as it can. But Etherites (and Virtual Adepts and Technocrats) are inventive people, and love their flexibility. It makes sense that, if they spent many hours designing, building, and testing a machine, that they'd want to cram as much variability in as they could. Hell, testing alone may necessitate that the scientist be able to see how their machine works at very amounts of power. They stick a dial on there to allow them to go from high to low voltage, and bam! The scientist can just keep the dial, and they've got a more flexible tool. Or they are so impressed by their genius, that they don't bother modifying the gun to take that function out. And when that dial could allow them to switch from a taser function (&quot;Stun&quot;), to man melter (&quot;Unlimited...POWER!&quot;), it makes perfect sense to keep it.<br /> <br /> This often leaves such machines - usually prototypes - in a state where the inventor knows perfectly well how to make it do whatever he wants, but a Sleeper can't make heads or tails of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:19:45-07:00","id":966625,"title":"","content":"That still doesn't change the fact that it is still a logical flaw for the setting. Sure a prototype might be like that but it wouldn't take long for a mage to want to simplify it to something that would be user friendly. Before you say that that is what Devices are for, that causes it's own problems. A mage needs to be an adept in prime in order to make anything that will last more than a single use which in canon are supposed to be rare. From a game balance point of view that can make sense but from the narrative point of view where inventing, building, and improving technology is the very bases of a technomancer's paradigm then it stops making logical sense unless you start performing mental jumping jacks on order for it to fit in with the game rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:08:32-07:00","id":966648,"title":"","content":"I would allow Technomancers to invest Quintessence in their tools to allow their tools to be used by Sleepers. Each point of Quintessence would allow one use by a Sleeper. When the Quintessence runs out, the tools runs out of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:19:08-07:00","id":966674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966550#post966550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when it doesn't work when a sleeper presses the button then that should start raising questions for the technomancer in question. It is especially the case with something where the technomancer would want it to have the simplest interface as possible such as a laser gun for when combat happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't think so.<br /> Remember that the Technocracy *DOES* believe that the Consensus shapes what works and what doesn't. Heck, they are trying to shape the Consensus nonstop in turn. It's how they 'won' the Ascension War. They actively make use of the fact. *How* they explain the effects of the Consensus varies, but it's a truckload of scientific Star Trek style techbabble that an unenlightened mind clearly can't comprehend.<br /> <br /> So when a sleeper presses the button and nothing happens, the reason is clearly that the device is not ready for prime time yet, and the Consensus is preventing it to work in sleeper hands unless operated by an Enlightened Operative. It will be okay once the Time Table determines that the situation is right to introduce the technology to the masses.<br /> <br /> Technology that the consensus embraces starts working for everybody. Easily. And it becomes easily producable, too.<br /> See: Everyday technology that's normal *now*, which once was horrendously Magickal in the Mage sense, would have been having EXACTLY the same problems: Not working at all or Statistical Inevitability of horrendous failure. Now sleepers use it to drive at 70 miles an hour across the landscape.<br /> <br /> A Device is specifically built and adjusted to work under any circumstance, but it still has a statistical inevitability of failure until the technology is fully integrated into the Consensus.<br /> <br /> (And yes, that also means if sleepers started believing in the paradigms of mythical magick on a global scale, there would be a time when they would accept amulets that let you move items with mere thought, and said amulets would become everyday sleeper utensils that are producable with mundane means. The game, analog to our RL culture, just presents us with the Technocratic outcome so far.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-10-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T03:22:37-07:00","id":966686,"title":"","content":"This logical inconsistency is the biggest difference between the technocracy an the technomancers. In fact, this is one of the reasons why a lot of technocrats can't stand working with etherites. None of their stuff works the moment the Etherite leaves the room, but he's so good damn oblivious to this, or outright dismissive that working with him on his devises to make them more consensus friendly is a chore.<br /> <br /> This is what makes Etherites mystics at their core. Yes their focus is science, but it's a form of confirmation bias rather than investigative analysis. They don't try to discover what works and doesn't work within the confines of reality like most sleeper scientists would. They have a theory, often this theory has little to do with consensual reality, and their work is all about applying their theory to as many things as possible.<br /> <br /> One Etherite might have the theory that the universe is a giant clock, so all they need to is insert the correct gears into the correct configuration in order to wind up or down certain aspects of the universe. Thus they make clockwork contraptions which do exactly that.<br /> Why don't they work when another uses these devices? Fundamentally because the other does not see the universe as a giant clock. But if displayed with this information, they will not think &quot;hmm, my theory might be incorrect&quot; but rather &quot;well, they work for me, so the theory must have merit&quot;<br /> <br /> Etherite scientist who are aware of the shifting consensus, however, might be a bit more understanding about the limits of their personalised theories, but by that poit, they've already invested far to much time and effort into them to hen go and decide it was all meaningless.<br /> <br /> From the technocratic point of view, Etherites are mystics, and one promotion the value of steam power for time travel is just as damaging as a verbena who promotes homeopathy for curing cancer. They both do not work outside of the mages observation, but te mage is far too arrogant to even consider this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:21:16-07:00","id":966699,"title":"","content":"The Sons of Ether are believers of pseudoscience. While their Genius allows their Procedures to work for their own purposes, their inferiority is found in the non-generalizability and non-replicability of their Procedures. If they practiced Science, their Procedures could be used by the Masses when their Procedures stopped being Experimental (only useable by Enlightened Citizens) or Emergent (only useable by Extraordinary Citizens).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:11:18-07:00","id":966760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966699#post966699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sons of Ether are believers of pseudoscience. While their Genius allows their Procedures to work for their own purposes, their inferiority is found in the non-generalizability and non-replicability of their Procedures. If they practiced Science, their Procedures could be used by the Masses when their Procedures stopped being Experimental (only useable by Enlightened Citizens) or Emergent (only useable by Extraordinary Citizens).</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, when and how to things stop being &quot;exerimental&quot;? How does a procedure go from being an actively vulgar act of awakened magic/science at mundane effects that any sleeper and their dog can do? You can't just say &quot;because the consensus believes it works&quot; either as that would only negate paradox, a focus or wonder that requires arete would still require arete to function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:48:35-07:00","id":966776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966674#post966674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I don't think so.<br /> Remember that the Technocracy *DOES* believe that the Consensus shapes what works and what doesn't. Heck, they are trying to shape the Consensus nonstop in turn. It's how they 'won' the Ascension War. They actively make use of the fact. *How* they explain the effects of the Consensus varies, but it's a truckload of scientific Star Trek style techbabble that an unenlightened mind clearly can't comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately this goes back to the purple paradigm issue I stated before. When mages are fully aware of the consensus and that magic is based on beliefs then it makes the whole paradigm aspect hollow. Mage as a game has realized this problem and has made efforts to go away from that line of thought. With the purple paradigm technocrats simply like their magical trappings more and it makes it harder on more mystical mages. Nowadays however they don't believe that reality is consensual because that would fly in the face of what they believe in (the closest they have to a consensus now is the void engineers theory where each mind adds calculations to the great computer that is the universe) they believe that science and technology are the means for understanding and controlling the world around them. So that gets me back to my point of technomancers or technocrats at the least would make technology in such a way that it can be used for anyone to use regardless of if they are enlightened or not even if it requires a little instruction beforehand. It's a lot easier to learn how to use unfamiliar technology than it is to create and build it. Otherwise you have to start making justifications for it to fit with game rules like you &quot;it isn't primed yet&quot; one. Mystical mages (mostly) don't have this problem because they have inbuilt reasons that actually can better justify the lack of sleepers being able to do what they do. Lack of enlightened Will for OoH, not able to properly clear their mind for AB, not in tune with the spirit world for DS etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 09-10-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:46:40-07:00","id":966796,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4178\" data-vbnamecard=\"4178\">stanlemon</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> As much as I agree that explaining this issue with Device &quot;could&quot; solve it, stanlemon is completely right. And that's what my question was all about from the beggining.<br /> You guys came with a lot of made up explanations that wasn't part of the question. Talking about UI and things like that, that have nothing to do with the question.<br /> <br /> So, my conclusions are the following:<br /> <br /> - If the etherite knows the purple paradigm, which is an issue itself for technomancer, because why the fuck he's building so complicated things to do effects that can be done only with his Will and maybe some simple instrument to help concentrate?. Ignoring this, if he knows the purple paradigm, then he will understand why the device didn't worked, but again, then he would rethink all his paradigm, or simply isn't a technomancer.<br /> <br /> -If the etherite/technocrat doesn't know the purple paradigm, then he will have no clue why his laser gun, or any instrument he uses, it doesn't even need a trigger and that would make it even worse,<br /> . Like glasses to see other dimensions beings (Umbra) or earphones to hear radio signals directly into his mind. In this case the sleepers couldn't see the Umbra, then the etherite/technocrat takes it and do see the Umbra. He'll go &quot;WTF?!. Something must be wrong with my glasses&quot; then he takes a look and see that's nothing wrong with his glasses. The same continues to happen, Everyone in his Tradition/Convention can see the Umbra and every sleeper can't. This would make him believe that there is something about the user interfering with the results. His theory is therefore somewhat failed and must be revised...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:23:54-07:00","id":966814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966299#post966299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might a technomancer react if they see their machines used by someone else and simply not working? Simple, they'd say they're not doing it right, they haven't got the settings properly, the safety is on, the power's not plugged in properly, you're jamming it. Here let me do it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can sympathize with technomancer, as this is what regularly happens when someone near me try to use Excel and Power Point... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T11:40:29-07:00","id":966846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966814#post966814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can sympathize with technomancer, as this is what regularly happens when someone near me try to use Excel and Power Point... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excel and powerpoint aren't so simple as a switch turn on/off. What would you think if said person hit enter and Excel didn't go to the lower cell? Then you chek if anything is wrong and it isn't. Then you hit enter and it selects the lower cell. Then that person hits it and nothing happens. You'd think some bug or something's worng with the program or PC. But if you are the creator of Excel and see this happening after checking every bit of code and hardware you're going to give up and don't know why this is working (probably) or begin a huge investigation and theory of why it doesn't works for certain people, which might change everything you believe about programming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:25:40-07:00","id":966892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966356#post966356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can my mother fail to keep her VCR from flashing &quot;12:00&quot;?<br /> <br /> Even &quot;hard science&quot; technomantic devices are the focus of extremely advanced scientific theories - so advanced that they are revolutionary to common thought, as far outside the realm of common human knowledge as mystic sigils and fireballs.<br /> <br /> I think it's a non-starter hypothetical: It's entirely feasible that you can't <i>make </i>a lightning gun so simple that it's really just a matter of pulling a trigger. There's configuration concerns and dials and gauges; enough complexity that it's not surprising that an unAwakened mind can't juggle all of them at once. It's no different than why <i>most </i>Sleepers can't unlock their chakras or use their latent psychic powers: it's intuitive once you know how to do it, even effortless, but getting someone to that point is quite difficult. If you had streamlined the science and simplified the interface to the point a Sleeper could understand it, it wouldn't be dynamic magic anymore - it'd be an Extraordinary Device or just, y'know, an object.<br /> <br /> Think of giving a normal rifle - a relatively straightforward device - to a caveman. Intuitively that's a point-and-click device, but you're neglecting that we're from a culture where mechanical objects are common and guns are known qualities. Could Thog intuit that the device was a weapon? Would he grasp it correctly? Could you explain to him why he needs to hold it just so? Simple concepts like ammunition (and that it can run out, and that Thog can't just put more metal rocks in the gun's &quot;mouth&quot;), that it's a tool and not an entity, etc. etc. all hinge on a fair amount of unacknowledged &quot;cultural&quot; knowledge about the world and its contents that Thog just doesn't have.<br /> <br /> Have you ever tried to walk a grandparent through using an internet browser, pointing out <i>exactly </i>what to do, and met with limited success, despite hands-on, explicit instruction? That's us, with the Ethertie's lightning gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on the first comment. For an example, take a look at the &quot;Memory TV&quot; invention in Meet the Robinsons. Of course it can show people's memories, IF you know this really counter-intuitive way to set the dials, turn the knobs and push the buttons in exactly the right sequence (which might change depending on the situation... the memory was always supposed to to be the user's &quot;best&quot; memory, so it would probably take some additional modifications to get any other type of memory...) <br /> <br /> As far as the &quot;Caveman and the Gun&quot;. Absolutely not. A gun is REALLY simple. A &quot;caveman&quot; (for whatever value that term has... Neanderthal? Paleolithic hunter? Dweller in the underground cities of Cappadocia?) knows all about aiming at things and hitting them. Handing someone who had no idea of modern technology but who knows how to use an atl-atl and with a little bit of non-verbal communication, a couple of attempts, and &quot;Thog&quot; will be nailing shots right left and center. This was proved again and again all over the world when guys with guns (usually Europeans) showed up in areas with people who didn't have them. Usually the gun-disadvantaged will start seeking out firearms as they are hella good at doing damage easily and quickly. If they don't, it's not because they don't &quot;get&quot; guns. It's because they don't want them (resisting acculturation usually). <br /> <br /> As to whether &quot;Thog&quot; would know it's a weapon, that's a separate question and isn't really in the remit of the discussion. The initial condition wasn't &quot;the norm finds a lightning gun in a trash can&quot;, it's the creator handing it off. &quot;Thog&quot; might not know it's a weapon from first principles, but he's not going to be stupid about it once he knows what it can do. <br /> <br /> Hand &quot;Thog&quot; a cell phone and see what happens. Hells, hand one to Da Vinci, or Isaac Newton, etc. That's a better example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:52:45-07:00","id":966910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966550#post966550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sad thing is that in the end none of you are actually answering the question. This is a major logical problem in mage and especially with the purple paradigm where all mages are really doing is using there will to shape reality. The problem is that mage has moved beyond that in a number of respects. The purple paradigm is far too biased to thought processes like OoH. When it comes to technomancers who view science and technology as how the world works and they build something that only needs the push of a button to work then it should work regardless of who presses that button. So when it doesn't work when a sleeper presses the button then that should start raising questions for the technomancer in question. It is especially the case with something where the technomancer would want it to have the simplest interface as possible such as a laser gun for when combat happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A device that works by pressing a button is some form of wonder. The problem is really how people portray technomantic stuff. A technomantic sensory effect should be a complicated screen of numbers and gages the sleeper looks at and is all &quot;I have no idea what this mean&quot; the technomancer who lacks that sphere looks at it and is &quot;I have no idea what this means&quot;. The lightning gun is a bad example.<br /> <br /> Lets us real guns as an example. The &quot;magic&quot; of making a bullet isn't when you pull the trigger, its way back when the the powder was mixed and the bullet was machine tooled. We could also include the gun itself as part of the extended technomantic &quot;ritual&quot;. The Technomancer performs the extended gun ritual in his sacred space(workshop) and that ritual will have a number of successes to determine how many times the effect can be used before it stops working and how long it lasts. So the Technomancer has cast a ritual for 6 shots that last for a month, shots go off when trigger is pulled.<br /> <br /> If they don't have the spheres to do this they shouldn't be making &quot;guns&quot; any more than a sleeper who lacks gunsmithing skills should be making guns. Spheres and Arete matter just as much in the &quot;Purple Paradigm&quot; as anything else people seem to keep missing that for the &quot;BELIEVE BELIEVE&quot; your character still needs the spheres to do make shit not just their raw belief.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:57:54-07:00","id":966912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966892#post966892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the &quot;Caveman and the Gun&quot;. Absolutely not. A gun is REALLY simple. A &quot;caveman&quot; (for whatever value that term has... Neanderthal? Paleolithic hunter? Dweller in the underground cities of Cappadocia?) knows all about aiming at things and hitting them. Handing someone who had no idea of modern technology but who knows how to use an atl-atl and with a little bit of non-verbal communication, a couple of attempts, and &quot;Thog&quot; will be nailing shots right left and center. This was proved again and again all over the world when guys with guns (usually Europeans) showed up in areas with people who didn't have them. Usually the gun-disadvantaged will start seeking out firearms as they are hella good at doing damage easily and quickly. If they don't, it's not because they don't &quot;get&quot; guns. It's because they don't want them (resisting acculturation usually).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Its no where near that simple. various muzzle loaders are pretty intuative but modern fire arms? People who don't know what a safety is or hold the gun wrong etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:10:30-07:00","id":966916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966550#post966550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sad thing is that in the end none of you are actually answering the question. This is a major logical problem in mage and especially with the purple paradigm where all mages are really doing is using there will to shape reality. The problem is that mage has moved beyond that in a number of respects. The purple paradigm is far too biased to thought processes like OoH. When it comes to technomancers who view science and technology as how the world works and they build something that only needs the push of a button to work then it should work regardless of who presses that button. So when it doesn't work when a sleeper presses the button then that should start raising questions for the technomancer in question. It is especially the case with something where the technomancer would want it to have the simplest interface as possible such as a laser gun for when combat happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. 100% this.<br /> <br /> When Technomancers became playable and then again, when our players started choosing to play them, this whole &quot;Technocracy says there is no magic&quot; had to get kicked out the door, on its ass, into the gutter and get run over by a mack truck. <br /> <br /> Effectively, this requires a paradigm all it's own - &quot;The Technocracy is willfully stupid in a way that makes their objectives much much harder than they otherwise would be&quot;. Effectively, Room 101 would require a revolving door and every time a Technocrat encounters any sort of supernatural manifestation, they would need to be brain-raped back into drooling idiots. Which becomes impossible when you consider that most Conventions actually have a division or sub-group (if not a Methodology) that is all about &quot;protecting Humanity FROM the supernatural&quot; in whatever particular form that might take. That's a cognitive dissonance it's just not possible to encompass. <br /> <br /> &quot;What's our mission in their division?&quot; says the new transfer. <br /> &quot;We hunt PLEs&quot;<br /> &quot;What's that&quot;<br /> &quot;Post Life Entities&quot;<br /> &quot;Still not tracking&quot;<br /> &quot;The non-physical psychic remnants of the deceased. They exist largely in an adjacent dimension with a higher entropic coefficient.&quot;<br /> &quot;So what do they do?&quot;<br /> &lt;Insert description of such activities&gt;<br /> &quot;You mean... they're ghosts?&quot;<br /> ALL BRAINS IN THE ROOM SHORT-CIRCUIT. (Since EVERY Technocrat knows ghosts are &quot;magic&quot; and don't exist.)<br /> A door opens up and Room 101 tenders wheel in gurneys, load the agents onto them and wiskthem away for their 4th brainwashing of the day....<br /> <br /> The replacement is oh so easy. The Union knows what magic is and what mystics do. They know they do the same thing. They know that THOSE guys are doing it all wrong. They are unsafe. They are like handing plutonium to high school students to build A bombs as science fair projects. WE (the Union), do it the right way, the safe(-er/-ish) way, and we do it for the right reasons for the ultimate benefit of all humanity (instead of personal aggrandizement or the desire to monkeywrench the world back into the Dark Ages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:49:31-07:00","id":966931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966916#post966916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. 100% this.<br /> <br /> When Technomancers became playable and then again, when our players started choosing to play them, this whole &quot;Technocracy says there is no magic&quot; had to get kicked out the door, on its ass, into the gutter and get run over by a mack truck.<br /> <br /> Effectively, this requires a paradigm all it's own - &quot;The Technocracy is willfully stupid in a way that makes their objectives much much harder than they otherwise would be&quot;. Effectively, Room 101 would require a revolving door and every time a Technocrat encounters any sort of supernatural manifestation, they would need to be brain-raped back into drooling idiots. Which becomes impossible when you consider that most Conventions actually have a division or sub-group (if not a Methodology) that is all about &quot;protecting Humanity FROM the supernatural&quot; in whatever particular form that might take. That's a cognitive dissonance it's just not possible to encompass.<br /> <br /> &quot;What's our mission in their division?&quot; says the new transfer.<br /> &quot;We hunt PLEs&quot;<br /> &quot;What's that&quot;<br /> &quot;Post Life Entities&quot;<br /> &quot;Still not tracking&quot;<br /> &quot;The non-physical psychic remnants of the deceased. They exist largely in an adjacent dimension with a higher entropic coefficient.&quot;<br /> &quot;So what do they do?&quot;<br /> &lt;Insert description of such activities&gt;<br /> &quot;You mean... they're ghosts?&quot;<br /> ALL BRAINS IN THE ROOM SHORT-CIRCUIT. (Since EVERY Technocrat knows ghosts are &quot;magic&quot; and don't exist.)<br /> A door opens up and Room 101 tenders wheel in gurneys, load the agents onto them and wiskthem away for their 4th brainwashing of the day....<br /> <br /> The replacement is oh so easy. The Union knows what magic is and what mystics do. They know they do the same thing. They know that THOSE guys are doing it all wrong. They are unsafe. They are like handing plutonium to high school students to build A bombs as science fair projects. WE (the Union), do it the right way, the safe(-er/-ish) way, and we do it for the right reasons for the ultimate benefit of all humanity (instead of personal aggrandizement or the desire to monkeywrench the world back into the Dark Ages).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh... That's a rather extreme way of looking at it. The Technocracy are just like the Traditions in terms of Will equals Effect. Similarly they are just like each Tradition in that every single mage beleives what they are doing is the only &quot;real&quot; form of magic, those with methods that are close are kinda there, but those with completely contradictory methods are just plain wrong. If a Spirtual Dreamspeaker and an Techi Etherite talk, Neither of them will consider what the other one is doing is actually all that effective compared to their own techniques. The Dreamspeaker would think that the Etherite was just making a lot of things up on the spot, making a lot of noise and talking a lot of nonsense about science and machines. Sure the effect will be palpable, put the Dreampeaker wouldn't really see a difference between them an any other scientist. The Etherite would, funnily enough, think pretty much the same thing about the Dreamspeaker, that they're babbling on about spirits and mystic stuff, and harp on about old superstitions that don't really have much merit to them. Sure they can see the effects they produce, but to them it's unreliable and wishy-washy. There's nothing these guys do with their houdou vodou that can't be done better and more reliably with a good machine!<br /> <br /> The same it true with the technocrats. Sure they observe the effects of the reality deviants. and acknowledge that they are able to do quite astounding things. But where the Traditions go wrong is by trying to claim all of it is mystical. They say that the spirits are helping them, that it's all in between the numbers, that it's about changing the universal source code, or whatever flimsy explanation they might have. The fact that none of their explanations line up even with fellow members of the same tradition is just proof that everything they're saying to explain their effects is just nonsense. Sure the magic is potent, but these mystics don't understand what they're doing any better than a Sunday driver understands the inside of their own car.<br /> <br /> That is what set's the Technocratic Union apart from the rest of them, they have internal consistency. While Etherites will argue about whether empty space is Ether vs Dark Matter, all members of the union will agree that it is the Cosmological Constant which holds the fabric of space together, and when the time is right, they will be able to utilise this fact to produce new experimental procedures, slowly introduce the ideas to the masses, and then, slowly or suddenly, incorporate them into the zeitgeist where they become mundane.<br /> <br /> When a NSC talks about Post Life Entities, they are doing so not because they &quot;Don't believe in ghosts&quot;, but because the term &quot;ghost&quot; is muddied with so many contradictory definitions based on culture, superstition, and heresay. The Akashics may speak of ghosts like a fox who can turn into a lady and eats the hearts of humans in order to steal their skin, of they may speak of women jilted in life becoming horrible spectres of hatred, with long black hair which obscures their face. The Euthanatos would speak of ghosts as beings who are simply waiting to reincarnate, and are only temporarily trapped until they can pass on. The Celestial Chorus would speak of ghosts as unfortunate souls forever trapped in limbo, or even purgatory depending on what they are taught, awaiting judgement until the end of time. While Etherites have countless theories on ghosts and what they are, some consider them to be simple emotion patterns left as a footprint on the mundane world, others would consider them to be the very soul of a human stripped of a body, other's still will state that ghosts are just memories, kept alive by the combined cognotive resonance energies of the human's who knew the deceased.<br /> <br /> With all these convoluted ideas attached to the word &quot;ghost&quot;. The Union does away with this nonsense by rebranding them in purely analytical terms. When one NSC talks about Post Life Entities, they can be assured that everyone in the room knows exactly what they are talking about without any preconceived notions muddying up the picture. They are talking about an Extra-Dimensional Entitie which is native to the Shadow dimension, more formally known as Entropic Space. That's it. No talk of sentiments or purpose, simple clear cut analytics. That's how the Union get things done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:45:03-07:00","id":966961,"title":"","content":"I tend to reject the purple paradigm myself. The Traditions are allied by what they are against, modernity, rather than by having a common magical vision. The Conventions are also allied by what they are against, anachronisms, rather than by having a common magical vision. Every Mage filters their perceptions of reality and magic through their Avatars, which means that they are all insane, and should be given a Quiet of 0, which should grow as they become more and more divorced from reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:48:55-07:00","id":966962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966910#post966910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A device that works by pressing a button is some form of wonder. The problem is really how people portray technomantic stuff. A technomantic sensory effect should be a complicated screen of numbers and gages the sleeper looks at and is all &amp;quot;I have no idea what this mean&amp;quot; the technomancer who lacks that sphere looks at it and is &amp;quot;I have no idea what this means&amp;quot;. The lightning gun is a bad example.<br /> <br /> Lets us real guns as an example. The &amp;quot;magic&amp;quot; of making a bullet isn't when you pull the trigger, its way back when the the powder was mixed and the bullet was machine tooled. We could also include the gun itself as part of the extended technomantic &amp;quot;ritual&amp;quot;. The Technomancer performs the extended gun ritual in his sacred space(workshop) and that ritual will have a number of successes to determine how many times the effect can be used before it stops working and how long it lasts. So the Technomancer has cast a ritual for 6 shots that last for a month, shots go off when trigger is pulled.<br /> <br /> If they don't have the spheres to do this they shouldn't be making &amp;quot;guns&amp;quot; any more than a sleeper who lacks gunsmithing skills should be making guns. Spheres and Arete matter just as much in the &amp;quot;Purple Paradigm&amp;quot; as anything else people seem to keep missing that for the &amp;quot;BELIEVE BELIEVE&amp;quot; your character still needs the spheres to do make shit not just their raw belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does your gun example stack to say a ray gun? Especially if that builder doesn't have time or prime 4. Let's say a technocrat or etherite builds a ray gun that only requires point and shoot in order to work but ONLY needs to be plugged into a wall socket to charge. Are you saying that the real magic happened when when the gun was being built and they enchanted it for every single shot that will ever be fired from it? That's unreasonable to expect that. So what happens when a sleeper grabs hold of that ray gun and pulls the trigger and nothing happens despite the ray gun being recently charged. Ultimately holes can endlessly be poked into any argument on your side of the fence that says that sleepers shouldn't be able to use enlightened technology no matter how simple the interface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:53:04-07:00","id":966965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966961#post966961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to reject the purple paradigm myself. The Traditions are allied by what they are against, modernity, rather than by having a common magical vision. The Conventions are also allied by what they are against, anachronisms, rather than by having a common magical vision. Every Mage filters their perceptions of reality and magic through their Avatars, which means that they are all insane, and should be given a Quiet of 0, which should grow as they become more and more divorced from reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Didn't take you for a fan of Genius: The Transgression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966962#post966962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does your gun example stack to say a ray gun? Especially if that builder doesn't have time or prime 4. Let's say a technocrat or etherite builds a ray gun that only requires point and shoot in order to work but ONLY needs to be plugged into a wall socket to charge. Are you saying that the real magic happened when when the gun was being built and they enchanted it for every single shot that will ever be fired from it? That's unreasonable to expect that. So what happens when a sleeper grabs hold of that ray gun and pulls the trigger and nothing happens despite the ray gun being recently charged. Ultimately holes can endlessly be poked into any argument on your side of the fence that says that sleepers shouldn't be able to use enlightened technology no matter how simple the interface.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple. If they don't have Time or Prime 4, they can't build something that simple. Making a simple user interface isn't EASY Y'know. Especially for something like a laser. You have to automate every step that you are keeping from the user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:02:30-07:00","id":966970,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that the majority of defenses I've seen in support of sleepers not being allowed to use any enlightened science even if it is something as easy as pushing a button seem to be dependent on the purple paradigm. I've said it before that I think the purple paradigm should be forgotten because it (like the sphere system) is biased towards a small group such as OoH where Will is what shapes reality. But that isn't what mage is about. It's about how Belief is what shapes reality and what a mage believes they are doing IS what they are doing. So when a technocrat is using an antigravity propulsion drive to fly then that is what is happening versus say a dreamspeaker who believes they are being carried by air spirits to fly then that too is happening. To just say that they are both deluding themselves and what they are really doing is just using their Will to fly goes against the very core concept of mage of how beliefs change and shape how reality works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:09:18-07:00","id":966973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966965#post966965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm. Didn't take you for a fan of Genius: The Transgression.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Simple. If they don't have Time or Prime 4, they can't build something that simple. Making a simple user interface isn't EASY Y'know. Especially for something like a laser. You have to automate every step that you are keeping from the user.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't they? Just saying they can't and that it isn't easy without giving reason does not make for a defense. Are you really saying that a technomancer in the field who has prime 2 and forces 3 but not prime 4 who has built a ray gun would build one in a way that would require more complexity than pulled a trigger to fire despite the risks that having to fumble with a bunch settings in order for it to fit into your explanations would have for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:19:11-07:00","id":966977,"title":"","content":"I want you to design for me in the next ten minutes a gun that will fire bullets forever. Requiring only a simple push of a button. Even MODERN FIREARMS are more complex than that. And we're talking about hypothetical weaponry that we can't even get to work practically without requiring an entire roomful of apparatus's and a team of trained scientists and engineers in real life.<br /> <br /> Yes. It really has to be that complicated. You're energizing gasses until they plasmate then using a controlled magnetic field to hurl the resulting ball of blindingly hot plasma across a room to vaporize some poor unfortunate schlub. Do you realize the level of work it would take to AUTOMATE that so that it comes down to just 'pull the trigger'?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:00:49-07:00","id":966995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966977#post966977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want you to design for me in the next ten minutes a gun that will fire bullets forever. Requiring only a simple push of a button. Even MODERN FIREARMS are more complex than that. And we're talking about hypothetical weaponry that we can't even get to work practically without requiring an entire roomful of apparatus's and a team of trained scientists and engineers in real life.<br /> <br /> Yes. It really has to be that complicated. You're energizing gasses until they plasmate then using a controlled magnetic field to hurl the resulting ball of blindingly hot plasma across a room to vaporize some poor unfortunate schlub. Do you realize the level of work it would take to AUTOMATE that so that it comes down to just 'pull the trigger'?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it had to be easy but literally the FIRST thing that someone in the field would do after inventing something for the field would be to work out how to make it as easy to use as possible. Otherwise it will be more a detriment than an aid. And as people with any sphere at 4 dots are supposed to be rare then you reply that anyone without that isn't working to improve their technology to be easier to use. And what about if the technocrat leaves behind very detailed step by step instructions on how to operate the technology. How do you explain when absolutely no sleepers whatsoever can operate it even with the instructions? Sure some technocrats might justify it as they are just too stupid to use it but there would be plenty of others who would ask the obvious question of why. Following instructions is far easier than inventing something to the point where you don't need to know HOW it works, only that if you do these specific things then it should work. Take a phone for example, the vast majority of people don't know how it works, only that if you press these buttons then it will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:17:57-07:00","id":967004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966995#post966995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said it had to be easy but literally the FIRST thing that someone in the field would do after inventing something for the field would be to work out how to make it as easy to use as possible. Otherwise it will be more a detriment than an aid. And as people with any sphere at 4 dots are supposed to be rare then you reply that anyone without that isn't working to improve their technology to be easier to use. And what about if the technocrat leaves behind very detailed step by step instructions on how to operate the technology. How do you explain when absolutely no sleepers whatsoever can operate it even with the instructions? Sure some technocrats might justify it as they are just too stupid to use it but there would be plenty of others who would ask the obvious question of why. Following instructions is far easier than inventing something to the point where you don't need to know HOW it works, only that if you do these specific things then it should work. Take a phone for example, the vast majority of people don't know how it works, only that if you press these buttons then it will.</div> </div> </div> </div>As easy to use as possible <i>for them</i>. Like... I'm not sure why you think this is such an incomprehensible thing, but some people just don't know things or have certain mindsets, even if they are otherwise smart. Some people just don't know how to automate things. Some people get to the point of it having a big complicated interface scheme and just stop there and continue using it, because simplifying it further would actually <i>lessen</i> their ability to do things (see: the difference between power users and your average user). And <i>they</i> know how it works, what does it matter if some random guy off the street can't use it?<br /> <br /> Like, you and yours are fond of using these blithe whitewashed examples, but seriously? Lots of the shit that technomancers should be using for Enlightened Science likely involve shit like quickly solving physics problems or heavy-duty guesswork. It's called <i>Genius</i> for a reason. If the Enlightened Scientist can boil it down to a simple, straightforward, Sleeper-usable algorithm, either they know enough to automate it (meaning that, <i>in game mechanics, which are a representation of the state of things within the game which we are hypothetically playing</i>, they have the Traits which represent &quot;can make fully automated bits of superscience&quot;), or it is straight-up not deserving of being considered Enlightened Science, because you have <i>definitionally</i> said that it does not require Enlightenment to work.<br /> <br /> Your point-and-shoot thing made with pure Matter/Forces is a Sleepertech laser. There. Done. Easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:24:08-07:00","id":967007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966962#post966962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does your gun example stack to say a ray gun? Especially if that builder doesn't have time or prime 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they don't build a raygun.<br /> <br /> This isn't complicated. There'\\s a reason Technomancers have access to &quot;WOnder spheres&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's say a technocrat or etherite builds a ray gun that only requires point and shoot in order to work but ONLY needs to be plugged into a wall socket to charge. Are you saying that the real magic happened when when the gun was being built and they enchanted it for every single shot that will ever be fired from it? That's unreasonable to expect that. </div> </div> </div>No, its unreasonable you are allowing the device to be built to those standards. Not every Technomancer can make everything that's part of their paradigm. Its really simple. Either the Technomancer can make a raygun and it works for everyone. Or they just can't make a raygun!<br /> <br /> But assuming Forces 2 prime 4(Prime utility 3 if your syndicate.)<br /> <br /> Said gun exists. It converts prime into lightning bolts. And electriity into quint to charge it. The Sleeper goes off and shoots people with a lightning gun. IT eventually breaks(From Paradox) because its a high tech prototype.<br /> <br /> Now if we are assuming a base &quot;Technomancer only has forces&quot; well I don't let them make a simple ray gun. A hermetic, an Akashic and an Etherite each want to throw lightning across the room. They are all the same level of enlightenment. No one has a surpassed Focus. The Hermetic spends a round invoking the angel of Lightning, the Akashic slips into a minor meditation.. YOu think the Etherite jsut spends that time pressing a button? He's calebrating his equipment.<br /> <br /> Since technomancers are even less likely to have surpassed a focus/instrament they are more likely to have to spend time &quot;doing something&quot; to set up their effects. So anyone who just wants &quot;press a button&quot; for their character is missing the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:26:23-07:00","id":967009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966973#post966973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why can't they? Just saying they can't and that it isn't easy without giving reason does not make for a defense. Are you really saying that a technomancer in the field who has prime 2 and forces 3 but not prime 4 who has built a ray gun would build one in a way that would require more complexity than pulled a trigger to fire despite the risks that having to fumble with a bunch settings in order for it to fit into your explanations would have for them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why can't I make a SPirit with Matter? Why can't I make Bacteria with Forces? Why can't i use Entropy 1 to travel into the Deep umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:28:11-07:00","id":967010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967004#post967004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As easy to use as possible <i>for them</i>. Like... I'm not sure why you think this is such an incomprehensible thing, but some people just don't know things or have certain mindsets, even if they are otherwise smart. Some people just don't know how to automate things. Some people get to the point of it having a big complicated interface scheme and just stop there and continue using it, because simplifying it further would actually <i>lessen</i> their ability to do things (see: the difference between power users and your average user). And <i>they</i> know how it works, what does it matter if some random guy off the street can't use it?<br /> <br /> Like, you and yours are fond of using these blithe whitewashed examples, but seriously? Lots of the shit that technomancers should be using for Enlightened Science likely involve shit like quickly solving physics problems or heavy-duty guesswork. It's called <i>Genius</i> for a reason. If the Enlightened Scientist can boil it down to a simple, straightforward, Sleeper-usable algorithm, either they know enough to automate it (meaning that, <i>in game mechanics, which are a representation of the state of things within the game which we are hypothetically playing</i>, they have the Traits which represent &amp;quot;can make fully automated bits of superscience&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, or it is straight-up not deserving of being considered Enlightened Science, because you have <i>definitionally</i> said that it does not require Enlightenment to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that I am simply using whitewashed examples but I was just using those examples for simplicity's sake. Plus take the average thing that a player would use, it's not going to be the most complicated thing even if the internal logic is complicated. Also I noticed you never answered my question about if a sleeper got instructions. While yours was a better justification than most, it still has the same flaws I've pointed out before. Canon outright says that the majority of the technocracy's workforce are not awakened so it only makes sense that non awakened should be able to use their enlightened science at least to a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:31:47-07:00","id":967011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967009#post967009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Why can't I make a SPirit with Matter? Why can't I make Bacteria with Forces? Why can't i use Entropy 1 to travel into the Deep umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you are saying makes absolutely no sense. I'm pointing out the flaw in using a system that is designed with classical magics in mind and favors that for something like enlightened science. You are just babbling off things presumably because you think I don't understand the rules. I'm saying the rules are flawed and that people have to twist the narrative to fit the rules, not that they should be ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:14:04-07:00","id":967036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967010#post967010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that I am simply using whitewashed examples but I was just using those examples for simplicity's sake. Plus take the average thing that a player would use, it's not going to be the most complicated thing even if the internal logic is complicated. Also I noticed you never answered my question about if a sleeper got instructions. While yours was a better justification than most, it still has the same flaws I've pointed out before. Canon outright says that the majority of the technocracy's workforce are not awakened so it only makes sense that non awakened should be able to use their enlightened science at least to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocratic Conditioning makes you 'not a sleeper' once it hit's 8. You might not be enlightened, but you hang around them enough to fake it. How that works? Dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:27:03-07:00","id":967039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967010#post967010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that I am simply using whitewashed examples but I was just using those examples for simplicity's sake. Plus take the average thing that a player would use, it's not going to be the most complicated thing even if the internal logic is complicated. Also I noticed you never answered my question about if a sleeper got instructions. While yours was a better justification than most, it still has the same flaws I've pointed out before. Canon outright says that the majority of the technocracy's workforce are not awakened so it only makes sense that non awakened should be able to use their enlightened science at least to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the instructions are simple enough to put into an algorithm a Sleeper can reliably and repeatably perform to full effectiveness, it shouldn't qualify as Enlightened Science in the first place. It's just something Sleepers can do. I thought I already answered that, but apparently it fell out in the revisions. Actual Enlightened Science should entail some form of deep understanding or intuition.<br /> <br /> Maybe player instruments aren't normally going to be very complicated. Unless it works on its own with absolutely no adjustment and the character is just using it well, though, <i>that</i> is a flaw as well. Because <i>that's how you make technological paradigms self-consistent within the setting and with available observation</i>.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if you teach a Sleeper how to use your device with enough fidelity that they can operate it themselves... congratulations, you've just taught them a Path of Technosorcery. Maybe you showed them how to operate your array of high-energy weapons, and they learned the Path of Hellfire Missiles. Maybe you taught them how to use your manufactory, and now they have the Path of Nanofabrication (Enchantment) and can make a few low-end Devices of their own.<br /> <br /> Extraordinary Devices are also things. See Demon Hunter X for... basically everything in Strike Force Zero's arsenal; <i>all of that shit</i> is Extraordinary Devices, which any Sleeper who knows what they're doing can use. Same with the things listed as such in Iteration X Revised, and a bunch of equipment in Guide to the Technocracy. You want to make a 'ray gun' which requires no understanding of its inner workings to use, and doesn't cost the extensive time, effort, expertise, and cost as a proper Device? Make an Extraordinary Device. It won't be as good as Enlightened tech, but it'll work, and maybe your Scientist can make it work better on-the-fly (read: use it as an instrument for a Forces attack).<br /> <br /> Charms also exist, and are producible with Tass at Prime 2 (game term). If you can get by via giving your invention a limited number of charges, that's not a harsh requirement at all.<br /> <br /> That's an entire spectrum of things that can be retrofitted to make a coherent technological paradigm, if you're not actively opposed to <i>fixing</i> the seeming paradox after pointing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-10-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:55:29-07:00","id":967049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967039#post967039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the instructions are simple enough to put into an algorithm a Sleeper can reliably and repeatably perform to full effectiveness, it shouldn't qualify as Enlightened Science in the first place. It's just something Sleepers can do. I thought I already answered that, but apparently it fell out in the revisions. Actual Enlightened Science should entail some form of deep understanding or intuition.<br /> <br /> Maybe player instruments aren't normally going to be very complicated. Unless it works on its own with absolutely no adjustment and the character is just using it well, though, <i>that</i> is a flaw as well. Because <i>that's how you make technological paradigms self-consistent within the setting and with available observation</i>.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if you teach a Sleeper how to use your device with enough fidelity that they can operate it themselves... congratulations, you've just taught them a Path of Technosorcery. Maybe you showed them how to operate your array of high-energy weapons, and they learned the Path of Hellfire Missiles. Maybe you taught them how to use your manufactory, and now they have the Path of Nanofabrication (Enchantment) and can make a few low-end Devices of their own.<br /> <br /> Extraordinary Devices are also things. See Demon Hunter X for... basically everything in Strike Force Zero's arsenal; <i>all of that shit</i> is Extraordinary Devices, which any Sleeper who knows what they're doing can use. Same with the things listed as such in Iteration X Revised, and a bunch of equipment in Guide to the Technocracy. You want to make a 'ray gun' which requires no understanding of its inner workings to use, and doesn't cost the extensive time, effort, expertise, and cost as a proper Device? Make an Extraordinary Device. It won't be as good as Enlightened tech, but it'll work, and maybe your Scientist can make it work better on-the-fly (read: use it as an instrument for a Forces attack).<br /> <br /> Charms also exist, and are producible with Tass at Prime 2 (game term). If you can get by via giving your invention a limited number of charges, that's not a harsh requirement at all.<br /> <br /> That's an entire spectrum of things that can be retrofitted to make a coherent technological paradigm, if you're not actively opposed to <i>fixing</i> the seeming paradox after pointing it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually something I was intending on doing in a game once. Make Charms/Gadgets in the form of Ammo Packs or Energy Cells for energy weapons. Then distributing them to a characters unenlightened backup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:57:53-07:00","id":967050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967049#post967049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually something I was intending on doing in a game once. Make Charms/Gadgets in the form of Ammo Packs or Energy Cells for energy weapons. Then distributing them to a characters unenlightened backup.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this because it actually does something to bridge the gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:05:01-07:00","id":967055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967011#post967011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you are saying makes absolutely no sense. I'm pointing out the flaw in using a system that is designed with classical magics in mind and favors that for something like enlightened science. You are just babbling off things presumably because you think I don't understand the rules. I'm saying the rules are flawed and that people have to twist the narrative to fit the rules, not that they should be ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Flaw in the system is you are allowing people to do things without the skill to do so. For some reason you think technomancers should be able to spend ten minutes and make a raygun that anyone can use. This both isn't in their paradigm. Nor in the game rules. That's the Flaw. You seem to think that the &quot;Magic&quot; of a technomancer is pressing the button. Its building the machine, or maybe pulling a star trek and realigning something something technobable on something in the field.<br /> <br /> A simple easy to use Technological device with just current technology takes time to make. There is no reason that Technomancers who austensibly are just &quot;More advanced&quot; should violate those principles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:31:13-07:00","id":967076,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6072_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6072\" data-vbnamecard=\"6072\">Quantumboost</a> Are you telling me that when a technomancer teaches &quot;simple&quot; instructions like, &quot;pull this trigger&quot;, &quot;turn this key counter clockwise&quot; is in reality teaching a Path?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4178\" data-vbnamecard=\"4178\">stanlemon</a> I disagree that there shouldn't exist the purple paradigm. Remember that it is true, but lots of Mages don't know it, so their belief is actually creating the effect. The problem isn't the purple paradigm, but Technocrats and technomancers not believing that magick exist. The other Traditions have no problem with that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:38:12-07:00","id":967085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967055#post967055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Flaw in the system is you are allowing people to do things without the skill to do so. For some reason you think technomancers should be able to spend ten minutes and make a raygun that anyone can use. This both isn't in their paradigm. Nor in the game rules. That's the Flaw. You seem to think that the &quot;Magic&quot; of a technomancer is pressing the button. Its building the machine, or maybe pulling a star trek and realigning something something technobable on something in the field.<br /> <br /> A simple easy to use Technological device with just current technology takes time to make. There is no reason that Technomancers who austensibly are just &quot;More advanced&quot; should violate those principles.</div> </div> </div> </div>This proves you don't understand what I'm saying. For starters, at no point did I ever say anything like it should be simple or quick to do it, but I am saying that it would be in its initial construction to make it as simple as possible. It's a matter of efficiency. Nor am I saying that it needs to be easy to use but the Technomancer would likely want to make it as easy to use not just for their own use but for showing it off to their other Technomancer. Why shouldn't it be in their paradigm for making technology more efficient or making it as efficient in the initial design? That's what I mean by twisting the narrative to fit into the rules. Sure there is any number of reasons to explain it away but tell me then, if you are 50s style scifi Etherite and has a 50s style raygun that ONLY has a trigger and it was built by a mage that has forces 3 prime 2, then why wouldn't a sleeper be able to use it, especially a sleeper who is willing to accept 50s style scifi technology? A machine is a machine and with the right instructions and education then anyone should be able to do it. That's the BASES of the Technocracy's paradigm. You are all over thinking this and trying to make justifications to explain why it should fit into rules that weren't designed for a technomancer's paradigm just as you think I'm making justifications of my own. One reason I prefer dark ages is because the magic rules are built to support the narrative and paradigm rather than having the narrative twisted to fit with the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:57:38-07:00","id":967101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967076#post967076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4178\" data-vbnamecard=\"4178\">stanlemon</a> I disagree that there shouldn't exist the purple paradigm. Remember that it is true, but lots of Mages don't know it, so their belief is actually creating the effect. The problem isn't the purple paradigm, but Technocrats and technomancers not believing that magick exist. The other Traditions have no problem with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Sphere system is based upon the Technocracies 'Spheres of Influence.' You're thinking &quot;Why do the technologists use the same system as the magicians?&quot; When it's the other way around. The Sphere system was built on Technocratic ideas. And then the Traditions took it and added superstitious sentiments to it and we get the spheres we know today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:01:14-07:00","id":967104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967101#post967101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the Sphere system is based upon the Technocracies 'Spheres of Influence.' You're thinking &quot;Why do the technologists use the same system as the magicians?&quot; When it's the other way around. The Sphere system was built on Technocratic ideas. And then the Traditions took it and added superstitious sentiments to it and we get the spheres we know today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought the Spheres were classified by the hermetics. Nonetheless, the sphere system isn't the issue, but the belief that magick isn't real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:10:04-07:00","id":967113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967104#post967104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought the Spheres were classified by the hermetics. Nonetheless, the sphere system isn't the issue, but the belief that magick isn't real.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, it's stated directly in the Order of Hermes book that they created the idea of spheres which is a nice in universe justification for why they are more biased towards them than to anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:32:29-07:00","id":967118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967085#post967085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This proves you don't understand what I'm saying. For starters, at no point did I ever say anything like it should be simple or quick to do it, but I am saying that it would be in its initial construction to make it as simple as possible. It's a matter of efficiency. Nor am I saying that it needs to be easy to use but the Technomancer would likely want to make it as easy to use not just for their own use but for showing it off to their other Technomancer. Why shouldn't it be in their paradigm for making technology more efficient or making it as efficient in the initial design? That's what I mean by twisting the narrative to fit into the rules. Sure there is any number of reasons to explain it away but tell me then, if you are 50s style scifi Etherite and has a 50s style raygun that ONLY has a trigger and it was built by a mage that has forces 3 prime 2, then why wouldn't a sleeper be able to use it, especially a sleeper who is willing to accept 50s style scifi technology? A machine is a machine and with the right instructions and education then anyone should be able to do it. That's the BASES of the Technocracy's paradigm. You are all over thinking this and trying to make justifications to explain why it should fit into rules that weren't designed for a technomancer's paradigm just as you think I'm making justifications of my own. One reason I prefer dark ages is because the magic rules are built to support the narrative and paradigm rather than having the narrative twisted to fit with the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Let me use a mystic example of your argument. My hermetic believes if he says one word. It will blow up the Sun. Why shouldn't they be able to? For some reason you seem to think this is a unique problem for Technomancers. Rather than you completely being unwilling to engage in the conceits of the system. Either they do everything in the lab.. and the gun works for the Sleeper just as readily.. or they have to do something special on the fly to make their gun work because its a very complicated tool that no one without their level of understanding really can make work. Forces 3, prime 2 is not enough to make a simple easy to use raygun, period. Its no different than Verbena asking why they can't shapeshift or turn wiccans into Cats with Life 2.<br /> <br /> Have you never heard of a car that only &quot;I can keep running&quot;(A key plot point from Sin City) or dealt with a piece of tech that was 'finicky&quot; I have a lawnmower that practically requires the proper ritual invocation to Hephaestus to run(and blood). MY dad litterally can't turn it on. And this was a fully manufactured device built in a factory. Not some thing I cobbled together in my basement as an experiment. That's what etherite tech is. Stuff they cobble together to go out and experiment with, of course its going to be crazy complicated.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:41:57-07:00","id":967127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967118#post967118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Let me use a mystic example of your argument. My hermetic believes if he says one word. It will blow up the Sun. Why shouldn't they be able to? For some reason you seem to think this is a unique problem for Technomancers. Rather than you completely being unwilling to engage in the conceits of the system. Either they do everything in the lab.. and the gun works for the Sleeper just as readily.. or they have to do something special on the fly to make their gun work because its a very complicated tool that no one without their level of understanding really can make work. Forces 3, prime 2 is not enough to make a simple easy to use raygun, period. Its no different than Verbena asking why they can't shapeshift or turn wiccans into Cats with Life 2.<br /> <br /> Have you never heard of a car that only &amp;quot;I can keep running&amp;quot;(A key plot point from Sin City) or dealt with a piece of tech that was 'finicky&amp;quot; I have a lawnmower that practically requires the proper ritual invocation to Hephaestus to run(and blood). MY dad litterally can't turn it on. And this was a fully manufactured device built in a factory. Not some thing I cobbled together in my basement as an experiment. That's what etherite tech is. Stuff they cobble together to go out and experiment with, of course its going to be crazy complicated.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you keep using bloated exaggerated examples shows that you don't understand anything. Yes skill is a thing, but the technomancer's paradigm is built on science and being repeatable, that's what science IS. If they can't instruct others in the steps they used to get something to happen then they need to start figuring out WHY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:30:21-07:00","id":967150,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> , the problem is that you're using examples where the Mage doesn't have enough Spheres to do the effect. This is not true in the technomancer case. There's no where stating that to make a device that is easily activated it is needed Prime. The example is the same of the OoH Tradition book stating about &quot;preparing&quot; spells where their craft a talisman for hours and then in the battlefield just say a word and it cast the spell. Bring this to a etherite and he builds a complex device and in the battlefield he just pushes a button and it works.<br /> <br /> The problem is when they try to explain why their devices won't work for sleepers. The hermetic will say that the sleeper doesn't have the necessary Will to command his amulet. The etherite won't have any explanation, due to his instrument being completely external to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:40:19-07:00","id":967155,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could imbue a tool with Spheres? Could a Technocrat imbue a raygun with Forces and Prime, giving the raygun their Spheres at the cost of not being able to use their Spheres without their raygun? Perhaps it would work like this.<br /> <br /> The tool would be a standard foci and, if destroyed, the Technocrat would regain access to their Spheres within one day. If given to a Sleeper, the Sleeper would be able to use the raygun, though the Technocrat would lose access to the imbued Spheres, and any Paradox gained by the Sleeper would instead be gained by the tool. When the tool reaches 10 points of Paradox, the tool breaks, and the Technocrat receives the accumulated Paradox in one burst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:44:25-07:00","id":967158,"title":"","content":"This goes into the core issue of the debate, on those that are on the explain away the contradiction side, they are using the sphere rules as the end all be all to how magic works in mage. I and the others are using paradigm however as the end all be all to explaining how magic works and from the narrative that's exactly how magic is supposed to work. The spheres from an in-universe standpoint are merely an artificial construct to form a framework for how to learn and do magic but it isn't an actual law of magic in the system. The arguments against technomancers lacking the skill also falls flat when you look at Dark Age Mage and how magic works in that where the rules are built in to work with the narrative. For example a member of the Old Faith needs to be pretty darn skilled in 3 Pillars in order to teleport somewhere while on the other hand an Ahl-I-Batin can do it with far more ease in that setting and it is because of things like that where paradigm is having an actual effect on their magic is why we (or at least I) am arguing that the rules are flawed and that you need to twist the paradigm to fit into the rules for arguments about over complexity and lack of skill to start making sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:16:45-07:00","id":967196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967127#post967127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that you keep using bloated exaggerated examples shows that you don't understand anything. Yes skill is a thing, but the technomancer's paradigm is built on science and being repeatable, that's what science IS. If they can't instruct others in the steps they used to get something to happen then they need to start figuring out WHY.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can instruct others in the steps they used to get something to happen. That's called &quot;Teaching a Rote&quot; or &quot;Teaching a sphere&quot;<br /> <br /> I can instruct my dad all day on how to program. He will never learn. I'm not going to become a brain surgeon without years of study and teaching. And Even if I DO Study I might not learn how to be a brain surgeon. Actually there's a very good chance I won't be able to become a brain surgeon or follow their 'simple surgical steps&quot; only someone who has an equal amount of training could possibly follow said steps.<br /> <br /> Technomancers aren't just doing 'science&quot; they are doing super cutting edge science. Of course only their peers can understand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967150#post967150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> , the problem is that you're using examples where the Mage doesn't have enough Spheres to do the effect. This is not true in the technomancer case. There's no where stating that to make a device that is easily activated it is needed Prime. The example is the same of the OoH Tradition book stating about &quot;preparing&quot; spells where their craft a talisman for hours and then in the battlefield just say a word and it cast the spell. Bring this to a etherite and he builds a complex device and in the battlefield he just pushes a button and it works.<br /> <br /> The problem is when they try to explain why their devices won't work for sleepers. The hermetic will say that the sleeper doesn't have the necessary Will to command his amulet. The etherite won't have any explanation, due to his instrument being completely external to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>OH that one's easy.<br /> <br /> He spends an extra success on building it so the &quot;target&quot; is someone else or he doesn't and its not a push button make things happen.<br /> <br /> This isn't complicated. An St who allows the contradiction is missing the point of how these things work. SInce the Technomancer cannot concieve of building a device taht only works when he presses the button and not when a sleeper does.. he can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:58:29-07:00","id":967207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967158#post967158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This goes into the core issue of the debate, on those that are on the explain away the contradiction side, they are using the sphere rules as the end all be all to how magic works in mage. I and the others are using paradigm however as the end all be all to explaining how magic works and from the narrative that's exactly how magic is supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>No you aren't you're ignoring both. You're asking &quot;why can someone do something that both their paradigm and game mechanics don't support&quot; when we keep saying that's not how this works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The spheres from an in-universe standpoint are merely an artificial construct to form a framework for how to learn and do magic but it isn't an actual law of magic in the system. </div> </div> </div>No. I treat SPhere as &quot;This is what the character can do in the system&quot; they are no more metaphysically true to the setting than &quot;Stealth&quot; or &quot;Dexterity&quot;. Your argument reads &quot;Why can't a Technomancer punch something with Intelligence and Subterfuge because they believe they can!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The arguments against technomancers lacking the skill also falls flat when you look at Dark Age Mage and how magic works in that where the rules are built in to work with the narrative. For example a member of the Old Faith needs to be pretty darn skilled in 3 Pillars in order to teleport somewhere while on the other hand an Ahl-I-Batin can do it with far more ease in that setting and it is because of things like that where paradigm is having an actual effect on their magic is why we (or at least I) am arguing that the rules are flawed and that you need to twist the paradigm to fit into the rules for arguments about over complexity and lack of skill to start making sense. </div> </div> </div>The spheres are arbitrary. Lets make a set of pillars for the Etherites for example. UFOS, Rayguns, Beams, Abominations, and Hypnosis. My etherite has alot of dots in UFOs. But no dots in Rayguns. so.. he can't make a raygun. That's how your argument has looked to us so far. The 9 spheres while a setting conceit are also an Game mechanical conceit for a game covering 10+ different magical practices(and that's being conservative, more generous reads might hit over 50) and making it fundimentally runable by a GM. But since the 9 spheres are a one size fits all thing they won't fit perfectly like a custom tailored suit so you have to make adjustments, but here's the thing. That's a problem for each and every magical practice, the 9 spheres no more perfectly fit the Hermetics(Who supposedly invented them as a compromise concept) than it does the Technocracy, or the Verbena, etc. Its a compromise for playability.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:11:14-07:00","id":967211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967207#post967207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No you aren't you're ignoring both. You're asking &quot;why can someone do something that both their paradigm and game mechanics don't support&quot; when we keep saying that's not how this works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No. I treat SPhere as &quot;This is what the character can do in the system&quot; they are no more metaphysically true to the setting than &quot;Stealth&quot; or &quot;Dexterity&quot;. Your argument reads &quot;Why can't a Technomancer punch something with Intelligence and Subterfuge because they believe they can!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The spheres are arbitrary. Lets make a set of pillars for the Etherites for example. UFOS, Rayguns, Beams, Abominations, and Hypnosis. My etherite has alot of dots in UFOs. But no dots in Rayguns. so.. he can't make a raygun. That's how your argument has looked to us so far. The 9 spheres while a setting conceit are also an Game mechanical conceit for a game covering 10+ different magical practices(and that's being conservative, more generous reads might hit over 50) and making it fundimentally runable by a GM. But since the 9 spheres are a one size fits all thing they won't fit perfectly like a custom tailored suit so you have to make adjustments, but here's the thing. That's a problem for each and every magical practice, the 9 spheres no more perfectly fit the Hermetics(Who supposedly invented them as a compromise concept) than it does the Technocracy, or the Verbena, etc. Its a compromise for playability.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Really just how dense are you? The argument you are making has NOTHING to do with what I am saying. You are saying that I am making claims that I should be able to set things on fire by using life or some nonsense like that and at no point I have made a claim like that which just proves you are completely oblivious to what this debate is about. What I'm saying are logical inconsistencies where between how technology should work within their paradigm and that you have to twist their paradigms to make justifications for why they fit into the rules as set when science and technology don't work like that. Spheres and their limits are exactly that, arbitrary if you paid attention to my actual account on Pillars you would understand that it was about logically being able to do something within their paradigm but as you have done with every single one of your posts is a bunch of false comparisons. Either you are a troll or you just don't understand anything. You are the one making a bunch of absurd claims about what I am talking about that are outright untrue.<br /> <br /> Your Pillar argument is particularly annoying and a great example of your false comparisons and lack of understanding to the topic of this debate. My arguments have been all about how inventing and building things is at the very core of what a technomancer does and believes. It's the machine that has the power and does the work and at most he operates it. Arguments where there is a claim that operating it are at least valid arguments where I've countered that the technomancer would make it as simple as possible because that's what inventors do, but that isn't what you've degraded this into. You just keep making a lot of claims about things that have nothing to do with what I'm saying. Your UFO and raygun example for example. Where I'm talking about the foundation where making things is the core of of what they do regardless of the pillars they focus on you are making claims that I am saying that someone who focuses on making UFOs should be able to make rayguns which is nothing like what I'm saying. The closest is that regardless of what they are making they are still making something and their paradigm posits that it is the device and not them who does whatever the magic they are trying to accomplish so it should still work even with the not around. If you can't understand that then you have failed utterly at understanding anything.<br /> <br /> I would love to know where you are getting things like I'm arguing for punching with intelligence or using spheres that are unrelated to the effect I'm trying to do. Those are things you made up in order to try to discredit what I've been saying without actually debating what I've been saying. The closest I've come was asking why should a technocrat need prime 4 to make a device that sleepers can use when the technocrat paradigm has it that any machine should work as long as the proper sequences are used. So it would be nice if you stopped making up things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 09-11-2016, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T03:20:16-07:00","id":967249,"title":"","content":"Well, I think a more important concern is not the Sphere level, but the one level of permanent Willpower sacrificed per Device. Even if a quarter of Technomancers had sufficient skill, they would not produce more than a handful of Devices per generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T03:20:52-07:00","id":967250,"title":"","content":"This ongoing argument serves as a pretty good example of how technomancers function, in a way.<br /> <br /> One side argues that there are fundamental flaws in the game's system which undermine it to the point of meaninglessness. This is like the non-Etherite trying to use their machines and guns, finding that they don't work at all and explaining to said Etherite why their machine sucks.<br /> <br /> The other side is instead arguing that the system is fine, and that if they find fault with it, it's actually THEIR fault for misunderstanding it or applying nonsensical logic. So the Etherite response goes.<br /> <br /> The sleeper gets frustrated by the arrogance, the hand waveing, the dismissal of criticism. The Etherite gets frustrated with what they see as dismissal of reasoned responses, and that they direct their anger towards the creator for not being able to use their machines when it's actually the Sleeper who's at fault.<br /> <br /> Just like this thread, the discussion devolves into angry shouts of &quot;how can you be this stupid?&quot; Countered by &quot;are you just wilfully blind?&quot;<br /> <br /> And that is what happens when an Etherite sees a sleeper use their machines and find them not to work. No soul searching, trying to understand where their theories went wrong, just a condescending attitude followed by angry shouts of just not &quot;getting it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:46:07-07:00","id":967303,"title":"","content":"Or he is actually somewhat aware of how True Magick works, and understands that what works for him, doesn't work for the world at large. As far as I know, the Etherites are aware of the Consensus etc. and are warring with Technocracy extensively in regards to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:38:27-07:00","id":967336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967250#post967250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This ongoing argument serves as a pretty good example of how technomancers function, in a way.<br /> <br /> One side argues that there are fundamental flaws in the game's system which undermine it to the point of meaninglessness. This is like the non-Etherite trying to use their machines and guns, finding that they don't work at all and explaining to said Etherite why their machine sucks.<br /> <br /> The other side is instead arguing that the system is fine, and that if they find fault with it, it's actually THEIR fault for misunderstanding it or applying nonsensical logic. So the Etherite response goes.<br /> <br /> The sleeper gets frustrated by the arrogance, the hand waveing, the dismissal of criticism. The Etherite gets frustrated with what they see as dismissal of reasoned responses, and that they direct their anger towards the creator for not being able to use their machines when it's actually the Sleeper who's at fault.<br /> <br /> Just like this thread, the discussion devolves into angry shouts of &amp;quot;how can you be this stupid?&amp;quot; Countered by &amp;quot;are you just wilfully blind?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And that is what happens when an Etherite sees a sleeper use their machines and find them not to work. No soul searching, trying to understand where their theories went wrong, just a condescending attitude followed by angry shouts of just not &amp;quot;getting it&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is likely directed at me, but here is the thing that you are glossing over. I have specifically made my point clear multiple times while Lian has on many occasions twisted this conversation away from my point with fake comparisons of what I was talking about. I can appreciate your post of sleepers &quot;just not getting it&quot; especially in regards to an Etherite but my point still stands, especially with the technocracy who are trying to disseminate their technocracy to the masses at large. There comes a point where &quot;not getting it&quot; starts becoming willful ignorance and lies to support your side of the argument which is the territory that Lian has been entering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:49:17-07:00","id":967340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967336#post967336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is likely directed at me, but here is the thing that you are glossing over. I have specifically made my point clear multiple times while Lian has on many occasions twisted this conversation away from my point with fake comparisons of what I was talking about. I can appreciate your post of sleepers &quot;just not getting it&quot; especially in regards to an Etherite but my point still stands, especially with the technocracy who are trying to disseminate their technocracy to the masses at large. There comes a point where &quot;not getting it&quot; starts becoming willful ignorance and lies to support your side of the argument which is the territory that Lian has been entering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's why Etherites are Mages and not mundane Scientists.<br /> <br /> Regarding Technocracts. Their job is to dripfeed tech to the masses. Brand new Enlightened Science is too unstable, and far to User Unfriendly to be trusted in the hands of untrained personnel. Once the devices become simple enough to be used by the masses, and once the technology behind it is accepted as possible by the masses, then the procedures and devices cease to be Enlightened Science, and just become Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-11-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:13:28-07:00","id":967356,"title":"","content":"That is a fair point and a completely valid argument. Ultimately, minus the tangents, the two different sides of the argument seem to be on how paradigm should be handled in relation to the rules. And a debate on that can go on forever because on my side of things I like to have the rules integrated with paradigm like DA:M gives whereas you (making an assumption here so correct me if I'm wrong) like to have paradigm fit into the standard rule framework that modern day mage lays out. And as it can be explained away then you are fine with it like how technocrats explain away the magic their enemies use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:25:56-07:00","id":967361,"title":"","content":"I think the problem here is that both sides are using extremes in the arguing when the spectrums are far more broad. This is like all the misgivings in the Ascension War in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> Yes, the purple paradigm is present in all the Traditions paradigms in one way or another, but not all of them look at it like Hermetics do, each Tradition have their own way to look at it and introduce it into their own PoV of how the world works. Some Tradition books explain this better than others but this is what the whole Grand Convocation was about in the first place, all of them got a common point to revolve around even if they interpret it in their own way. Then of course each individual will understand it as they see fit or disregard it and they will evolve or devolve their own mindsets by interacting with other mages and the world as a whole, because that's what the path of a mage is about and characters change after all.<br /> <br /> Then with the Union I always prefer the approach that has the Union knowing what reality is really about and using it for their whole agenda, as I think painting the Technocracy ouright delusional as a whole it hurts the setting and there are many books in the line that prefers the former. Then if I have to defend it from a agent or a scientist standpoint who clashes with the supernatural and still doesn't accept it as what it is, we have to understand that not every single Technocrat (or Traditionalist, that's the same for both) know every single detail of how reality is supposed to work according to their organization, so if something like their own Enlightened Science has a place, it's not that much of a stretch that other strange things have it too, even if they aren't properly explained yet or their true workings it's secret for the upper echelons to know and deal with it in extreme secrecy to protect the masses. We like to equate the Technocratic Union to Science but they are also Control after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:30:07-07:00","id":967364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967196#post967196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH that one's easy.<br /> <br /> He spends an extra success on building it so the &quot;target&quot; is someone else or he doesn't and its not a push button make things happen.<br /> <br /> This isn't complicated. An St who allows the contradiction is missing the point of how these things work. SInce the Technomancer cannot concieve of building a device taht only works when he presses the button and not when a sleeper does.. he can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>An extra success won't let Sleepers cast the effect, if that's what you mean.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4178\" data-vbnamecard=\"4178\">stanlemon</a> Your discussion is getting so confused that I just can't keep it up. Lian, you have distorted stanlemon example to a point that it have nothing to do with the question at hand. Let me try to explain with simple questions:<br /> <br /> 1- Can an hermetic &quot;prepare&quot; a spell in the tranquility of his home enchanting his wand (or whatever instrument) with a Forces 2 effect only to make it levitate anything(up to Forces 2 weight limit) that its pointed by it with just a magick word? Remember, no Time or Prime used. <br /> <br /> 2- Can an etherite &quot;prepare&quot; a spell by building a gravity gun in the tranquility of his lab with a Forces 2 effect, only to make it levitate things (up to Forces 2 weight limit) that are pointed by the gun and &quot;shooted&quot; (pulling a trigger)? It's the same as the #1 question, without Prime or Time, just like the hermetic example.<br /> <br /> 3- If the hermetic hands his wand to his sleeper friend and tells him to say the magic word while pointing it to a tennis ball to make it levitate, it will levitate?<br /> <br /> 4- If the etherite hands his gravity gun to his sleeper friend and tells him to pull the trigger while aiming at a tennis ball to make it levitate, it will?<br /> <br /> Now, if you answered Yes,Yes,No,No we can agree until here. If not, care to explain, please.<br /> <br /> To me, since the hermetic will see that the wand won't work with anyone that doesn't have Forces 2, that is, in-game anyone with an enlightened Will and enough knowledge of the universe's Forces, he understand that the wand is simply a tool to focus their knowledge and Will.<br /> <br /> Now, to the etherite, there is no such thing as Willing something to happen, the power is entirely of the gravity gun. He had the enlightened mind to design and build it, but once built, the device is the source of the power (that's why technomancers have hard time trying to drop focus).<br /> <br /> So, what would the etherite think when he sees that only fellow etherites with knowledge of Forces 2 can make the gravity gun work?<br /> <br /> Please, answer only this question and consider that it is not a Wonder, it has not a complicated trigger, just like the hermetic, all the complications were already made in his lab.<br /> <br /> <b>what would the etherite think when he sees that only fellow etherites with knowledge of Forces 2 can make the gravity gun work?</b><br /> <br /> Won't he realise that the power isn't from his device, but from the user and this wouldn't fuck with all his theories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:36:37-07:00","id":967366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967211#post967211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really just how dense are you? The argument you are making has NOTHING to do with what I am saying. You are saying that I am making claims that I should be able to set things on fire by using life or some nonsense like that and at no point I have made a claim like that which just proves you are completely oblivious to what this debate is about. What I'm saying are logical inconsistencies where between how technology should work within their paradigm and that you have to twist their paradigms to make justifications for why they fit into the rules as set when science and technology don't work like that. Spheres and their limits are exactly that, arbitrary if you paid attention to my actual account on Pillars you would understand that it was about logically being able to do something within their paradigm but as you have done with every single one of your posts is a bunch of false comparisons. Either you are a troll or you just don't understand anything. You are the one making a bunch of absurd claims about what I am talking about that are outright untrue.<br /> <br /> Your Pillar argument is particularly annoying and a great example of your false comparisons and lack of understanding to the topic of this debate. My arguments have been all about how inventing and building things is at the very core of what a technomancer does and believes. It's the machine that has the power and does the work and at most he operates it. Arguments where there is a claim that operating it are at least valid arguments where I've countered that the technomancer would make it as simple as possible because that's what inventors do, but that isn't what you've degraded this into. You just keep making a lot of claims about things that have nothing to do with what I'm saying. Your UFO and raygun example for example. Where I'm talking about the foundation where making things is the core of of what they do regardless of the pillars they focus on you are making claims that I am saying that someone who focuses on making UFOs should be able to make rayguns which is nothing like what I'm saying. The closest is that regardless of what they are making they are still making something and their paradigm posits that it is the device and not them who does whatever the magic they are trying to accomplish so it should still work even with the not around. If you can't understand that then you have failed utterly at understanding anything.<br /> <br /> I would love to know where you are getting things like I'm arguing for punching with intelligence or using spheres that are unrelated to the effect I'm trying to do. Those are things you made up in order to try to discredit what I've been saying without actually debating what I've been saying. The closest I've come was asking why should a technocrat need prime 4 to make a device that sleepers can use when the technocrat paradigm has it that any machine should work as long as the proper sequences are used. So it would be nice if you stopped making up things.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my core argument is, its not at all the basis of the Technomancer Paradigms. Both Etherites and the Technocracy accept the idea of Being a Great Scientist but a Shitty Engineer. I played a Progenitor CSI agent. I didn't Invent new machines, or Drugs or what have you, I used my Hyper Science to track down crimes that were beyond mundane understanding(Mages, Vampires.. etc), SO the idea that every technomancer should be good at making stuff for Sleepers to casually use comes off as nonsensical. <br /> <br /> Or to simply put it. If you want to make an Etherite who can make a raygun who anyone can use. Do that. But there's going to be plenty of Etherites who have UFO crystals only they can use because Technobabble. You have to actively build a character for Engineering to Engineer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:40:11-07:00","id":967367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967364#post967364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Won't he realise that the power isn't from his device, but from the user and this wouldn't fuck with all his theories?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sons of Ether as a Tradition believe that true genius is needed to really practice their Science, so they accept the power of will as a part of what they do, they just have many theories of how it works, from quantum observers to ether particles. Them being a bunch of mages so individualstic doesn't help for them to have a consensus on it, but that's what it makes them what they are. And that's why they are arguing all the time, even between themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:52:53-07:00","id":967371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967356#post967356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a fair point and a completely valid argument. Ultimately, minus the tangents, the two different sides of the argument seem to be on how paradigm should be handled in relation to the rules. And a debate on that can go on forever because on my side of things I like to have the rules integrated with paradigm like DA:M gives whereas you (making an assumption here so correct me if I'm wrong) like to have paradigm fit into the standard rule framework that modern day mage lays out. And as it can be explained away then you are fine with it like how technocrats explain away the magic their enemies use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not an unfair assumption. When it comes to mechanics, I start with the spheres to know more or lease what the character is capable of doing, broad strokes wise. Then I narrow in on the specific effect to see if it makes sense to their paradigm, as well as to determine the specific end result.<br /> <br /> For example. I have a few players that can do Entropy effects. One of them is a Hollow One, the other is a Virtual Adept. If they both tried to do an Entropy effect in order to find the safest route out and away from their enemy. The Virtual Adept would run the numbers and either get a list of direction or even a literal trail map in front of them with the safest route, while the Hollow one would just be able to intuit the correct route while running down it. They'll feel out that they should turn this corner, climb this ladder,and jump over that fence.<br /> <br /> For me, Paradigm will also limit what things the mage will be able to affect with certain sphere levels. For example, a Hermetic who believes that Light and Dark are separate energies would need Forces 3, since it's changing one form of energy into another. However, with Forces 2, they would be able to move and shift the darkness around, perhaps even wear it as a cloak, as though it were its own energy pattern.<br /> <br /> And Etherite who believes in photons, however, would not see such a distinction between Light and Dark. As a consequence, they would be able to turn light into dark with Forces 2 by moving away the photons. The whole idea of &quot;wearing&quot; darkness or moving darkness around would be completely foreign to them, and would make no real sense.<br /> <br /> Paradigm for me functions to limit the mage's thinking into a strict set of parameters. As a result, certain rotes will be impossible for certain mages to perform.<br /> A mage who thinks time is a constant forward movement that cannot be reversed would not be able to Loop time with Time 3.<br /> A Dreamspeaker that considers elemental forces to be the work of spiritual entities may need a bit of Spirit in order to control things like Fire and Wind properly (with Forces on their own being useful only for Kinetic energy, light manipulation, and sound).<br /> A Chorister, who considers themselves to merely be a conduit by which the will of The One is performed might think that a Botched magic effect, or an effect that leads to Paradox Backlash is a demonstration of the Wrath of The One. They would therefor not be able to try the effect again, because they don't believe their deity wants this particular effect to happen.<br /> <br /> That sort of a thing. Again, it's very specific to each individual mage, and similar traditions may still have very different details within their paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:54:48-07:00","id":967372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966931#post966931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eh... That's a rather extreme way of looking at it. The Technocracy are just like the Traditions in terms of Will equals Effect. Similarly they are just like each Tradition in that every single mage beleives what they are doing is the only &quot;real&quot; form of magic, those with methods that are close are kinda there, but those with completely contradictory methods are just plain wrong. If a Spirtual Dreamspeaker and an Techi Etherite talk, Neither of them will consider what the other one is doing is actually all that effective compared to their own techniques. The Dreamspeaker would think that the Etherite was just making a lot of things up on the spot, making a lot of noise and talking a lot of nonsense about science and machines. Sure the effect will be palpable, put the Dreampeaker wouldn't really see a difference between them an any other scientist. The Etherite would, funnily enough, think pretty much the same thing about the Dreamspeaker, that they're babbling on about spirits and mystic stuff, and harp on about old superstitions that don't really have much merit to them. Sure they can see the effects they produce, but to them it's unreliable and wishy-washy. There's nothing these guys do with their houdou vodou that can't be done better and more reliably with a good machine!<br /> <br /> The same it true with the technocrats. Sure they observe the effects of the reality deviants. and acknowledge that they are able to do quite astounding things. But where the Traditions go wrong is by trying to claim all of it is mystical. They say that the spirits are helping them, that it's all in between the numbers, that it's about changing the universal source code, or whatever flimsy explanation they might have. The fact that none of their explanations line up even with fellow members of the same tradition is just proof that everything they're saying to explain their effects is just nonsense. Sure the magic is potent, but these mystics don't understand what they're doing any better than a Sunday driver understands the inside of their own car.<br /> <br /> That is what set's the Technocratic Union apart from the rest of them, they have internal consistency. While Etherites will argue about whether empty space is Ether vs Dark Matter, all members of the union will agree that it is the Cosmological Constant which holds the fabric of space together, and when the time is right, they will be able to utilise this fact to produce new experimental procedures, slowly introduce the ideas to the masses, and then, slowly or suddenly, incorporate them into the zeitgeist where they become mundane.<br /> <br /> When a NSC talks about Post Life Entities, they are doing so not because they &quot;Don't believe in ghosts&quot;, but because the term &quot;ghost&quot; is muddied with so many contradictory definitions based on culture, superstition, and heresay. The Akashics may speak of ghosts like a fox who can turn into a lady and eats the hearts of humans in order to steal their skin, of they may speak of women jilted in life becoming horrible spectres of hatred, with long black hair which obscures their face. The Euthanatos would speak of ghosts as beings who are simply waiting to reincarnate, and are only temporarily trapped until they can pass on. The Celestial Chorus would speak of ghosts as unfortunate souls forever trapped in limbo, or even purgatory depending on what they are taught, awaiting judgement until the end of time. While Etherites have countless theories on ghosts and what they are, some consider them to be simple emotion patterns left as a footprint on the mundane world, others would consider them to be the very soul of a human stripped of a body, other's still will state that ghosts are just memories, kept alive by the combined cognotive resonance energies of the human's who knew the deceased.<br /> <br /> With all these convoluted ideas attached to the word &quot;ghost&quot;. The Union does away with this nonsense by rebranding them in purely analytical terms. When one NSC talks about Post Life Entities, they can be assured that everyone in the room knows exactly what they are talking about without any preconceived notions muddying up the picture. They are talking about an Extra-Dimensional Entitie which is native to the Shadow dimension, more formally known as Entropic Space. That's it. No talk of sentiments or purpose, simple clear cut analytics. That's how the Union get things done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, it's not. That's not the party line. That's taking a reasonable stance that works and, really, isn't much different from the 2-3 sentence description I put at the end of my post as the obvious fix, just broken out with a lot of explication. <br /> <br /> However, this is NOT how the paradigm of the Union is typified (as has been detailed earlier in this thread) . The orthodoxy that is maintained in the game as a core ethos is that the Technocrat rank and file KNOW that magic DOES NOT EXIST. Then, later on, they figure out the &quot;Big Lie&quot; and know that they are doing the same thing as the RD's. Then they contradict this assertion idea all over the place in the remainder of the material either by complete omission or by mental gymnastics that are as tortuous as they are unnecessary. Which leads to the joke conversation I inserted. If you don't believe the supernatural exists, it becomes nigh impossible to fight them effectively. It ends up with every encounter with any sort of RD resulting in a trip to Room 101 (which really seems like it should be more for issues of loyalty to the the orthodoxy of the Union's ideals than as a way to insure endless willful ignorance and incompetence.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:55:37-07:00","id":967373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967364#post967364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An extra success won't let Sleepers cast the effect, if that's what you mean.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4178\" data-vbnamecard=\"4178\">stanlemon</a> Your discussion is getting so confused that I just can't keep it up. Lian, you have distorted stanlemon example to a point that it have nothing to do with the question at hand. Let me try to explain with simple questions:</div> </div> </div> </div>Stanlemon is on a different subject. Its related but different. He believes All Technomancers should intrinsically be good at Engineering(I think) while I believe that's not true at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please, answer only this question and consider that it is not a Wonder, it has not a complicated trigger, just like the hermetic, all the complications were already made in his lab.<br /> <br /> <b>what would the etherite think when he sees that only fellow etherites with knowledge of Forces 2 can make the gravity gun work?</b><br /> <br /> Won't he realise that the power isn't from his device, but from the user and this wouldn't fuck with all his theories? </div> </div> </div>I as an ST don't allow someone to make something that violates their beliefs in Mage. Either the Etherite can make a button anyone can use. Or they can't. If they can't I tell the player &quot;make the effect something any idiot can't do because of Science&quot; and that's that. As a player I accept that the game requires you to tailor it to the Character. Its like a pair of pants that comes with a belt. The game expects you to use a belt.<br /> <br /> But the Etherite might also include things like &quot;observer quantum theory&quot; Etherites include alot of crazy fringe and Psuedoscience in their various systems. I mean presumably the Etherite has already come to some understanding of Paradox and why his devices don't work as well in some places as others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:58:55-07:00","id":967377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967372#post967372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, of course, it's not. That's not the party line. That's taking a reasonable stance that works and, really, isn't much different from the 2-3 sentence description I put at the end of my post as the obvious fix, just broken out with a lot of explication.<br /> <br /> However, this is NOT how the paradigm of the Union is typified (as has been detailed earlier in this thread) . The orthodoxy that is maintained in the game as a core ethos is that the Technocrat rank and file KNOW that magic DOES NOT EXIST. Then, later on, they figure out the &quot;Big Lie&quot; and know that they are doing the same thing as the RD's. Then they contradict this assertion idea all over the place in the remainder of the material either by complete omission or by mental gymnastics that are as tortuous as they are unnecessary. Which leads to the joke conversation I inserted. If you don't believe the supernatural exists, it becomes nigh impossible to fight them effectively. It ends up with every encounter with any sort of RD resulting in a trip to Room 101 (which really seems like it should be more for issues of loyalty to the the orthodoxy of the Union's ideals than as a way to insure endless willful ignorance and incompetence.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, never mind then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:12:59-07:00","id":967387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967372#post967372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, of course, it's not. That's not the party line. That's taking a reasonable stance that works and, really, isn't much different from the 2-3 sentence description I put at the end of my post as the obvious fix, just broken out with a lot of explication.<br /> <br /> However, this is NOT how the paradigm of the Union is typified (as has been detailed earlier in this thread) . The orthodoxy that is maintained in the game as a core ethos is that the Technocrat rank and file KNOW that magic DOES NOT EXIST. Then, later on, they figure out the &quot;Big Lie&quot; and know that they are doing the same thing as the RD's. Then they contradict this assertion idea all over the place in the remainder of the material either by complete omission or by mental gymnastics that are as tortuous as they are unnecessary. Which leads to the joke conversation I inserted. If you don't believe the supernatural exists, it becomes nigh impossible to fight them effectively. It ends up with every encounter with any sort of RD resulting in a trip to Room 101 (which really seems like it should be more for issues of loyalty to the the orthodoxy of the Union's ideals than as a way to insure endless willful ignorance and incompetence.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know the Technocracy looks like a Methodology, they even use that term for their subConventions. Its not. Its an ideology. Which means they rationalize things and can hold two contradictory premises. I live in a world where people call themselves Christian Objectivists I don't really see a problem with Monster Hunters who don't believe in Monsters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:14:11-07:00","id":967388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967373#post967373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stanlemon is on a different subject. Its related but different. He believes All Technomancers should intrinsically be good at Engineering(I think) while I believe that's not true at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand how what I've said probably comes off that way and there is an entire Convention dedicated to engineering. You did however give a good example of technocracy members who aren't engineers or other such things. I was using the engineering aspect as an example of the problems of when paradigm doesn't mix with rules. I admit I'm not particularly eloquent at debates and I probably said things along the way that might make people have certain assumptions to what I've meant which is why I've tried to repeat the paradigm/rules thing multiple times in order to stay on that point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:28:23-07:00","id":967395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967388#post967388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can understand how what I've said probably comes off that way and there is an entire Convention dedicated to engineering. You did however give a good example of technocracy members who aren't engineers or other such things. I was using the engineering aspect as an example of the problems of when paradigm doesn't mix with rules. I admit I'm not particularly eloquent at debates and I probably said things along the way that might make people have certain assumptions to what I've meant which is why I've tried to repeat the paradigm/rules thing multiple times in order to stay on that point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me the mage Rules are a pair of pants that explicitly comes with a belt. They don't fit everyone, but if you use the belt you have a good chance of fitting alot of people, but its not going to be perfect. Rules aren't perfect you need to adapt them to your game.<br /> <br /> <br /> So maybe we should begin again: describe then what you think the Technocracy Foundation Should be if this were DA: Mage or Etherite. What do you think Every Technomancer should do? What do you feel the Foundation should be? It doesn't need to be balanced or gameable just a broad strokes &quot;This is what is the Core of Science&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:14:11-07:00","id":967413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967387#post967387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know the Technocracy looks like a Methodology, they even use that term for their subConventions. Its not. Its an ideology. Which means they rationalize things and can hold two contradictory premises. I live in a world where people call themselves Christian Objectivists I don't really see a problem with Monster Hunters who don't believe in Monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that makes you one of the worst possible monster hunters. Sure it's possible to hold contradictory ideas, but it's seldom practical or efficient. Particularly when one of the ideas directly impacts the ability actualize the mission. Hence the &quot;revolving door on Room 101&quot; and a brain-burned Technocracy or one with a substantial number of members that have to spend lots of time in internal ideological subversion and avoidance to simply stay alive and is, therefore, less efficient or practical. Which could be an interesting Union, if that's how you want them to appear. Literally institutionally schizoid. But it's not the Union as it is portrayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:21:36-07:00","id":967418,"title":"","content":"As far as broad strokes go, I would go with the scientific method which is based on observation, testing, and repeatable experimentation. How to adapt that into broad strokes game rules would take me time to sit down and think about it then test it and refine it to make it playable. It would be that ability to repeat that would be important to what I've said before. I'm not saying that all of their enlightened science should just be usable by anyone but it people with the proper instructions and/or knowledges on what the enlightened science science is based on should be able to at least partially usable. The reason I say that is because what they make or discoveries they find are external to them. Now some things I'll admit might be so far outside a sleeper's experience that it becomes far more difficult to use but it would still raise eyebrows when no unenlightened scientists no matter how intelligent can duplicate the experiment even when they are given all the tools they need to at least do the same things even if they don't understand all the principals. Like a computer for instance, most people don't understand what all the pieces do but most people can at least operate simple functions if they are given the instructions. Or if the are told that mixing a certain amount of chemicals has a certain reaction, most people won't understand the chemistry going on but will know that baking soda and vinegar mix to have an iconic reaction. Simplified examples yes, but I use them to underscore what I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:25:57-07:00","id":967426,"title":"","content":"That's already a thing. Again, this is already covered under the current system. Anyone with sufficient Technocratic Conditioning doesn't count as a sleeper. Technocratic training and Technocratic Conditioning tend to go hand in hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:33:48-07:00","id":967430,"title":"","content":"And what about an Etherite who is more grounded in modern science? They don't have conditioning so what about them? Are you saying that they are like people who just believe in magic? What about if they want to conduct an experiment where they bring in a random sleeper, give them all the instructions to use a machine only telling them that if they follow the instructions exactly then something cool will happen but not tell them what that cool thing is and the sleeper does follow the instructions perfectly and nothing happens? What then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 09-11-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:36:32-07:00","id":967432,"title":"","content":"Etherites are by definition not grounded in modern science. They might use the trappings but they are all about pseudo-science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:47:07-07:00","id":967437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967432#post967432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etherites are by definition not grounded in modern science. They might use the trappings but they are all about pseudo-science.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite a thing to say about Etherites. I've personally played Etherites who are grounded in modern science but aren't members of the technocracy because they can't stand the fact that the technocracy is more concerned with controlling the masses than pure scientific discovery. Etherites are about the wonders of scientific research and discover and sure plenty of them go into the steampuck, star trek, or whatever direction but there is nothing whatsoever stopping them from being grounded in modern science and plenty of them do, that's why they publish their work for peer review.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:50:16-07:00","id":967439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967437#post967437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's quite a thing to say about Etherites. I've personally played Etherites who are grounded in modern science but aren't members of the technocracy because they can't stand the fact that the technocracy is more concerned with controlling the masses than pure scientific discovery. Etherites are about the wonders of scientific research and discover and sure plenty of them go into the steampuck, star trek, or whatever direction but there is nothing whatsoever stopping them from being grounded in modern science and plenty of them do, that's why they publish their work for peer review.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did your character do that couldn't be done with mundane stats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:50:59-07:00","id":967440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967437#post967437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's quite a thing to say about Etherites. I've personally played Etherites who are grounded in modern science but aren't members of the technocracy because they can't stand the fact that the technocracy is more concerned with controlling the masses than pure scientific discovery. Etherites are about the wonders of scientific research and discover and sure plenty of them go into the steampuck, star trek, or whatever direction but there is nothing whatsoever stopping them from being grounded in modern science and plenty of them do, that's why they publish their work for peer review.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they're doing Etherite wrong. Being an Etherite is about developing your own dynamic vision of science. All inclusive science. The very concept of peer review is anathema to the Etherite philosophy. You build up your theories. Your discoveries, and then you kick anyone who tries to tell you you're wrong in the teeth.<br /> <br /> They're a fun concept, to be sure. But they're nothing like a modern scientist. They're more along the lines of the MAD scientist than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:55:07-07:00","id":967443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967440#post967440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then they're doing Etherite wrong. Being an Etherite is about developing your own dynamic vision of science. All inclusive science. The very concept of peer review is anathema to the Etherite philosophy. You build up your theories. Your discoveries, and then you kick anyone who tries to tell you you're wrong in the teeth.<br /> <br /> They're a fun concept, to be sure. But they're nothing like a modern scientist. They're more along the lines of the MAD scientist than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Peer review is anathema to them? Then please explain why their tradition book specifically talks about how they do peer review and that the scientific method is important to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:24:42-07:00","id":967460,"title":"","content":"I dunno what Tradition Book you're reading. But the one I have has a section called &quot;Smash the Method&quot; About, surprise surprise, how the Scientific Method is wrong because it assumes Reductionism is right and because it assumes there can only be one way things are done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:52:04-07:00","id":967472,"title":"","content":"There is a nice little side bar that talks about paradigma talking about peer review in the revised tradition book. Second, in that very smashing the method segment that you talk about it talks about how observation and experimentation are important, the difference is unlike a technocrat who would dismiss say acupuncture out of hand or call it a placebo effect the Etherite will do the standard scientific experiment and then do a secondary experiment where they test it under its own model in which it tests to see if there is some not readily noticeable chi. This is actually a real world problem where real world scientists have ignored traditional herbal medicines because they have their own biases and then much later other more open minded scientists have come in and found that these previously dismissed medicines actually do have pharmaceutical merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:32:52-07:00","id":967503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967472#post967472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a nice little side bar that talks about paradigma talking about peer review in the revised tradition book. Second, in that very smashing the method segment that you talk about it talks about how observation and experimentation are important, the difference is unlike a technocrat who would dismiss say acupuncture out of hand or call it a placebo effect the Etherite will do the standard scientific experiment and then do a secondary experiment where they test it under its own model in which it tests to see if there is some not readily noticeable chi. This is actually a real world problem where real world scientists have ignored traditional herbal medicines because they have their own biases and then much later other more open minded scientists have come in and found that these previously dismissed medicines actually do have pharmaceutical merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It talks about Observation and Experimentation <b>not peer review</b>. And the very ideals it espouses makes a mockery of peer review. You can't have peer review in a world where EVERYTHING is true. Peer review, and the scientific method, posits that most things are false and that only a portion of theories are really right. The point of the review is to ensure that the authors own biases aren't corrupting the experiment.<br /> <br /> Only the Etherites will <i>punch you in the face </i>for telling them they are wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:17:18-07:00","id":967521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967503#post967503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It talks about Observation and Experimentation <b>not peer review</b>. And the very ideals it espouses makes a mockery of peer review. You can't have peer review in a world where EVERYTHING is true. Peer review, and the scientific method, posits that most things are false and that only a portion of theories are really right. The point of the review is to ensure that the authors own biases aren't corrupting the experiment.<br /> <br /> Only the Etherites will <i>punch you in the face </i>for telling them they are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>You obviously don't understand the Etherites as well as you think you do. One, if a Etherite would as you say punch someone if the face for telling them they are wrong, it's not as bad as the genocide that the Technocracy has committed against those who say they are wrong. Secondly an excerpt from the SoE book &quot;They would organize subscriptions, <b>PEER REVIEW</b>, and actual printing.&quot; and that is talking about the Etherite scientific journal Paradigma. Secondly the Etherites are arguably the better scientists because unlike the Technocracy they observe and experiment from multiple points of view in regard to singular subjects thus giving them a better overall understanding of the way the universe works. Sure in our world where as best we can tell reality isn't subjective and follows a strict set of rules that govern the universe, however in Mage where we as players objectively know that the Technocracy is wrong and that the Etherites have accepted that seemingly magical things are happening and have expanded the their methodolgies to include that in their experimentation means that the Etherites have adapted their scientific principles the universe as a whole better than the Technocracy. Example, an Etherite and a Technocrat see a Hermetic cast a fireball and the Technocrat discounts it as an elaborate hoax because to them MAGIC ISN'T REAL whereas the Etherite will see it and think &quot;Cool, how did they do that? Time for some experiments.&quot; They have discarded the models the Technocracy uses because they understand that there is more to the world and more to scientifically study than the Technocratic party line allows for. So in the end as I've already said, their scientific experiments have (as a whole) allowed them to gain a better grasp on the true reality of Mage the the Technocrats have. Unless you go with the purple paradigm where everyone is fully aware be they Traditionalist or Technocrat that reality is consensual and that the Technocracy does what they do because it's convenient for them, in which case they are making just as much an affront to science as you claim the Etherites do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:42:50-07:00","id":967529,"title":"","content":"That's a single sentence. Against an entire philosophy that is as against the concept of peer review as we know it as anything. Secondly Paradigma is GONE. It doesn't exist anymore. Even in the Revised book it's stated that it died.<br /> <br /> And finally, you don't understand the Technocracy at all if that's what you think.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is aware that reality is consensual and has been all along. That's nothing to do with the purple paradigm and everything to do with the way they think. The Technocracies goal is not to Observe and Report. As traditional science dictates. The Technocracies goal is to BUILD the natural world. To write the rules that others would then Observe and report. To build a world where everything can be understood and everything fits together neatly. THAT is Hyperscience. THAT is the difference between the two. The Technocrat acknowledges that the rules don't matter to the universe. And sets out to MAKE them matter. Portraying them as Arbitrary Skeptics is not only stupid, it robs them of much of what makes them WORK as a faction.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Technocracy doesn't kill people because they told the Technocracy they were wrong. They Kill people because those people undermine the consensus that the Technocracy has painstakingly built. Science and Reason are not facts in mage. They're beliefs. And the Technocracy will do ANYTHING to make those beliefs justified. If they have to kill, steal, lie, or yes, even commit genocide. They will do it. Because otherwise you open the door to the crazy house and suddenly you get a world where the earth could possibly randomly vomit forth a demonic horde to lay waste to civilization.<br /> <br /> The Etherite instead sets out to take advantage of that fact. The Rules don't matter because every Rule is true. You just have to believe it enough, or to use their own terminology, you just have to build your wall of troy that way. Therefore everyone is a visionary scientist out to break new ground. Because everyone is different. Everyone's wall encompasses different incomplete pieces of the puzzle, Etc Etc. They take the trappings of science and engineering and use them any which way. Because they can.<br /> <br /> Both have discovered the Truth. One revels in it. The other Abhors it and seeks to kill it.<br /> <br /> THAT is the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:53:15-07:00","id":967538,"title":"","content":"That is more of a purple paradigm viewpoint you espouse. Yes that is how they were written originally, but as time went on that characterization drifted away from both groups making your argument outdated and invalid. The writers (mostly) as time went by realized the problem in even having paradigms when mages understood completely that reality was malleable and that a mage can't truly believe their beliefs were the right way when they know that everyone else's beliefs are equally valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:54:20-07:00","id":967578,"title":"","content":"The other beliefs AREN'T equally valid in the Technocrat or Etherites eyes. Accepting that reality is malleable does not mean they agree on what to do or how to view that malleability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:52:50-07:00","id":967629,"title":"","content":"Except that still doesn't work because Mage as a whole has moved away from the whole &quot;everyone knows about the true nature of reality&quot; reasoning. The Technocracy are about science and technology and don't hate magic because it undermines their control but because it is supernatural crap that is a threat to society in the way a lot of modern day atheists consider religion a threat to society. Unfortunately they also are obsessed with control and controlling every aspect of societies advancement because they believe if they don't then it will be the dangerous and chaotic if they don't. This is a view where they aren't aware they of the true nature of reality but they still control and build society which is what they have become since the early days of Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:06:31-07:00","id":967639,"title":"","content":"Your explanation works if you view the purple paradigm as being the true way but if you are going into the line of the different groups truly believe that it is their way that is right then it becomes harder but not impossible to justify. I personally (and from several other threads I've read, other people do too) however find the story better when mages don't know the truth about reality and they honestly believe they know how reality works and everyone else is wrong and although they might have theories explaining the inconsistency that verge on what we out of game know to be true like what the Void Engineers have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:14:39-07:00","id":967641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967418#post967418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as broad strokes go, I would go with the scientific method which is based on observation, testing, and repeatable experimentation. How to adapt that into broad strokes game rules would take me time to sit down and think about it then test it and refine it to make it playable. It would be that ability to repeat that would be important to what I've said before. I'm not saying that all of their enlightened science should just be usable by anyone but it people with the proper instructions and/or knowledges on what the enlightened science science is based on should be able to at least partially usable. The reason I say that is because what they make or discoveries they find are external to them. Now some things I'll admit might be so far outside a sleeper's experience that it becomes far more difficult to use but it would still raise eyebrows when no unenlightened scientists no matter how intelligent can duplicate the experiment even when they are given all the tools they need to at least do the same things even if they don't understand all the principals. Like a computer for instance, most people don't understand what all the pieces do but most people can at least operate simple functions if they are given the instructions. Or if the are told that mixing a certain amount of chemicals has a certain reaction, most people won't understand the chemistry going on but will know that baking soda and vinegar mix to have an iconic reaction. Simplified examples yes, but I use them to underscore what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am fundimentally missing your problem. I do not understand at all what you want. So I'm going to throw out some examples and see what is closest I am not saying this is what you are saying. I am asking what is closest.<br /> <br /> <br /> Currently an Etherite or Technocrat can make a device that is useable by anyone(but its harder) or they can make one useable for only for Enlightened types. And ones only for themselves. This matches up in broad strokes to my understanding of the real world, there's Stuff made for everyone(iphone for example) stuff made for fellow Makers, and shit people make just for themselves.<br /> <br /> If we were using skills rather than spheres, Forces would be the equivalent of having Physics 6. You just can't explain it to someone who has no physics no matter what and even someone with physics 5 would have trouble understanding. Its just dumbed down for playablity because we aren't all Steven hawkings.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other way I see it is Enlightened Scientist pours baking soda and vinegar together and now forever more it makes an effect. Before the Enlightened Scientist did this though no one else could do it, but now its there forever. Is that what you are edging towards?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:43:37-07:00","id":967658,"title":"","content":"I think that each Mage is attempting to make reality reflect their own beliefs, rather than shaping reality with their will, which is why the Traditions and the Conventions are a bit of a mess. While Mage within each Tradition (or Convention) share similar beliefs, their alliances are based on the beliefs that they reject in common rather than the beliefs that they share in common. In effect, every Mage is insane, it is just that the Marauders are the only ones who are insane enough to gain any mechanically bonuses from their insanity, beyond the ability to shape reality to reflect their beliefs.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think that there should be rules to allow any Mage could create a tool that would serve as a 'lock' that would store one specific rote or procedure that could be used by Sorcerers or Sleepers (whether it is a flaming enchanted sword or a gamma ray laser, it really does not matter). The 'lock' would function as a focus for the Mage and, in order to store the rote, the Mage would have to spend one point of Willpower and one point of Quintessence. Until the Mage withdraws the rote from the 'lock', they could not use the rote and, even worse, they would accumulate any Paradox produced by the 'lock'. I would suggest that a Mage could support one 'lock' per level of Arete.<br /> <br /> If desired, a Mage could permanently transfer a 'lock' to a Sleeper. The Sleeper would spend (Sum of Spheres * Minimum Arete) experience points to 'purchase' the 'lock' from a Mage. Sleepers could spend one point of Willpower or one point of Chi (depending on their training) to activate a 'lock' for a scene or (in the case of instant effects) one use. The 'lock', since it is attuned to a Sleeper that accepts its Reality, would not produce Paradox. Just an idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:41:44-07:00","id":967682,"title":"","content":"Aya.. that's called Prime. and to a lesser extent Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:47:50-07:00","id":967687,"title":"","content":"...seriously, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4178\" data-vbnamecard=\"4178\">stanlemon</a>, you are going back and forth now about how the Mage books contradict themselves.<br /> <br /> This is <i>not new</i>. The books were written by different authors, some of whom take a very dim view of science and modernity in general, and rarely if ever had any remotely thorough editorial process. I'm not actually sure if they had editorial processes that checked for anything aside from spelling and grammar errors.<br /> <br /> You are <i>going</i> to have contradictions in what people take away from the books, especially about various groups, and even issues where the paradigms described therein aren't self-consistent, becasue <i>The Holy Writ Canon Of Mage The Ascension</i> isn't even self-consistent in itself. It's a bunch of in-character viewpoints sprinkled with game mechanics, many of which were one-off things written because they 'felt right'.<br /> <br /> Some views of the Etherites will have them as pseudoscientists who can't into peer review that isn't a hugbox/social club. Some will have them be srs bizness scientists with peer review who focus on descriptivist rather than proscriptivist science and exploration of possibilities, or whatever. Hell, they barely have organizational oversight for consistency of paradigm by design, so maybe they have both depending on which country and state/province/county/etc. you're in.<br /> <br /> And the books will probably support every single one of those interpretations because lol what's editors, self-consistency is THE MAN trying to keep you down<br /> <br /> It's really genuinely up to the ST, the reader, and the player to try and make things self-consistent for their game, their headcanon, and their character. All we can do here is decide what is helpful for doing so, so that others are able to make a good, informed decision on whichever topic we're talking about..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:51:22-07:00","id":967688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967249#post967249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think a more important concern is not the Sphere level, but the one level of permanent Willpower sacrificed per Device. Even if a quarter of Technomancers had sufficient skill, they would not produce more than a handful of Devices per generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trivially fixable if you just go with the optional rule for Technomancer's Toybox where Devices (unlike mystical Talismans) don't cost Permanent Willpower, but also don't really act on their own.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967658#post967658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If desired, a Mage could permanently transfer a 'lock' to a Sleeper. The Sleeper would spend (Sum of Spheres * Minimum Arete) experience points to 'purchase' the 'lock' from a Mage. Sleepers could spend one point of Willpower or one point of Chi (depending on their training) to activate a 'lock' for a scene or (in the case of instant effects) one use. The 'lock', since it is attuned to a Sleeper that accepts its Reality, would not produce Paradox. Just an idea...</div> </div> </div> </div>With a Quintessence cost instead, this is the Prime/Primal Utility 5 effect Master's Enchantment, using the 'Training Montage' instrument. Big favorite of the NWO and Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Though formalizing as an alternate method of teaching/learning Sorcery rituals also seems like a usable idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-11-2016, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:17:07-07:00","id":967703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966931#post966931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... That's a rather extreme way of looking at it. The Technocracy are just like the Traditions in terms of Will equals Effect. Similarly they are just like each Tradition in that every single mage beleives what they are doing is the only &quot;real&quot; form of magic, those with methods that are close are kinda there, but those with completely contradictory methods are just plain wrong. If a Spirtual Dreamspeaker and an Techi Etherite talk, Neither of them will consider what the other one is doing is actually all that effective compared to their own techniques. The Dreamspeaker would think that the Etherite was just making a lot of things up on the spot, making a lot of noise and talking a lot of nonsense about science and machines. Sure the effect will be palpable, put the Dreampeaker wouldn't really see a difference between them an any other scientist. The Etherite would, funnily enough, think pretty much the same thing about the Dreamspeaker, that they're babbling on about spirits and mystic stuff, and harp on about old superstitions that don't really have much merit to them. Sure they can see the effects they produce, but to them it's unreliable and wishy-washy. There's nothing these guys do with their houdou vodou that can't be done better and more reliably with a good machine!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just so... so very unfortunately wrong. You are presuming that all Tradition mages share the belief of their most hardlined, ignorant members. Where exactly does it even hint that all mages believe their magick is the only real kind? The entire foundation of the modern day Council of Nine is that people should have the choice of following their own beliefs, and that a person's beliefs bring value to their lives. A shaman does not expect everyone to have the gift of speaking with the spirits, the destined Euthanatoi do not believe all mages were meant to follow their path, and technomancers don't believe everyone has what it takes to hack the world the way they do. Sure, they might feel that their craft is the best, the way a neurosurgeon finds the brain the most enticing of fields. That does not mean they doubt the validity of genetic research, or tell the mechanic they should change jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:37:15-07:00","id":967712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966970#post966970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that the majority of defenses I've seen in support of sleepers not being allowed to use any enlightened science even if it is something as easy as pushing a button seem to be dependent on the purple paradigm. I've said it before that I think the purple paradigm should be forgotten because it (like the sphere system) is biased towards a small group such as OoH where Will is what shapes reality. But that isn't what mage is about. It's about how Belief is what shapes reality and what a mage believes they are doing IS what they are doing. So when a technocrat is using an antigravity propulsion drive to fly then that is what is happening versus say a dreamspeaker who believes they are being carried by air spirits to fly then that too is happening. To just say that they are both deluding themselves and what they are really doing is just using their Will to fly goes against the very core concept of mage of how beliefs change and shape how reality works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is not about people having their own divorced perceptions of the world and standing amongst peers with their eyes/ears shut. Mage is about the premise that there isn't one right way to view reality, and that there are benefits to looking at the world in different ways.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the faith of the Choirister can grant strength and bring a community together, even if there is no God.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Akashics are right that jobs, money, and the pursuit of power distracts us from a spiritual peace that's within reach, even if that comes at the cost of attachments and ambitions.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Etherites' endless pursuit of fantastical applications for science inspires wonder and lures the masses into their field, even if they can never truly share the creations.<br /> <br /> There is no delusion in the stance that Will is the source of magick. It is not the purple paradigm, for it is not a paradigm at all. Using computers and knowing it is powered by tiny little electrons does not constitute a paradigm except for the most well-versed physicist who can build that into a framework for viewing the rest of the world. Knowing that with their Will they can control reality is literally the first step of becoming a mage, but it doesn't tell the mage WHY the world is the way it is, WHAT is actually happening, or HOW they should use this power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:40:22-07:00","id":967713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967703#post967703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just so... so very unfortunately wrong. You are presuming that all Tradition mages share the belief of their most hardlined, ignorant members. Where exactly does it even hint that all mages believe their magick is the only real kind? The entire foundation of the modern day Council of Nine is that people should have the choice of following their own beliefs, and that a person's beliefs bring value to their lives. A shaman does not expect everyone to have the gift of speaking with the spirits, the destined Euthanatoi do not believe all mages were meant to follow their path, and technomancers don't believe everyone has what it takes to hack the world the way they do. Sure, they might feel that their craft is the best, the way a neurosurgeon finds the brain the most enticing of fields. That does not mean they doubt the validity of genetic research, or tell the mechanic they should change jobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how you're getting that out of what I wrote, fundamentally I agree with you. There's a reason I put &quot;real&quot; in quotation marks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:50:00-07:00","id":967720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967713#post967713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure how you're getting that out of what I wrote, fundamentally I agree with you. There's a reason I put &quot;real&quot; in quotation marks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But you did say &quot;those with completely contradictory methods are just plain wrong&quot;, so I thought you were sharing in stanlemon's stance that mages adhere to their beliefs to the utter exclusion of all others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:02:29-07:00","id":967727,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, missed this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967076#post967076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6072_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6072\" data-vbnamecard=\"6072\">Quantumboost</a> Are you telling me that when a technomancer teaches &quot;simple&quot; instructions like, &quot;pull this trigger&quot;, &quot;turn this key counter clockwise&quot; is in reality teaching a Path?</div> </div> </div> </div>:|<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> If it's &quot;push this button&quot; or &quot;pull this trigger&quot;, then the Technomancer has set things up beforehand so that when it comes time the thing will work properly, rather than fail. Device, Charm, delayed effect, whichever. You've either made it fault-tolerant enough to work in brightest day or darkest night, neither snow nor rain nor heat nor random velociraptors, etc. (Prime 2+), or anticipated what is likely to mess up its operation and taken appropriate precautions (Time-delayed or an Entropy blessing or whatever). If you don't do those things or give it enough duration to last until whenever or something, the Effect is as fragile as spun glass.<br /> <br /> What my &quot;you're teaching someone Technosorcery&quot; example is for is when you teach the Sleeper in question &quot;okay, here is how you set up the missile feed, here's how to work the nanofabricator so it makes the missiles, you do this and this and this to make sure it's well-maintained and won't explode in your face when you fire it, here's what you do if the belt jams&quot;? Yeah, that's teaching them genuine legitimate technomagic. And it'll take awhile, because it's superscience, and that shit is fiddly and difficult to learn for most people. It needs to be fiddly and require brilliance or crazy training to reliably pull off, or you have the very contradiction that my entire line of reasoning is entirely dedicated to rectifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:11:32-07:00","id":967882,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the problem isn't how to make a sleeper use the device, but how would the technomancer react after it failed to work.<br /> <br /> The hermetic would say that the sleeper doesn't have the Will and Knowledge.<br /> <br /> Since some etherites believe in a &quot;mystic science&quot; some could explain by quantum particles in the user mind or whatever bullshit they made up.<br /> But a technocrat, or an etherite that has more of a mundane science paradigm couldn't explain the fact. <br /> Unless technocrats also believe in bullshit like those mystic science explanation, in this case, it is not science what they are doing and they would be extremely hypocritical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:03:31-07:00","id":968003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=966361#post966361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sleeper operating the gun doesn't have to know how it works. Thog the caveman will firebthe rifle if he pullbthe trigger, even if accidentally.<br /> <br /> I agree that you could argue that no laser gun would be so simple as to pull a trigger and shoot. But the etherite could make this way. Even though there is a very complicated mechanism inside it, the trigger is enough to shoot, as the etherite do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The solutions pretty easy: the only way a technomage can make a device simple enough to use for a sleeper to just press a button or trigger etc.. is if they made a Wonder of some kind first. Rote/procedures are done &quot;on the fly&quot; making shit up as you go along, the foci in those cases for technomages aren't going to be fully functioning, totally integrated devices, they're going to be bits and pieces of techno stuff that they &quot;mash up&quot; like macgyver.<br /> <br /> So there's simply no way an etherite could fire laser blasts using a rote/procedure simply by squeezing a trigger on a laser pistol. It would have to be a jury rigged contraption on the spot for it to be a rote/procedure, otherwise it would have to be a Wonder.<br /> <br /> E.g. an etherite using a procedure to fire laser blasts ISN'T going to be able to whip together a robustly functioning laser pistol that looks like it just came off the line... they're going to take a pocket laser pointer, hook it up to a a flux capacitor that taps in to the ether with some bits of random wire, use the circuit board from a busted calculator to control it and then trigger the thing by touching two wires together when the flux in the capacitor reaches the correct reverse polarity to affect the differential ether density of the target.<br /> <br /> Any sleeper trying to &quot;use&quot; the jury rigged device is going to easily get some part wrong and it simply won't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:37:23-07:00","id":968013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967882#post967882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the problem isn't how to make a sleeper use the device, but how would the technomancer react after it failed to work.<br /> <br /> The hermetic would say that the sleeper doesn't have the Will and Knowledge.<br /> <br /> Since some etherites believe in a &quot;mystic science&quot; some could explain by quantum particles in the user mind or whatever bullshit they made up.<br /> But a technocrat, or an etherite that has more of a mundane science paradigm couldn't explain the fact.<br /> Unless technocrats also believe in bullshit like those mystic science explanation, in this case, it is not science what they are doing and they would be extremely hypocritical</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fundamental conceit that needs to be accepted in order for this to make sense is thus:<br /> <br /> Any machine built by an Etherite must require genius to operate. Even if the mechanism of use is simple, it still needs genius either to aim, to power, to focus, or anything else.<br /> <br /> When an Etherite sees a Sleeper use his machine and said machine does not work, either the sleeper is doing something wrong, or their lack of genius means their attempt to use the machine in some way breaks it. A lightning gun may be so delicate that simply holding it in the wrong way would result in some of the contacts becoming loose, and the circuit being broken.<br /> <br /> In order to make their machines more robust, Prime magic must be employed. In this way, the Etherite is investing time and energy into making their machines reliable.<br /> <br /> <br /> The same is true for Technocrats. Their procedures are simply too experimental to be both reliable and user friendly. It takes years of training (and indoctrination) to be able to use some of these devices, simply holding them the wrong way will stop them from working.<br /> <br /> If you think that's far-fetched, then rest assured that this is how science can function in real life. I've been in labs that have apparatus so sensitive and so temperamental that simply touching them will contaminate them to the point of uselessness. If people without sufficient training tried to use these tools, even if they were as simple as pressing a few buttons and letting it all go, simply not being aware of the idiosyncrasies of the work in question can lead to problems.<br /> <br /> Heck, I once had one job in a lab where all the mechanics people had set up the controls for me, and I was just testing samples on it, but for each setting, the interface had to be shifted before the program would run. Once, by accidentally neglected to change the interface, and instead ran the new program immediately, and the whole thing just ground to a halt. Nothing I did made it go again as the program was stuck in its own internal loop. I had to get one of the mechanics back in to reset the program and start it up as if it was new.<br /> This is how temperamental these new machines can be.<br /> <br /> I imagine this is what more grounded Science based Etherites or Technocrats would conclude from seeing sleepers fail to use their machines and procedures. The sleeper has inadvertently done something which has rendered the machine inoperable. Perhaps some of the lasers have misaligned, perhaps a few of the contacts are lost, perhaps he pressed the trigger before the gun had finished preparing its charge. It doesn't matter, the point is that, without training, the sleeper is so likely to break this thing while using it, that it happens every time.<br /> <br /> Etherites would conclude that Sleepers are simply not careful enough, or knowledgeable enough about the delicacy of their works, to use their stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:57:36-07:00","id":968058,"title":"","content":"If etherites instruments were this precise and fragile, then the most simple effect would have a diff 9.<br /> <br /> JoeDuncan, this is one example. I might as well make an etherite that builds a device to be uaed in battlefield. The fact is, to the etherite he's just pulling a trigger, but in reality he's soing much more (using his Will). But he doesnt know that. That's the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:46:38-07:00","id":968083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968058#post968058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If etherites instruments were this precise and fragile, then the most simple effect would have a diff 9.<br /> <br /> JoeDuncan, this is one example. I might as well make an etherite that builds a device to be uaed in battlefield. The fact is, to the etherite he's just pulling a trigger, but in reality he's soing much more (using his Will). But he doesnt know that. That's the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if you're so determined to say &quot;nope, not good enough&quot; to each explanation given to you. Then fine, there's a plot hole in the game. Oh Dear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:07:39-07:00","id":968098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968058#post968058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If etherites instruments were this precise and fragile, then the most simple effect would have a diff 9.<br /> <br /> JoeDuncan, this is one example. I might as well make an etherite that builds a device to be uaed in battlefield. The fact is, to the etherite he's just pulling a trigger, but in reality he's soing much more (using his Will). But he doesnt know that. That's the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>But does he? That's pure Purple Paradigm and that's very much an OoH idea that runs throughout the game like a seam of gold through rock or the mold through blue cheese, depending on your POV. One could just as easily say that it's not his Enlightened Will, it's his Genius or it's just the way SCIENCE! works. <br /> <br /> The whole, &quot;Why can't I hand my blaster to Joe&quot; is an issue, and, like how the Union cognitively deals with the existence of magic, the RAW don't really give a decent way to deal with it. Possibly sink some successes into duration and lock the effect into the Instrument, allow for a way to allocate successes to &quot;anyone can use this&quot; (kinda like &quot;it takes x successes for the effect to work on someone else) OR have it take one dot higher (since the system can't really decide on which way to handle that problem either) and roll with it? Of course it's easier for the creator to use it. He knows all the peculiarities. To hand it off, he has to get everything set up just so to idiot-proof the thing for the mouth-breather he's handing it to. <br /> <br /> I finally, just created a Machine Sphere as a Matter alternate and built the whole concept of being able to &quot;hand the blaster to Joe&quot; into the crunch (and fluff). Kinda like a bush league to create certain kinds of magic objects a la Prime. We're play-testing it right now and it seems to work pretty well. The character with Machine 3 is more likely to make cool stuff for himself, but he has come up with stuff and handed it around from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:29:06-07:00","id":968114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968058#post968058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If etherites instruments were this precise and fragile, then the most simple effect would have a diff 9.<br /> <br /> JoeDuncan, this is one example. I might as well make an etherite that builds a device to be uaed in battlefield. The fact is, to the etherite he's just pulling a trigger, but in reality he's soing much more (using his Will). But he doesnt know that. That's the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your premise is not correct. The Etherite DOES know they are using their Will. The Society of Ether is built on the idea of &quot;what would science look like if our expectations colored the results&quot;. This is what separates them from the Technocracy, who very much want to use science as it exists in the real world. This is also why not all Etherites use the same machines or laws of physics; each has an avenue and style they'd like to explore. Each brilliant mind takes a &quot;what-if this is how reality functioned&quot; and builds a line of inventions that only work when that theory is true. When they run into Paradox or those annoying Sleepers who reject their ideas, they'd just smile, say &quot;but what if...&quot;, and carry on their experimentation. There is no refutation of a theory in the science of the Etherites.<br /> <br /> If large numbers of mages are ignorant about the roll of Will in magic then a ton of the setting unravels out of logical inconsistency. The same is true to a lesser extent of the Technocracy (though someone once made an excellent point that double-think is very 1984). All of these issues disappear if you accept that the process of Awakening means you realize you can control reality with your mind, and that it is only a very small subset of Awakened that willfully refuse this fact. It is the only sensible interpretation of the setting when the Tradition mages have been working closely together for centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:17:45-07:00","id":968135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967882#post967882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the problem isn't how to make a sleeper use the device, but how would the technomancer react after it failed to work.<br /> <br /> The hermetic would say that the sleeper doesn't have the Will and Knowledge.<br /> <br /> Since some etherites believe in a &quot;mystic science&quot; some could explain by quantum particles in the user mind or whatever bullshit they made up.<br /> But a technocrat, or an etherite that has more of a mundane science paradigm couldn't explain the fact.<br /> Unless technocrats also believe in bullshit like those mystic science explanation, in this case, it is not science what they are doing and they would be extremely hypocritical</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, get off your strawman soapbox and <i>listen to what people are telling you</i> for once.<br /> <br /> If the device is actually legitimately set up to fire at the touch of a button, then in a self-consistent technomantic paradigm, <i>it will do so</i>. If it isn't set up that way, <i>it will not</i>. Regardless of who is doing the pressing.<br /> <br /> Plain. And. Fucking. Simple.<br /> <br /> Properly set-up effect with the button pressed by a Sleeper? It works. Properly set-up effect with the button pressed by the Scientist? It works. Improperly set-up effect with the button pressed by a Sleeper? Oh no, it fails. Improperly set-up effect with the button pressed by the Scientist?<br /> <br /> <i>It fails.</i><br /> <br /> That's because the Science isn't in the pressing of the button. There is no Science there, nothing that requires one be Enlightened. The paradigm of the Technomancer simply is not consistent with it differing when the button press is performed by a Sleeper than if performed by the Scientist, nor is Reality, and thus imposing their paradigm on Reality - as Mages do - will not give that result,<br /> <br /> The Science is in the <i>setup</i> that the Enlightened Scientist does beforehand. The button is just a release trigger. If the Scientist can work their Effects from afar, or if they are present, then you the player can roll for it at the moment of the button-press. Otherwise, unless they've made the precautions I've already described to you - <i>at length</i>, multiple times - then... while the Scientist is somewhere else, something must've happened to make the causal chain of whatever happens after the button press 'misalign'. The Scientist can go back and see 'oh, this bit was what made it fail, must'e been jostled' or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But you don't accept that. Which means, simply, that you are not willing - or Willing - to accept a self-consistent technomantic paradigm. No more and no less. That's unfortunate if you personally want to play a technomancer who isn't aware they're a postmodern chaos magician using sciency props, but otherwise not really very important.<br /> <br /> This isn't restricted to technomancers either - if a Shinto priest has blood on them but isn't aware of the fact, their own paradigm should likewise stop their abilities from working. If the paradigm you use and Reality agree that your abilities don't work, they don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you really really just want a Sleeper-usable raygun, here's something that someone I know made for Strike Force Zero, you can adapt it to Etherite aesthetics as you like. It's an Extraordinary Device, so Enlightenment isn't <i>required</i> at any step from manufacture to firing, though it does make things substantially easier. Also won't work too well outside of high-tech areas or modern battlefields. It's advanced technology, not nearly as durable to adverse conditions as an AK-47, you see.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ12_Commando</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Raiden Heavy Electrolaser</b><br /> <br /> Part of the push to make death rays coincidental, the Raiden is a significantly downgraded derivative of the hypertech plasma cannon, although it works on only tangentially related principles. Using a laser to ionize the air into a conductive channel, and then a powerful electrical charge through it, the Raiden is an impressive weapon to see in action and devastating against most targets.<ul><li>Uses Dex + Firearms, Dex + Heavy Weapons, or Dex + Energy Weapons to fire.</li> <li>Damage is adjustable from 1-10 Bashing or Lethal. Every point of Bashing costs 1 power, and every point of Lethal costs 2. If the Raiden deals any levels of unsoaked damage, the target is stunned and is at +1 difficulty to all actions for his next action.</li> <li>Battery has 40 power. Rate 1, Range 150.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Some formatting adjustment to fit with the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-12-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:38:59-07:00","id":968193,"title":"","content":"Something else occurred to me: with the use of any ability in which you roll Traits - Abilities, Arete, etc. - there is the possibility of failure. This is inherent to the system.<br /> <br /> So whenever a technomancer uses a machine, they know that there is the possibility that it will just fail to function, or fail to get the result they desired. So of course, they might not think twice about a Sleeper being unable to get an advanced piece of hardware to work. Parts fail or go on the fritz, glitches in the system pop up, environmental factors work against it. Not even getting into human error. None of these things can be entirely prevented or predicted. Especially in the case of prototypes, they can be tempermental. The entire point of making the prototype is to create a proof of concept, that can then be improved upon in subsequent iterations.<br /> <br /> The iteration that can be reliably used by anyone (who isn't very familiar with the tech and knows how to minimize complications) is called a Device. Many of the bugs have been worked out, and the thing has no more control options distracting a user than it needs to do a particular function or functions. The iteration that has been refined to the point where the tech is stable, and can be used under most any condition, is a machine accepted into the Consensus. (Although, even then, things can still always go wrong).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T18:48:09-07:00","id":968300,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6072_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6072\" data-vbnamecard=\"6072\">Quantumboost</a> Calm down. My issue isn't &quot;how to make a one-button gun&quot; rather what the hell would the technomancer think when he sees a guy doing EXACTLY the same thing he do and the device not working...EVERYTIME.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6807_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6807\" data-vbnamecard=\"6807\">moogle001</a> Ok, then what would a technocrat think?<br /> <br /> Please, forget the &quot;to make it one button work do this&quot; thing. All those wall of text aren't really helping. IF the technomancer doesn't believe in magic or observer afecting reality (normal real world proved science) what kind of explanation would he have to made up, or would he just rethink his paradigm?<br /> <br /> Also, technocrats seeing people flying and shooting fireballs can't believe it's a trick unless they'e morons. I know people stated that they were brainwashed, so there is this immense number of brainwash in Technocracy? (Every time they see something vulgar)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:16:09-07:00","id":968310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968193#post968193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else occurred to me: with the use of any ability in which you roll Traits - Abilities, Arete, etc. - there is the possibility of failure. This is inherent to the system.<br /> <br /> So whenever a technomancer uses a machine, they know that there is the possibility that it will just fail to function, or fail to get the result they desired. So of course, they might not think twice about a Sleeper being unable to get an advanced piece of hardware to work. Parts fail or go on the fritz, glitches in the system pop up, environmental factors work against it. Not even getting into human error. None of these things can be entirely prevented or predicted. Especially in the case of prototypes, they can be tempermental. The entire point of making the prototype is to create a proof of concept, that can then be improved upon in subsequent iterations.<br /> <br /> The iteration that can be reliably used by anyone (who isn't very familiar with the tech and knows how to minimize complications) is called a Device. Many of the bugs have been worked out, and the thing has no more control options distracting a user than it needs to do a particular function or functions. The iteration that has been refined to the point where the tech is stable, and can be used under most any condition, is a machine accepted into the Consensus. (Although, even then, things can still always go wrong).</div> </div> </div> </div>But when it fails to work every single time then that becomes a pattern and is no longer a chance of it not work. Any good scientist would notice that pattern and try to find out why. When a sleeper does all the things the Technomancer does to operate a device and it fails once is chance, twice is a coincidence, but every time it becomes something that needs to be investigated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:27:03-07:00","id":968316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968300#post968300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6072_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6072\" data-vbnamecard=\"6072\">Quantumboost</a> Calm down. My issue isn't &quot;how to make a one-button gun&quot; rather what the hell would the technomancer think when he sees a guy doing EXACTLY the same thing he do and the device not working...EVERYTIME.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6807_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6807\" data-vbnamecard=\"6807\">moogle001</a> Ok, then what would a technocrat think?<br /> <br /> Please, forget the &quot;to make it one button work do this&quot; thing. All those wall of text aren't really helping. IF the technomancer doesn't believe in magic or observer afecting reality (normal real world proved science) what kind of explanation would he have to made up, or would he just rethink his paradigm?<br /> <br /> Also, technocrats seeing people flying and shooting fireballs can't believe it's a trick unless they'e morons. I know people stated that they were brainwashed, so there is this immense number of brainwash in Technocracy? (Every time they see something vulgar)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Technocrat would just think said procedure isn't reliable enough in the hands of the untrained masses, more work will need to be done on the procedure to improve it.<br /> <br /> As far as the &quot;seeing shooting fireballs&quot; thing, it depends what kind of Technocrat they are.<br /> If they are a Sympathiser (i.e. a sleeper) then they will probably start to ask a few questions. Questions are expected, but seldom tolerated for long, Sympathisers are encouraged to treat mages as potentially dangerous. If they start to believe that the Traditions are right, and that their explanation of magic is correct, however, that would certainly be enough to consider Room 101 depending on how said opinion develops.<br /> If they are an Extraordinary Citizen (The Technocracy's Sorcerers), then they may see what the Traditions are doing, they will most likely describe it as something science has yet to explain, but will do one day, and will be quite amused by the superstisious rubbish such mystics use to describe away their effects. &quot;Focusing your chi to conjure a ball of energy? Yeah, we've got theories about Balled Lightning too, it's a build up of atomic forces condensed into a point so small that it causes a chain reaction in the localised area of space. There's nothing mystical about it, and there's certainly has nothing to do with &quot;mental energy&quot; or whatever you call it. One day we'll find a way to reliably create it by hand, but for now, that's what plasma canons are for.&quot; However, if they start to get too chummy with the traditions, then Room 101 may be considered.<br /> Enlightened Scientists are a bit more keyed up on things, however. The lower ranks may share some of the views of the Extraordinary Citizens, but with a tinge of understanding of what a will worker is, and how what they do is basically undoing the work done by the union. They are therefor dangerous not just because of their activity, but because they threaten to drag the masses back down into the dark ages (or whatever weird &quot;utopia&quot; this guys are deluded with). Seeing the fire up close doesn't really shake this view. They know what these guys are capable off, but they also know that they can do it much better, and much more consistently. If an Enlightened Scientist starts to share these delusions, however, Room 101 would be considered.<br /> Higher Ranked Enlightened Scientists, however, have the clearest picture of the nature of the consensus, and that the Union's job is to make a predictable and reliable consensus for all of the masses to live by safely and securely. Reality deviants are the antithesis of this vision. Their very existence undermines the consensus they have worked so hard to maintain. These are the guys who are in favour of reinstating the Pogrom. Other don't see these Reality Deviants as a threat, but rather as a sign of how much more work there is to be done. They know that the Union has created the dominant paradigm, and that the number of Reality Deviants is slowly decreasing as their influence spreads. Already many members of the Traditions are adopting technology into their practices, it's only a matter of time before the distinction between Technocrat and Tradition mage becomes a matter of heritage rather than practice. Technocrats at this level are so set within the Technocracy that it's very unlikely they would ever require Room 101.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Conditioning, I sort of imagine Room 101 to be almost a last resort. Many other more useful methods exist including propaganda, group pressure, fear of the &quot;other&quot; and the &quot;them vs us&quot; mentality, etc. They'd restrict the Room 101 stuff only for people who are directly sabotaging their efforts or are so far gone that the only way inside is to break them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:28:24-07:00","id":968318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968310#post968310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But when it fails to work every single time then that becomes a pattern and is no longer a chance of it not work. Any good scientist would notice that pattern and try to find out why. When a sleeper does all the things the Technomancer does to operate a device and it fails once is chance, twice is a coincidence, but every time it becomes something that needs to be investigated.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be the thing which triggers said Technomancer to invest in the Prime sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:30:27-07:00","id":968319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968300#post968300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6807_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6807\" data-vbnamecard=\"6807\">moogle001</a> Ok, then what would a technocrat think?<br /> <br /> Please, forget the &quot;to make it one button work do this&quot; thing. All those wall of text aren't really helping. IF the technomancer doesn't believe in magic or observer afecting reality (normal real world proved science) what kind of explanation would he have to made up, or would he just rethink his paradigm?<br /> <br /> Also, technocrats seeing people flying and shooting fireballs can't believe it's a trick unless they'e morons. I know people stated that they were brainwashed, so there is this immense number of brainwash in Technocracy? (Every time they see something vulgar)</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds to me that you and I agree that Awakened members of the Technocracy being ignorant of the power of Will and the Consensus is problematic at best. To me, it is clear that the Technocracy's members know all about it because the books repeatedly discuss (from their POV) the importance of shaping the Consensus and how vulgar Enlightened Science is frowned upon. While I can give some leniency to illogical thinking because of brainwashing, I also agree that Room 101 is not sufficient justification for the Enlightened being blind to what they're actually doing.<br /> <br /> To answer what I think your question is, the Enlightened Technocrats operate their Will but shackles it with the constraints that their effects should be reproducible and not contradictory with established science. We have centuries of established knowledge of how the world works, and Technocrats choose to build upon that rather than replace it. Seriously, if this is not a deliberate choice they are making, why do the Technocrats talk about recruiting the newly Awakened to their way of thinking?<br /> <br /> If you're just proposing a thought experiment about how a Technocrat who IS truly ignorant of the Will and Consensus rationalizes a world of magic, I would refer to the Cthulu mythos. There is an alien existence of magic and horror that is intruding upon our reality and threatening its existence. To understand it is to be driven mad; the only hope is resisting it. I think this belief justifies an individual Technocrat, but it does not scale to the entire organization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:21:16-07:00","id":968333,"title":"","content":"Of course, one of the factors that helps the Technocracy is that they are the Establishment. You want to shut down a member of the Traditions? Use a robot to plant drugs in their house and have your connections at the DEA snag them. Have a few Extraordinary Citizens accompany the raid as 'Homeland Security' agents so that they can Counterspell the magic of the Tradition Mage. If the Tradition Mage tries to do magic, their Paradox will go through the roof as the Counterspells do not prevent Paradox from accruing. After the Tradition Mage is knocked out by backlash, use your connections to transfer them to 'Homeland Security'. When they next resurface, they will be working for your team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:33:11-07:00","id":968358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968300#post968300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6072_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6072\" data-vbnamecard=\"6072\">Quantumboost</a> Calm down. My issue isn't &quot;how to make a one-button gun&quot; rather what the hell would the technomancer think when he sees a guy doing EXACTLY the same thing he do and the device not working...EVERYTIME.</div> </div> </div> </div>:|<br /> <br /> Your issue is that for some reason you are unwilling to accept &quot;that is not actually going to happen, because Scientists have super-intuition and the Sleepers don't unless they're borrowing it&quot; as a resolution.<br /> <br /> It's like your question is &quot;why can't my grandma who never saw a computer program Microsoft Word&quot;. Like, exactly equivalent.<br /> <br /> The chances of her actually doing all the right keystrokes and clicks at exactly the right times is so phenomenally unlikely that the system doesn't even bother modeling it.<br /> <br /> And the noise for if it does happen to occur is so far below the noise threshold that nobody could tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, technocrats seeing people flying and shooting fireballs can't believe it's a trick unless they'e morons. I know people stated that they were brainwashed, so there is this immense number of brainwash in Technocracy? (Every time they see something vulgar) </div> </div> </div>&quot;Blatant misuse of psychic powers&quot; or &quot;misuse of Genius to do dumb things&quot; is the means I've seen used to pave over that little bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:57:40-07:00","id":968363,"title":"","content":"Indeed, Psionics is practically a blank check for explaining what the mystics do. It's also why the Technocracy suppresses it in the Consensus, alongside realistic holograms and nanomachines. If those three got out, everything could be explainable (and thus coincidental).<br /> <br /> And really, the Technocracy's upper echelons couldn't ask for a better cover story to feed to the rank and file. It neatly explains patently absurd feats, and undermines the fundamental paradigms of their competition. The Practices of traditionalists are painted as crutches to focus psionic ability, rather than being the outgrowth of valid world views. Moreover, it can imply that the Traditions are not only delusional, but possibly mentally unstable. After all, that much channeling of Genius through raw thought (assisted by superfluous mystic trappings) can't be good for the psyche, and there are plenty of psychopathic Chakravanti, obsessive compulsive Hermetics, and shamans who talk to themselves to support the point. From that perspective, any given Traditionalist is only a few steps away from going full Marauder.<br /> <br /> No, it's better for good Technocrats to channel Inspired Science through technology, which won't twist the user's mind into knots until they have delusions of godhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:17:34-07:00","id":968474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan </strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Can an hermetic &amp;quot;prepare&amp;quot; a spell in the tranquility of his home enchanting his wand (or whatever instrument) with a Forces 2 effect only to make it levitate anything(up to Forces 2 weight limit) that its pointed by it with just a magick word? Remember, no Time or Prime used. <br /> <br /> 2- Can an etherite &amp;quot;prepare&amp;quot; a spell by building a gravity gun in the tranquility of his lab with a Forces 2 effect, only to make it levitate things (up to Forces 2 weight limit) that are pointed by the gun and &amp;quot;shooted&amp;quot; (pulling a trigger)? It's the same as the #1 question, without Prime or Time, just like the hermetic example.<br /> <br /> 3- If the hermetic hands his wand to his sleeper friend and tells him to say the magic word while pointing it to a tennis ball to make it levitate, it will levitate?<br /> <br /> 4- If the etherite hands his gravity gun to his sleeper friend and tells him to pull the trigger while aiming at a tennis ball to make it levitate, it will?<br /> <br /> Now, if you answered Yes,Yes,No,No we can agree until here. If not, care to explain, please.<br /> <br /> To me, since the hermetic will see that the wand won't work with anyone that doesn't have Forces 2, that is, in-game anyone with an enlightened Will and enough knowledge of the universe's Forces, he understand that the wand is simply a tool to focus their knowledge and Will.<br /> <br /> Now, to the etherite, there is no such thing as Willing something to happen, the power is entirely of the gravity gun. He had the enlightened mind to design and build it, but once built, the device is the source of the power (that's why technomancers have hard time trying to drop focus).<br /> <br /> So, what would the etherite think when he sees that only fellow etherites with knowledge of Forces 2 can make the gravity gun work?<br /> <br /> Please, answer only this question and consider that it is not a Wonder, it has not a complicated trigger, just like the hermetic, all the complications were already made in his lab.<br /> <br /> <b>what would the etherite think when he sees that only fellow etherites with knowledge of Forces 2 can make the gravity gun work?</b><br /> <br /> Won't he realise that the power isn't from his device, but from the user and this wouldn't fuck with all his theories?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quantumboost, please answer rhose questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:24:43-07:00","id":968534,"title":"","content":"((Am I even in this conversation anymore?))<br /> <br /> 1. No he cannot. You cannot enchant anything without prime. The wand is but a focus, it hold no power outside of the mage who wields it.<br /> 2. Again, No. The gun is but a focus. The time he'd put into making the gun would essentially be like putting time into making a rote. The effect only happens as he turns on his gun, and thus starts focusing on the effect at hand. Without Prime, the gun itself hold no intrinsic power (unless he did some mundane technology stuff to it in addition).<br /> 3. No, the mage must be the one to use their focus, and only those who use similar focuses or have aligned paradigms would be able to get an effect out of them.<br /> 4. No, the same mechanics of the game apply to all.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind is that not all Etherites with Force 2 would be able to get the gravity gun to work. Some would consider the science behind a gravity gun impossible because they don't subscribe to the specific theories behind what is supposed to make this gun work.<br /> <br /> This is not unlike one Verbena thinking that the Crystal magic another Verbena does is silly and rather trivialised the more primordial practices involving blood rituals and runes. This Verbena may consider crystals to be pretty, but on the whole not all that effective compared to their tried and true methods.<br /> <br /> Same thing with Etherites, One might say the gravity gun is quaint, but rather antiquated compared to their Relative Field Theory of Etheric Particle Physics. With their newest device, they'll be able to rend an objects momentum in physical space changable via electrode impulses that disrupt their etheric fields. None of this &quot;Gravity particle manipulation&quot; stuff, which while effective enough, doesn't really make all that much sense on the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> Etherites are really difficult to get to work together, so many competing theories usually results in more arguments than actual work being done.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to answer your question for the Nth time. They could think the following:<br /> <br /> - These sleepers are idiots! There's nothing wrong with my machines! My machines are perfect! It's their lack of Genius which is at fault. Yes, everyone! True Genius is so hard to come by these days...<br /> - The gun is dealing with delicate forces, so the slightest mistake in its use will obviously result in in failure. Pulling the trigger before the power is at capacity, or letting the power reach over capacity, firing the gun at an inappropriate frequency, These machines can be quite temperamental... Hmm... Perhaps I should invest some research time into these Primal Field Theories I keep hearing about, from the cursory reading I've done, they seem to produce more robust machines with out as much need for specialised training or Genius to operate.<br /> - If they don't understand the theory behind the machine, then how in the world can they know what they are doing? Without theoretical understanding, of course they won't know what to aim the gun at. Not the object itself, but the field that hold the object within gravity's constraint!<br /> <br /> The one things they are very unlikely to think is that their devices are irrelevant when it comes to effects. The only thing that might grant such an insight is a Seeking and a sufficiently high level of Arete.<br /> <br /> Even then, their theories will still be at the core of their practice, machines or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:15:09-07:00","id":968591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968534#post968534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">((Am I even in this conversation anymore?))<br /> <br /> 1. No he cannot. You cannot enchant anything without prime. The wand is but a focus, it hold no power outside of the mage who wields it.<br /> 2. Again, No. The gun is but a focus. The time he'd put into making the gun would essentially be like putting time into making a rote. The effect only happens as he turns on his gun, and thus starts focusing on the effect at hand. Without Prime, the gun itself hold no intrinsic power (unless he did some mundane technology stuff to it in addition).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry if you felt ignored. <br /> <br /> Here, my friend, is where we diverge. The OoH Tradition book has this part covering &quot;prepared&quot; spells. Just like a D&amp;D wizard, the hermetic casts 90% of the spell before, in the form of enchanting a wand for example, and later in the battlefield he just shouts the magic word and points, casting the remaining 10%.<br /> <br /> This is possible and is covered in the book. The same happens when a etherite use a technological device created by him. The magick begins in the lab and takes place when he pushes that little button of the gravity gun. <br /> Of course the gravity gun is not magical per se. It's the etherite Will focusing his magick through his instrument, the gun.<br /> Until we can't agree on this, we will not be able to continue the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:21:48-07:00","id":968596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968591#post968591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry if you felt ignored.<br /> <br /> Here, my friend, is where we diverge. The OoH Tradition book has this part covering &quot;prepared&quot; spells. Just like a D&amp;D wizard, the hermetic casts 90% of the spell before, in the form of enchanting a wand for example, and later in the battlefield he just shouts the magic word and points, casting the remaining 10%.<br /> <br /> This is possible and is covered in the book. The same happens when a etherite use a technological device created by him. The magick begins in the lab and takes place when he pushes that little button of the gravity gun.<br /> Of course the gravity gun is not magical per se. It's the etherite Will focusing his magick through his instrument, the gun.<br /> Until we can't agree on this, we will not be able to continue the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fine, let's pretend we agree. How about the rest of my response?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:40:52-07:00","id":968612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968474#post968474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantumboost, please answer rhose questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a paradigm essentialist standpoint, and assuming it's a genuine Technomancer and not a chaos magician masquerading as an Etherite:<br /> <br /> 1. Yes. However, his preparations will need to be at least partially incorporated into himself. It's not in the wand, it's in the Hermetic + wand + whatever forces he's invoking.<br /> 2. Yes. However, his preparations will need to be at least partially incorporated into himself. It's not in the gun, it's in the Etherite + gun + circumstances.<br /> 3. No. He could prepare the Sleeper beforehand, but just 'handing it off' is inadequate.<br /> 4. No. He could prepare the Sleeper beforehand, but just 'handing it off' is inadequate.<br /> <br /> The Etherite would think that he hadn't prepared the Sleeper to fire the gravity gun beforehand, so of course he can't make it work. It'd be like him trying to fire off the gravity beam by pointing his hand in a firing position and going 'pew pew' - part of the instrument is missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> To use a Technocratic example, let's say we have an Iterator who builds a fancy gravitic projector. They're a very Void Engineerish Iterator, you see. So they build this gun, but they want to be able to physically just point it and pull the trigger. But there's a lot of things that could go wrong with this, and the Iterator doesn't know how to build Devices, he's got better things to do, like shoot shit with sweet gravity weapons..<br /> <br /> So he writes up a device driver for the weapon, installs it on his ADEI, and uses his smartlink system to link up to the gun's regulatory system CPU. He fires the gun, gravity smashes an old car in the junkyard, everything is gravy (that is a pun).<br /> <br /> Then he hands it to a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> The Sleeper points the gun at another car, pulls the trigger and... nothing happens.<br /> <br /> So naturally, the Iterator concludes &quot;OH MY GOD I'M A MAGICAL WIZARD&quot;<br /> <br /> wait no<br /> <br /> He doesn't conclude that, he concludes that the Sleeper isn't a kickass cyborg with the right drivers and smartlink setup. <i>Obviously</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:30:37-07:00","id":968638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968058#post968058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">JoeDuncan, this is one example. I might as well make an etherite that builds a device to be uaed in battlefield.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revan, you're either failing to understand the replies given to you, or simply unwilling to accept them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968058#post968058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact is, to the etherite he's just pulling a trigger, but in reality he's soing much more (using his Will). But he doesnt know that. That's the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, that is incorrect. <br /> <br /> Technomancers don't Will things simply by &quot;thinking about it hard&quot;; the imposition of a Technomancer's Will MUST be mediated through their foci, which is why technomancers can NEVER abandon their foci, and their foci are physical things. <br /> <br /> Ergo, when you say the Etherite is not simply &quot;pulling the trigger&quot; but *also* using his WILL to make the device fire, the fact is that to &quot;USE his Will&quot; the Etherite MUST do something physical which is MORE than simply pulling a trigger and mentally wishing it to work (because mental wishes are NOT how the technomancer paradigm works!!!). <br /> <br /> That bit about the &quot;Etherite using his Will&quot; MUST have a real world physical correlate in terms of actions the Etherite is performing with his foci: e.g. using bits of wire to hook up an old laser pointer to a source of ether, monitoring a gauge readout for the correct values for when to fire etc...<br /> <br /> So the only two scenarios that make any sense in your example are:<br /> <br /> 1) The Etherite makes a Device in advance, which can be activated by anyone, sleeper or not. A sleeper picks up the device and fires it, it works, so no problem.<br /> <br /> 2) The Etherite uses a Procedure and his foci to shoot laser blasts, this involves &quot;MacGyvering&quot; stuff with his foci (elctronics tools, components etc...) to create the effect. A sleeper then picks up the jury rigged device, tries to use it and it fails. Again this isn't a real problem for the Etherite because he would just explain it like (oh, well you connected the flux inverter to the polarizing anode instead of the tachyon cathode and you didn't know how to read the eather capacitance gauge properly to know when to fire...).<br /> <br /> In the Technomantic paradigm &quot;Willing&quot; something is not some intangible mental act, it involves actually, physically, DOING something to make said &quot;Will&quot; manifest.<br /> <br /> If you still don't see this, then I'm afraid no one can help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T16:30:59-07:00","id":968820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968596#post968596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fine, let's pretend we agree. How about the rest of my response?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we agree that it is possible to build an instrument (gun) in a lab just like an hermetic does with his staff to quickly shoot in the battlefield with but a simple magic wod, which in the case of the Etherite would be a button, then there is no way the etherite would think that the sleeper could have pushed the button wrong. And ALL the sleepers push the button wrong. And ALL the mages which deosn't share Forces 2 and his instrument (technological devices) pushes the button wrong.<br /> <br /> While we as players know that it is required an enlightened mind and Will to make the effect happen through the instrument, the technomancer think the effect is cast by the instrument itself. That's why they have such a hard time droping instruments.<br /> <br /> Please, don't make examples, the situation is this one: Etherite creates a gravity gun in his lab, his instrument is technological devices/guns. The magick begins in its construction and ends when the etherite pushes just a button. That's it. Aim and pushes the button. Don't add bullshit to this example to try to explain it. Now, what do you think would cross the etherite mind when EVERYONE that doesn't have knowledge in Forces 2 AND share his paradigm/instrument fail to use the gravity gun.<br /> <br /> This is what we must discuss after you agree that it's possible to use this focus just like the hermetic do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T16:42:34-07:00","id":968822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968612#post968612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a paradigm essentialist standpoint, and assuming it's a genuine Technomancer and not a chaos magician masquerading as an Etherite:<br /> <br /> 1. Yes. However, his preparations will need to be at least partially incorporated into himself. It's not in the wand, it's in the Hermetic + wand + whatever forces he's invoking.<br /> 2. Yes. However, his preparations will need to be at least partially incorporated into himself. It's not in the gun, it's in the Etherite + gun + circumstances.<br /> 3. No. He could prepare the Sleeper beforehand, but just 'handing it off' is inadequate.<br /> 4. No. He could prepare the Sleeper beforehand, but just 'handing it off' is inadequate.<br /> <br /> The Etherite would think that he hadn't prepared the Sleeper to fire the gravity gun beforehand, so of course he can't make it work. It'd be like him trying to fire off the gravity beam by pointing his hand in a firing position and going 'pew pew' - part of the instrument is missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it. You answered number 2 yes, which means he can activate is with a touch of a button. But later you said that it needs a preparation...in the battlefield? What would that preparation be, teaching a path?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968612#post968612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To use a Technocratic example, let's say we have an Iterator who builds a fancy gravitic projector. They're a very Void Engineerish Iterator, you see. So they build this gun, but they want to be able to physically just point it and pull the trigger. But there's a lot of things that could go wrong with this, and the Iterator doesn't know how to build Devices, he's got better things to do, like shoot shit with sweet gravity weapons..<br /> <br /> So he writes up a device driver for the weapon, installs it on his ADEI, and uses his smartlink system to link up to the gun's regulatory system CPU. He fires the gun, gravity smashes an old car in the junkyard, everything is gravy (that is a pun).<br /> <br /> Then he hands it to a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> The Sleeper points the gun at another car, pulls the trigger and... nothing happens.<br /> <br /> So naturally, the Iterator concludes &quot;OH MY GOD I'M A MAGICAL WIZARD&quot;<br /> <br /> wait no<br /> <br /> He doesn't conclude that, he concludes that the Sleeper isn't a kickass cyborg with the right drivers and smartlink setup. <i>Obviously</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Then the answer of my question number 2 should be no, since you're requiring the to be a kickass cybor with the right drivers and smartlink setup.<br /> <br /> So let me ask you a question. If a fellow Etherite which uses &quot;devices and machines&quot; instrument and has Forces 2, but isn't a kickas cyborg with the right drivers and smartlink setup gets the gun and shoots. Visually, he's just like that sleeper that couldn't use it. What would the kickass cyborg think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T16:47:40-07:00","id":968823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968638#post968638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revan, you're either failing to understand the replies given to you, or simply unwilling to accept them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I believe you're not understaing my reasoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968638#post968638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, that is incorrect.<br /> <br /> Technomancers don't Will things simply by &quot;thinking about it hard&quot;; the imposition of a Technomancer's Will MUST be mediated through their foci, which is why technomancers can NEVER abandon their foci, and their foci are physical things.<br /> <br /> Ergo, when you say the Etherite is not simply &quot;pulling the trigger&quot; but *also* using his WILL to make the device fire, the fact is that to &quot;USE his Will&quot; the Etherite MUST do something physical which is MORE than simply pulling a trigger and mentally wishing it to work (because mental wishes are NOT how the technomancer paradigm works!!!).<br /> <br /> That bit about the &quot;Etherite using his Will&quot; MUST have a real world physical correlate in terms of actions the Etherite is performing with his foci: e.g. using bits of wire to hook up an old laser pointer to a source of ether, monitoring a gauge readout for the correct values for when to fire etc...<br /> <br /> So the only two scenarios that make any sense in your example are:<br /> <br /> 1) The Etherite makes a Device in advance, which can be activated by anyone, sleeper or not. A sleeper picks up the device and fires it, it works, so no problem.<br /> <br /> 2) The Etherite uses a Procedure and his foci to shoot laser blasts, this involves &quot;MacGyvering&quot; stuff with his foci (elctronics tools, components etc...) to create the effect. A sleeper then picks up the jury rigged device, tries to use it and it fails. Again this isn't a real problem for the Etherite because he would just explain it like (oh, well you connected the flux inverter to the polarizing anode instead of the tachyon cathode and you didn't know how to read the eather capacitance gauge properly to know when to fire...).<br /> <br /> In the Technomantic paradigm &quot;Willing&quot; something is not some intangible mental act, it involves actually, physically, DOING something to make said &quot;Will&quot; manifest.<br /> <br /> If you still don't see this, then I'm afraid no one can help you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That's another issue. According the books, every mage is actually using their Will upon reality, even that lots of users in this forum doesn't like this concept. What you are saying is also answering my number 2 question a big no. No, the etherite cannot use an instrument like a hermetic that builds it in his home and later just activates by a magic word (or button) and his will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:00:59-07:00","id":968832,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;Will&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:33:32-07:00","id":968849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968820#post968820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, don't make examples, the situation is this one: Etherite creates a gravity gun in his lab, his instrument is technological devices/guns. The magick begins in its construction and ends when the etherite pushes just a button. That's it. Aim and pushes the button. Don't add bullshit to this example to try to explain it. Now, what do you think would cross the etherite mind when EVERYONE that doesn't have knowledge in Forces 2 AND share his paradigm/instrument fail to use the gravity gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what he thinks? He thinks that perhaps he should stop giving his stuff to Sleepers because they're obviously too stupid to use them. The fact that his devices work for everyone who has Force 2 AND shares his paradigm is proof enough for him that all you need to work his stuff is the right know-how. Other mages don't have that know-how. Sleepers especially couldn't possibly have the right know-how.<br /> <br /> Yes, you need know-how even to aim and push the button because you need to know WHAT you're aiming at and WHEN to push the button. Nothing is simple for an Etherite, because if it was simple then it wouldn't be &quot;Science!&quot;<br /> <br /> And if that's not good enough for you, then what the heck are you expecting out of this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:26:45-07:00","id":968886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968823#post968823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. That's another issue. According the books, every mage is actually using their Will upon reality, even that lots of users in this forum doesn't like this concept. What you are saying is also answering my number 2 question a big no. No, the etherite cannot use an instrument like a hermetic that builds it in his home and later just activates by a magic word (or button) and his will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure he could, provided that the part about the Etherite exercising his Will involved him actually doing something &quot;techno-sciency&quot; to activate the efftect. Think Dr. Who or MacGyver.<br /> <br /> This is how I interpret it anyway, but I would go so far as to say that even most mystic paradigm mages can't just intangibly Will something either.<br /> <br /> If I was ST, I would say that for the Hermetic who made the wand as part of a hanging Rote - that his activation of it would require *something* more tangible than him just pointing, saying a word and &quot;wishing&quot; for it in his head. At least until they get to near Oracle level in spheres - then mystics are able to abandon their Foci. But technomancers can never abandon their Foci, thus they will always be required to do *something* physical to manifest their Will and enact their hung Procedures, it's what their paradigm says, how their belief works.<br /> <br /> In either case though, as ST the only way I would allow PCs to make any kind of item that could be used by anybody (even sleepers) with the equivalent of pushing a button - would be to have that item be a Talisman/Device.<br /> <br /> Is this purely hypothetical, or does it have some relevance to a chronicle you're in as ST or player?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","user":"JoeDuncan","date":". 09-13-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:59:29-07:00","id":968913,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a> That's one of the most difficult concepts of Mage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> Ok. Again, a big &quot;no&quot; to number 2 question. I really don't know what I expected as an answer. To me it's really a flaw in the system. My answer would be that the etherite simply doesn't know and would probably try to find the problem and give up or maybe start to discover the purple paradigm. This could even be a way to start dropping his instruments (after Arete 6).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1815\" data-vbnamecard=\"1815\">JoeDuncan</a> Five Eyes got it. Will is a very broad and confusing term in Mage. The hermetic use it when pointing and shooting with the wand, of course. But when you bring this to etherite (or even worse, technocrats) the &quot;Will&quot; part gets more confusing.<br /> Your, and almost everyone here, answer is a valid one. I just don't think its the better one, I prefer the one I gave in this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:03:20-07:00","id":968916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968913#post968913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ok. Again, a big &quot;no&quot; to number 2 question. I really don't know what I expected as an answer. To me it's really a flaw in the system. My answer would be that the etherite simply doesn't know and would probably try to find the problem and give up or maybe start to discover the purple paradigm. This could even be a way to start dropping his instruments (after Arete 6)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, you've answered your own question, and I bet this will be the only answer you'll accept.<br /> <br /> Go home everyone, the answer has been found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:05:02-07:00","id":969328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968913#post968913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a> That's one of the most difficult concepts of Mage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1815\" data-vbnamecard=\"1815\">JoeDuncan</a> Five Eyes got it. Will is a very broad and confusing term in Mage. The hermetic use it when pointing and shooting with the wand, of course. But when you bring this to etherite (or even worse, technocrats) the &quot;Will&quot; part gets more confusing.<br /> Your, and almost everyone here, answer is a valid one. I just don't think its the better one, I prefer the one I gave in this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes &quot;Will&quot; such a &quot;difficult concept&quot; in Mage? It's pretty clearly spelled out in a number of places, but this will do:<br /> <br /> &quot;While all mages are willworkers, bringing about effects by imposing their will on the Tapestry,<b> it is hubris to imagine that an Awakened mage may simply think of something and have it occur</b>.&quot;<br /> ...<br /> &quot;Instead,<b> each mage comes to an understanding of magic through the rituals and trappings of a particular style of magic, which focuses their will </b>and resonates through the Tapestry...&quot;<br /> ...<br /> &quot;Integral to all paradigms, especially at the beginning of a mage's Awakened life, are foci: magical tools and rituals which focus the mage's will. <b>Foci are the practical expression of the paradigm, the means by which the mage turns his internal understanding into reality</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> (from here: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Paradigm\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Paradigm</a>)<br /> <br /> Seems pretty clear to me.<br /> <br /> A mage's &quot;Will&quot; is simply what they want, or wish to happen. For the vast majority of them (who aren't enlightened masters), they CANNOT *execute* their &quot;Will&quot; by simply thinking about it - they HAVE to use their foci in a *physical* expression/correlate of that Will.<br /> <br /> For Mages of mystic paradigms, they can eventually reach a level of enlightenment where they realize the &quot;Truth&quot; and are able to abandon their foci. The only reason mystic mages are able to do this is because their paradigms *allow* for magic to be accomplished by simply &quot;thinking&quot; about it.<br /> <br /> Technomancers are unable to abandon their foci because their paradigm doesn't allow for it, the technomantic paradigm rules out the possibility of firing laser blasts by just thinking hard enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:38:04-07:00","id":969525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968822#post968822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it. You answered number 2 yes, which means he can activate is with a touch of a button. But later you said that it needs a preparation...in the battlefield? What would that preparation be, teaching a path?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop it with the blatant dishonesty and misrepresentation.<br /> <br /> This is what I said:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=968612#post968612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Yes. However, his preparations will need to be at least partially incorporated into himself. <b>It's not in the gun, it's in the Etherite + gun + circumstances.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>In <i>exact parallel</i> to the Hermetic's case.<br /> <br /> The Etherite would need to prepare the Sleeper in <i>exactly the way</i> that the Etherite prepared himself in question 2, in a way that won't degrade. That is, he has to use the Sleeper as part of his instrument, so that they can enact the Procedure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. Then the answer of my question number 2 should be no, since you're requiring the to be a kickass cybor with the right drivers and smartlink setup. </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see!<br /> <br /> Then the answer to <i>all of the questions</i> is no. The Hermetic can't prepare the wand independently of all other circumstances, including the Hermetic himself. Because all things are connected in the Hermetic paradigm, and to ignore the various circumstances and one's own ritual preparaedness like some undisciplined rube is to fail.<br /> <br /> Otherwise he's casting without foci and has to take a +3 difficulty penalty and spend a point of Willpower.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So let me ask you a question. If a fellow Etherite which uses &quot;devices and machines&quot; instrument and has Forces 2, but isn't a kickas cyborg with the right drivers and smartlink setup gets the gun and shoots. Visually, he's just like that sleeper that couldn't use it. What would the kickass cyborg think? </div> </div> </div>This is an Iterator. The Etherite is a Reality Deviant, he's clearly doing something weird. Possibly psychic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's become apparent you're not even bothering to read the content of anyone else's posts anymore. Do you have any reason I shouldn't consider this actively malicious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-14-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:57:21-07:00","id":969538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=969328#post969328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technomancers are unable to abandon their foci because their paradigm doesn't allow for it, the technomantic paradigm rules out the possibility of firing laser blasts by just thinking hard enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, Technomancers among the Traditions and in Revised those among the Technocracy <i>can</i> learn to abandon their foci at Arete/Enlightenment 6 - which probably comes with the same sort of worldview-shattering trauma and horrified realization you'd expect from encountering such a Truth.<br /> <br /> Naturally, such a Technomancer is no longer so limited as the ones we're discussing here, because they don't actually <i>have</i> to use their paradigmatic limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:26:32-07:00","id":970225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=969538#post969538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking, Technomancers among the Traditions and in Revised those among the Technocracy <i>can</i> learn to abandon their foci at Arete/Enlightenment 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I don't own any of the splatbooks or Revised though.<br /> <br /> Either way, the question of what an Etherite would think if a Sleeper tried to duplicate their firing of a laser blast but failed is pretty easy to answer.<br /> <br /> If the Etherite has reached the level of abandoning his foci, he's also reached an understanding of the Purple Paradigm and therefore knows *exactly* why it didn't work for the Sleeper - no confusion.<br /> <br /> If the Etherite has not abandoned their foci yet, then the only way to for him to fire a laser blast by just pushing a button is to use a Device, which should also work for the Sleeper. Without a Device, the Etherite would have to physically execute a complex Procedure with his foci before firing. If a Sleeper tried the same and failed, the Etherite would just blame it on the Sleeper's incompetence - again, no confusion.<br /> <br /> Revan's main confusion seems to be that he thinks that journeymen Mages of all stripes are able to execute Rotes/Procedures by simply thinking about it hard enough, and without performing complicated physical actions in order to make their Will manifest.<br /> <br /> Basically, he doesn't seem to grasp how foci work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","user":"JoeDuncan","date":". 09-15-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:25:00-07:00","id":970370,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1815\" data-vbnamecard=\"1815\">JoeDuncan</a> All mystic mages can cast effects without any instrument, using nothing but their Will by the cost of 1 WP and +3 diff on Arete.<br /> <br /> My issue isn't with mages willworking effects, but instruments used without such complexity outside the mage mind. I know the etherite is in reality using his enlightened Will. I also disagree that etherites can't build devices that activate (aparently) by a single button (we know the magick is in its creation and the etherite Will on the time of activation). And I know that to make it work for sleepers it would have to be a device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:21:01-07:00","id":970405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970370#post970370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue isn't with mages willworking effects, but instruments used without such complexity outside the mage mind. I know the etherite is in reality using his enlightened Will. I also disagree that etherites can't build devices that activate (aparently) by a single button (we know the magick is in its creation and the etherite Will on the time of activation). And I know that to make it work for sleepers it would have to be a device.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are free to assume that. It isn't compatible with a paradigm that believes the character's power comes from understanding and manipulating outside forces, but you can make that assumption.<br /> <br /> It is nonetheless not the only possible interpretation, and many of us here like to have Technomancers who believe that the power is in their instruments and foci, not specific to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-15-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:39:02-07:00","id":970641,"title":"","content":"I think that, as long as the Mage is conscious and in sight, the tool will work because the Mage will be forced by her paradigm to unconsciously use her magic to make the tool work. The Avatar of the Mage will force the Mage to drop everything else so that her paradigm will not be violated. Of course, that offers unique challenges, like the fact that she is being forced to power the device that kills her if the Sleeper turns against her, but paradigms are more important than life to Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:46:46-07:00","id":970642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970641#post970641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, as long as the Mage is conscious and in sight, the tool will work because the Mage will be forced by her paradigm to unconsciously use her magic to make the tool work. The Avatar of the Mage will force the Mage to drop everything else so that her paradigm will not be violated. Of course, that offers unique challenges, like the fact that she is being forced to power the device that kills her if the Sleeper turns against her, but paradigms are more important than life to Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that. I like that a lot actually. The only problem with it is that it sort of borders on Marauder territory in that their inventions only work within their &quot;sphere of influence&quot;. But then that can be somewhat fitting for certain kinds of Etherite. &quot;Mad Scientist&quot; is a stock character after all.<br /> <br /> I think this is the sort of thing that would make more sense as a form of Quiet than a standard mechanic for all Technomancers to employ. It would especially work as a form of Denial. &quot;What do you mean it doesn't work when I leave the room? It's working right now! Try it!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:14:34-07:00","id":970671,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that the mechanic would work for any Mage that uses tools that should be useful for Sleepers, whether they are death rays or magic carpets. I tend to think that all Mages have Quiet 0 and their Avatars are trying to constantly shape local reality to reflect their paradigms. Marauders just have a stronger Quiet that gives discernable benefits to Marauder Mages. In effect, Marauders are just the truest manifestation of what a Mage is and should be.<br /> <br /> A fun NPC to throw into any Mage game is a Marauder with Quiet 1 because the effects of the Quiet are quite subtle. If the ST plays the Marauder right, the players will be unable to figure out why the NPC is so successful and why the PCs are accumulating so much Paradox. I would suggest though that the ST makes the magic rolls for the players, so the players do not know where their Paradox is coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:42:33-07:00","id":970686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970671#post970671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest that the mechanic would work for any Mage that uses tools that should be useful for Sleepers, whether they are death rays or magic carpets. I tend to think that all Mages have Quiet 0 and their Avatars are trying to constantly shape local reality to reflect their paradigms. Marauders just have a stronger Quiet that gives discernable benefits to Marauder Mages. In effect, Marauders are just the truest manifestation of what a Mage is and should be..</div> </div> </div> </div>I dispute that a Marauder is the truest manifestation of a Mage and represents what they should be. Marauders are effectively walking Echo Chambers. Anything that does not fit into their world view is either removed or changed into something that does, be that internally or externally. Such activity goes directly against what it means to reach true Ascension, which is, as I see it, to be able to move beyond your earthly trappings, to shrug off the need to have your world view as correct, and to understand that control is merely an illusion, a trick we tell ourselves in order to feel powerful, something we try to convince other off in order to feel justified in our belief.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy are all about controlling mass acceptance of paradigm, the Mad are more about extreme control of ones paradigm at a local level. While the technocracy need everyone else to belive things the way they do, the Mad don't need to, because their belief is so strong that other people become irrelevant.<br /> <br /> The job of the Mage, as I see it, is to balance the needs of the many with the needs of one's self. To deny the self is step in line with Technocratic reasoning, to deny the many is to step towards the Mad. Whereas to deny both is to become on par with the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-16-2016, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:27:52-07:00","id":970770,"title":"","content":"I personally see the development of Arete to be symptomatic of the failure to Ascend. You see a portion of the truth when you Awaken, enough to develop Arete, but some personality flaw prevents you from Ascending. Some Mages are able to address their personality flaw and Ascend, but the majority are incapable of the required level of self-reflection and just accumulate magical power until they are killed or are forced from the Earth because they have become too alien to remain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:47:45-07:00","id":970777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970642#post970642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like that. I like that a lot actually. The only problem with it is that it sort of borders on Marauder territory in that their inventions only work within their &quot;sphere of influence&quot;. But then that can be somewhat fitting for certain kinds of Etherite. &quot;Mad Scientist&quot; is a stock character after all.<br /> <br /> I think this is the sort of thing that would make more sense as a form of Quiet than a standard mechanic for all Technomancers to employ. It would especially work as a form of Denial. &quot;What do you mean it doesn't work when I leave the room? It's working right now! Try it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine most Etherites would rationalize it as a finicky invention they needed to keep in tune, so if its out of their sight for more than a minute or two it can't be relied upon. You want reliability, you make a Device (that's the term for a technological Talisman, right?), otherwise you keep pliers on hand. <br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that this isn't even the first time we've seen a magic roll that that the player was aware of but the mage himself wasn't. I forget which book it is in but Technocrats have a technique where they can use statistical or structural analysis to &quot;observe&quot; that an event, like the ceiling collapsing on a reality deviant, is about to happen. In actuality they are causing the event, but they don't realize they are doing anything at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:12:58-07:00","id":970793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970370#post970370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1815\" data-vbnamecard=\"1815\">JoeDuncan</a> All mystic mages can cast effects without any instrument, using nothing but their Will by the cost of 1 WP and +3 diff on Arete.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure those rules are for when a mystic mage wants to cast a rote, but doesn't have their foci, or their foci have been destroyed etc...<br /> <br /> I could be wrong, but as far as I recall, while it is technically possible for a mystic mage to cast a rote without their <b>normal </b>foci, doing so *still* requires the mage to use some kind of improvised foci or physical expression of their Will. It's different than &quot;surpassing&quot; or &quot;abandoning&quot; your foci at arete 6; these are *penalties* for missing foci, not a shortcut to enlightenment. The foci are still required, and the mage is penalized for not having their pre-prepared ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970370#post970370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also disagree that etherites can't build devices that activate (aparently) by a single button (we know the magick is in its creation and <b>the etherite Will on the time of activation</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they can - by making a Device.<br /> <br /> You still don't seem to get that &quot;the etherite WIll on the time of activation&quot; <b>MUST</b> constitute something *more* than a mere trigger pull and mentally &quot;wishing on a star&quot;. It must be represented by something that the Etherite does which is too complex for Sleepers to simply copy - otherwise the Etherite is activating a Device and not executing a Procedure (hanging or otherwise).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:42:34-07:00","id":970804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970777#post970777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine most Etherites would rationalize it as a finicky invention they needed to keep in tune, so if its out of their sight for more than a minute or two it can't be relied upon. You want reliability, you make a Device (that's the term for a technological Talisman, right?), otherwise you keep pliers on hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Device is Talisman, Invention is Artifact, Gadget is Charm, etc. The requirements for &quot;make this actually work without my personal intervention/observation&quot; are actually very very low - anyone with the barest meta-physical influence (Prime 2) can pull it off, even if that only gives it Arete x 2 &quot;charges&quot; per Forged by Dragon's Fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also worth noting that this isn't even the first time we've seen a magic roll that that the player was aware of but the mage himself wasn't. I forget which book it is in but Technocrats have a technique where they can use statistical or structural analysis to &quot;observe&quot; that an event, like the ceiling collapsing on a reality deviant, is about to happen. In actuality they are causing the event, but they don't realize they are doing anything at all. </div> </div> </div>As long as it's subtle enough, Passive-Aggressive Troll Casting is an <i>amazing</i> tool for &quot;I'm just that good&quot; paradigm-facets. Easy to explain away when it fails too, with &quot;no, that was just not a correct observation&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970793#post970793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure those rules are for when a mystic mage wants to cast a rote, but doesn't have their foci, or their foci have been destroyed etc...<br /> <br /> I could be wrong, but as far as I recall, while it is technically possible for a mystic mage to cast a rote without their <b>normal </b>foci, doing so *still* requires the mage to use some kind of improvised foci or physical expression of their Will. It's different than &quot;surpassing&quot; or &quot;abandoning&quot; your foci at arete 6; these are *penalties* for missing foci, not a shortcut to enlightenment. The foci are still required, and the mage is penalized for not having their pre-prepared ones.\\</div> </div> </div> </div>You're wrong. Mysticks can just use wishcasting with that rule. Essentially, they''re borrowing from the Traditions meta-paradigm, which says &quot;everything is just the enacting of pure Will on reality&quot;, which while true violates them actually <i>having</i> their own Paradigm. In my headcanon, they've been indoctrinated into it, but don't <i>fully</i> believe it except as dogma until Arete 6 (I use Revised's placement of everyone on equal footing), so it's ridiculously difficult for them to pull off.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy meta-paradigm, &quot;the power is in a tool/people with Genius are more talented than the unEnlightened/etc.&quot; is... considerably easier to swallow for people in the organization. By design, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Of course, Technomancers <i>can't</i> use that rule, so its relevance to this topic is tenuous at best, and I'm not sure why Revan thought it would help his case. Rather than showing &quot;wait, no, Etherites <i>can't</i> actually violate their Paradigm and make things they think are impossible happen&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-16-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:59:19-07:00","id":970814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970793#post970793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure those rules are for when a mystic mage wants to cast a rote, but doesn't have their foci, or their foci have been destroyed etc...<br /> <br /> I could be wrong, but as far as I recall, while it is technically possible for a mystic mage to cast a rote without their <b>normal </b>foci, doing so *still* requires the mage to use some kind of improvised foci or physical expression of their Will. It's different than &amp;quot;surpassing&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;abandoning&amp;quot; your foci at arete 6; these are *penalties* for missing foci, not a shortcut to enlightenment. The foci are still required, and the mage is penalized for not having their pre-prepared ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This means a mystic mage can cast effects even without any instrument. Not just withou his normal instruments,this would be casting with differemt instruments. But without anything. The mage simply wish so hard it happens.<br /> But technomancers can't do that though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970793#post970793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure they can - by making a Device.<br /> <br /> You still don't seem to get that &amp;quot;the etherite WIll on the time of activation&amp;quot; <b>MUST</b> constitute something *more* than a mere trigger pull and mentally &amp;quot;wishing on a star&amp;quot;. It must be represented by something that the Etherite does which is too complex for Sleepers to simply copy - otherwise the Etherite is activating a Device and not executing a Procedure (hanging or otherwise).</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It's not that I don't &quot;get&quot; i just don't have any reason to think this way other thsn you guys saying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:37:41-07:00","id":970882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970814#post970814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Exactly. It's not that I don't &quot;get&quot; i just don't have any reason to think this way other thsn you guys saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>Consensus drives reality. If enough people agree on something, then it becomes equivalent to truth. That's how Mage works both in theme and in mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:42:10-07:00","id":970888,"title":"","content":"Consensus shapes magic. If enough people agree that something is not magical, it stops being magical and becomes mundane. That's Mage 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:58:38-07:00","id":970898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970804#post970804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're wrong. Mysticks can just use wishcasting with that rule. Essentially, they''re borrowing from the Traditions meta-paradigm, which says &quot;everything is just the enacting of pure Will on reality&quot;, which while true violates them actually <i>having</i> their own Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, on a purely technical interpretation of the rule mechanics, it is *possible* for mystic mages to &quot;wishcast&quot;, but I'm skeptical that the intent was to allow mystic mages a shortcut to arete enlightenment, as opposed to penalizing them for not having the correct foci or being unable to improvise something.<br /> <br /> From a fluff/flavour perspective, it's highly unlikely that the intent of those rules was to be like &quot;hey, completely intangible wish casting for all!!! Yay!!!!&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the end it's all up to how much rules lawyering and power gaming the ST will allow, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:07:59-07:00","id":970902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970814#post970814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. It's not that I don't &quot;get&quot; i just don't have any reason to think this way other thsn you guys saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, man, you asked how X was possible, we said it wasn't for a proper Technomancer (without Arete 6+ etc. etc.).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick#post966290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, technomancers don't believe in magick. They always have a good scientific explanation for everything. But they know that other traditions can make effects and they often look like magic, even though in the technomancers mind, it's just a trick.<br /> <br /> Also, almost all technomancer build and use devices to cast effects. <b>How coule they explain a device working for them and not for a sleeper?</b><br /> If a technomancer builds a laser gun that all he habe to do is pull a trigger, how could it not work if a sleeper pull it? You know, a lot of devices don't require an &quot;enlightened mind&quot; specially those that were build with a sinple trigger. We do this all the time in real life, we don't have to know how electricity works to turn a switch and light the light bulb.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't want to accept that, <i>come up with a fucking answer yourself</i> and stop wasting everyone's time with your total unwillingness to consider viewpoints you yourself asked for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-16-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:09:27-07:00","id":970903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970898#post970898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, on a purely technical interpretation of the rule mechanics, it is *possible* for mystic mages to &quot;wishcast&quot;, but I'm skeptical that the intent was to allow mystic mages a shortcut to arete enlightenment, as opposed to penalizing them for not having the correct foci or being unable to improvise something.<br /> <br /> From a fluff/flavour perspective, it's highly unlikely that the intent of those rules was to be like &quot;hey, completely intangible wish casting for all!!! Yay!!!!&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the end it's all up to how much rules lawyering and power gaming the ST will allow, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a shortcut. It's insanely difficult for them. Gaining Arete lets you do so trivially, without lying to yourself, and just makes things easier when you do use a focus. Now, yes, it's also blatantly asymmetric, but they did that with the Arete enlightenment too, so that's not really a good reason that the developers wouldn't do that.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;fuck The Man/coherency&quot; is all the reason the authors would need to actually deliberately put that into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-16-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:11:24-07:00","id":970909,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I never allowed people to use Abilities or to spend Quintessence to reduce difficulty when they were 'wishcasting', which meant that the difficulty of even the simplest rotes were a minimum of '7' in my games. That meant that most damaging effects in front of witnesses would be a minimum difficulty of '11' with wishcasting, which translated to difficulty '9' minus two success, which meant that 'wishcasting' was a good way to botch a vulgar magic roll in front of witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:21:19-07:00","id":970914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970903#post970903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a shortcut..</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we'll just have to disagree on that.<br /> <br /> For you, those rules were meant to represent an every day normal routine method for mages to cast spells without using foci, if they just don't feel like grabbing their wand out of their rucksack.<br /> <br /> I on the other hand, view those rules as an emergency &quot;hail mary&quot; &quot;oh shit, I don't have my foci WTF am I going to do?!?&quot;; a &quot;last resort&quot; method of casting when they have no other choice, instead of just a matter of convenience for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T15:00:33-07:00","id":970930,"title":"","content":"Yes, last resort is a good description in my mind as well. I think that is why most of my players never took their foci for granted. If they lacked their foci, they were screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:58:00-07:00","id":970984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970804#post970804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're wrong. Mysticks can just use wishcasting with that rule. Essentially, they''re borrowing from the Traditions meta-paradigm, which says &quot;everything is just the enacting of pure Will on reality&quot;, which while true violates them actually <i>having</i> their own Paradigm. In my headcanon, they've been indoctrinated into it, but don't <i>fully</i> believe it except as dogma until Arete 6 (I use Revised's placement of everyone on equal footing), so it's ridiculously difficult for them to pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, do you happen to remember where that rule is. I specifically remember it, and I thought it was somewhere in Revised, but every time I go looking for it I can't find it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T19:21:33-07:00","id":971089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970914#post970914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess we'll just have to disagree on that.<br /> <br /> <b>For you, those rules were meant to represent an every day normal routine method for mages to cast spells without using foci, if they just don't feel like grabbing their wand out of their rucksack.</b><br /> <br /> I on the other hand, view those rules as an emergency &quot;hail mary&quot; &quot;oh shit, I don't have my foci WTF am I going to do?!?&quot;; a &quot;last resort&quot; method of casting when they have no other choice, instead of just a matter of convenience for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're putting words in my mouth. <i>Stop it</i>.<br /> <br /> I didn't suggest that it was normal or everyday. It <i>is</i> a desperation move. It's willing something to just happen, without prior cause aside from the Mage's will. It's violating the very thing that normally lets you do magic at all. And that. Is. Fucking. Hard. +3 difficulty and a Willpower surcharge hard, which given what spending Willpower <i>represents</i> is a pretty clear indicator that it's not supposed to be something you do on a whim.<br /> <br /> The benefit is that they can do that <i>at all</i>. It's when you get to high Arete that it's actually <i>easy</i>, because someone with Arete 8+ doesn't even <i>need</i> foci for the majority of their Spheres known.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970984#post970984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, do you happen to remember where that rule is. I specifically remember it, and I thought it was somewhere in Revised, but every time I go looking for it I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>*checks* Surpassing Foci, page 203.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T19:22:26-07:00","id":971091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970902#post970902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, man, you asked how X was possible, we said it wasn't for a proper Technomancer (without Arete 6+ etc. etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>That`s not what I asked for. I asked for what he would think, considering he saw someone failing to activate his instrument. I had the premise that he was able to craft such a instrument that is activated instantly in the frist place. Everyone gave their opinion. That`s nice, helped to form my own about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970902#post970902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't want to accept that, <i>come up with a fucking answer yourself</i> and stop wasting everyone's time with your total unwillingness to consider viewpoints you yourself asked for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That`s already what I fucking did. Also I`m not pointing a fucking gun in your head and asking for answers, if you are so annoyed by this thread get the fuck out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T19:23:52-07:00","id":971092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971089#post971089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're putting words in my mouth. <i>Stop it</i>.<br /> <br /> I didn't suggest that it was normal or everyday. It <i>is</i> a desperation move. It's willing something to just happen, without prior cause aside from the Mage's will. It's violating the very thing that normally lets you do magic at all. And that. Is. Fucking. Hard. +3 difficulty and a Willpower surcharge hard, which given what spending Willpower <i>represents</i> is a pretty clear indicator that it's not supposed to be something you do on a whim.<br /> <br /> The benefit is that they can do that <i>at all</i>. It's when you get to high Arete that it's actually <i>easy</i>, because someone with Arete 8+ doesn't even <i>need</i> foci for the majority of their Spheres known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:53:00-07:00","id":971120,"title":"","content":"For what it counts, thank you guys for this thread. Years ago I had wondered about this exact problem. And it seems it wasn't exactly a black and white issue (things in Mage rarely seem to be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:50:03-07:00","id":971171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=967364#post967364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Can an hermetic &quot;prepare&quot; a spell in the tranquility of his home enchanting his wand (or whatever instrument) with a Forces 2 effect only to make it levitate anything(up to Forces 2 weight limit) that its pointed by it with just a magick word? Remember, no Time or Prime used.<br /> <br /> 2- Can an etherite &quot;prepare&quot; a spell by building a gravity gun in the tranquility of his lab with a Forces 2 effect, only to make it levitate things (up to Forces 2 weight limit) that are pointed by the gun and &quot;shooted&quot; (pulling a trigger)? It's the same as the #1 question, without Prime or Time, just like the hermetic example.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yes. The exact spheres involved may differ substantially, and the preparations involved will differ <i>dramatically</i>, but yes, they can do that. The Hermetic mage is probably using Spirit, too, and carving the names of angels/demons/God into the wand in Enochian, while the Etherite probably needs Matter . . . but yes, its possible. They'd still need to work some sort of &quot;power supply&quot; into the mix (even if unconsciously) . . .but yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3- If the hermetic hands his wand to his sleeper friend and tells him to say the magic word while pointing it to a tennis ball to make it levitate, it will levitate?<br /> <br /> 4- If the etherite hands his gravity gun to his sleeper friend and tells him to pull the trigger while aiming at a tennis ball to make it levitate, it will? </div> </div> </div>That gets messier. It depends on what the Sleeper believes, and what the local Consensus will accept. You've just added a Witness, after all, and most reality zones don't allow levitation/antigravity.<br /> <br /> In all four examples, the object levitates because of the mage's Avatar imposing his will on reality. What <i>was </i>a Coincidental effect when the mage was all alone can easily become Vulgar with Witnesses when the Sleeper friend shows up, with all the nasty potential for Paradox that presents<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what would the etherite think when he sees that only fellow etherites with knowledge of Forces 2 can make the gravity gun work?<br /> <br /> Please, answer only this question and consider that it is not a Wonder, it has not a complicated trigger, just like the hermetic, all the complications were already made in his lab.<br /> <br /> <b>what would the etherite think when he sees that only fellow etherites with knowledge of Forces 2 can make the gravity gun work?</b><br /> <br /> Won't he realise that the power isn't from his device, but from the user and this wouldn't fuck with all his theories? </div> </div> </div>Not really. The Consensus isn't just a passive force opposing magic, its an active phenomenon that tries to force spells back into agreement with the local reality zone. Known in some editions as Unbelief, this is the reason why there aren't Nephandic demon armies battling T-rex cyborgs from the Technocracy in the middle of NYC. There can't be. &quot;That which should not exist, does not&quot; - even if the Consensus has to take a sledgehammer to it.<br /> <br /> Take the example of the lightning gun mentioned earlier. If its not fully grounded in scientific principles acceptable to the local Consensus, sooner or later, its going to get slagged. Depending on what the technomancer used to build it, it might short out (in a tech-friendly reality zone). Or catch fire. Or explode. Because that's what the Consensus says <i>has</i> to happen.<br /> <br /> There is no lightning gun. There never was one. Just a goofy machine that had no chance of working properly.<br /> <br /> Even to a technomancer, the destruction will <i>look</i> &quot;right&quot; - at least in a scientific reality zone - as if the lightning gun suffered some sort of serious malfunction. Melted plastic, fried resistors . . . If anything, the destruction would probably <i>reaffirm</i> his paradigm, because when he takes the ruined lightning gun apart to evaluate the damage, it will all be &quot;correct&quot; (from a scientific standpoint).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 09-17-2016, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:48:49-07:00","id":971685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971171#post971171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, yes. The exact spheres involved may differ substantially, and the preparations involved will differ <i>dramatically</i>, but yes, they can do that. The Hermetic mage is probably using Spirit, too, and carving the names of angels/demons/God into the wand in Enochian, while the Etherite probably needs Matter . . . but yes, its possible. They'd still need to work some sort of &quot;power supply&quot; into the mix (even if unconsciously) . . .but yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. If the effect itself doesn't involve spirits or the spirit world, the hermetic won't need Spirit sphere. This is the kind of house rule we see in HDYDT that completely goes against all Mage books ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971171#post971171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That gets messier. It depends on what the Sleeper believes, and what the local Consensus will accept. You've just added a Witness, after all, and most reality zones don't allow levitation/antigravity.<br /> <br /> In all four examples, the object levitates because of the mage's Avatar imposing his will on reality. What <i>was </i>a Coincidental effect when the mage was all alone can easily become Vulgar with Witnesses when the Sleeper friend shows up, with all the nasty potential for Paradox that presents</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, wrong. What determines if something is vulgar or coincident isn't the presence of witnesses, but the acceptance of such an effect by the Consensus and, if you use Reality Zone rules, the place where it is cast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971171#post971171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. The Consensus isn't just a passive force opposing magic, its an active phenomenon that tries to force spells back into agreement with the local reality zone. Known in some editions as Unbelief, this is the reason why there aren't Nephandic demon armies battling T-rex cyborgs from the Technocracy in the middle of NYC. There can't be. &quot;That which should not exist, does not&quot; - even if the Consensus has to take a sledgehammer to it.<br /> <br /> Take the example of the lightning gun mentioned earlier. If its not fully grounded in scientific principles acceptable to the local Consensus, sooner or later, its going to get slagged. Depending on what the technomancer used to build it, it might short out (in a tech-friendly reality zone). Or catch fire. Or explode. Because that's what the Consensus says <i>has</i> to happen.<br /> <br /> There is no lightning gun. There never was one. Just a goofy machine that had no chance of working properly.<br /> <br /> Even to a technomancer, the destruction will <i>look</i> &quot;right&quot; - at least in a scientific reality zone - as if the lightning gun suffered some sort of serious malfunction. Melted plastic, fried resistors . . . If anything, the destruction would probably <i>reaffirm</i> his paradigm, because when he takes the ruined lightning gun apart to evaluate the damage, it will all be &quot;correct&quot; (from a scientific standpoint).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the effect of reality forcing spells&quot;back into agreement&quot; is the paradox effect. Of unbelief, depending on the effect.<br /> <br /> And the gun would only fail if the Arete roll fails. In a successfull roll, the Etherite would make it work as expected by him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:48:49-07:00","id":971686,"title":"","content":"Double post...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:19:58-07:00","id":971917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, yes. The exact spheres involved may differ substantially, and the preparations involved will differ <i>dramatically</i>, but yes, they can do that. The Hermetic mage is probably using Spirit, too, and carving the names of angels/demons/God into the wand in Enochian, while the Etherite probably needs Matter . . . but yes, its possible. They'd still need to work some sort of &quot;power supply&quot; into the mix (even if unconsciously) . . .but yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971685#post971685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong. If the effect itself doesn't involve spirits or the spirit world, the hermetic won't need Spirit sphere. This is the kind of house rule we see in HDYDT that completely goes against all Mage books ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, its in the corebook - see &quot;Lady into Tiger&quot;, where it discussed examples of how the same spell effect can be achieved with different combinations of spheres. . . which is often necessary, when comparing different paradigms. In this case, I'm assuming the Hermetic mage is invoking an air elemental (or possibly an angel) in order to get a &quot;wand of levitation&quot;, which would require the Spirit sphere, along with Forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That gets messier. It depends on what the Sleeper believes, and what the local Consensus will accept. You've just added a Witness, after all, and most reality zones don't allow levitation/antigravity.<br /> <br /> In all four examples, the object levitates because of the mage's Avatar imposing his will on reality. What <i>was </i>a Coincidental effect when the mage was all alone can easily become Vulgar with Witnesses when the Sleeper friend shows up, with all the nasty potential for Paradox that presents</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, wrong. What determines if something is vulgar or coincident isn't the presence of witnesses, but the acceptance of such an effect by the Consensus and, if you use Reality Zone rules, the place where it is cast.</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Mage in Sanctum, or otherwise insulated from Sleepers - Coincidental</li> <li>Sympathetic Sleeper in Mage's Sanctum - Coincidental</li> <li>Mage (alone) in hostile Reality Zone - Vulgar, no Witnesses</li> <li>Sleeper in hostile Reality Zone - Vulgar with Witnesses</li> </ul>Depending on where the mage is, his magic might be coincidental or vulgar. If its vulgar, and you bring the Sleeper in to demonstrate the Wand of Levitation (or Anti-Gravity Gun), you've added a Witness.<br /> <br /> Hence my analysis. When its just the mage, the levitation spell can be coincidental (and can't be Vulgar with Witnesses, because he's alone). However, if a Sleeper demonstrates it, it can (and probably will) be Vulgar with Witnesses. Thus, having a Sleeper use the wand/gun poses a drastically increased risk of Paradox.<br /> <br /> And with the risk of Paradox through the roof, there's a dramatically increased risk of a backlash destroying the wand/gun, in a way that reaffirms the local Consensus<br /> <br /> (On a side note - if you add enough witnesses, with the right beliefs, you change the local Consensus/Reality Zone)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:12:39-07:00","id":971987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971917#post971917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, its in the corebook - see &quot;Lady into Tiger&quot;, where it discussed examples of how the same spell effect can be achieved with different combinations of spheres. . . which is often necessary, when comparing different paradigms. In this case, I'm assuming the Hermetic mage is invoking an air elemental (or possibly an angel) in order to get a &quot;wand of levitation&quot;, which would require the Spirit sphere, along with Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you change the effect to manipulate Spirits to levitate someting, it's ok. But then, you won't need Forces 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971802#post971802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Mage in Sanctum, or otherwise insulated from Sleepers - Coincidental</li> <li>Sympathetic Sleeper in Mage's Sanctum - Coincidental</li> <li>Mage (alone) in hostile Reality Zone - Vulgar, no Witnesses</li> <li>Sleeper in hostile Reality Zone - Vulgar with Witnesses</li> </ul>Depending on where the mage is, his magic might be coincidental or vulgar. If its vulgar, and you bring the Sleeper in to demonstrate the Wand of Levitation (or Anti-Gravity Gun), you've added a Witness.<br /> <br /> Hence my analysis. When its just the mage, the levitation spell can be coincidental (and can't be Vulgar with Witnesses, because he's alone). However, if a Sleeper demonstrates it, it can (and probably will) be Vulgar with Witnesses. Thus, having a Sleeper use the wand/gun poses a drastically increased risk of Paradox.<br /> <br /> And with the risk of Paradox through the roof, there's a dramatically increased risk of a backlash destroying the wand/gun, in a way that reaffirms the local Consensus<br /> <br /> (On a side note - if you add enough witnesses, with the right beliefs, you change the local Consensus/Reality Zone)</div> </div> </div> </div>You proved my point. The Consensus of the area determines vulgarity. Witnessess just makes it hard, if vulgar, in the Arete roll and paradox in cases of botch. What I mean is that the wand won't be coincident because the mage is alone. It could be if he's in a reaity zone, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:05:28-07:00","id":972057,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Lady Into Tiger&quot; example illustrated the difference between two approaches that were radically different, not just in Paradigm. The one is using Life to physically transform herself into a tiger. The other is using VR gear and Correspondence to direct a Forces simulation of a tiger made of force fields and light. There is a radical difference between shapeshifting and remotely controlled hard light holograms.<br /> <br /> What is the mechanical difference between a wand causing something to levitate and a gravity gun causing something to levitate? Nothing. It's Forces either way. That the Hermetic etched the names of archangels and airy spirits means nothing from a Sphere perspective, unless the Hermetic is literally calling upon those umbrood to use their spirit Charms to do the magic. The invocation of higher powers is a Paradigm thing, not a mechanics thing. Indeed, the Hermetic is probably of the opinion that the power to make something levitate comes entirely from his own Will; placating godforms is a formality inherent to the western esoteric tradition.<br /> <br /> And what's this about the Etherite needing Matter for the Gravity Gun? What does Matter have to do with levitation? The gravity gun itself is an Instrument - a tool for other Effects. It does not need Matter just to exist, and the only reason you would apply Matter to it is in a separate Effect to strengthen the object itself. The manipulation of gravity doesn't require Matter at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:26:52-07:00","id":972163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971987#post971987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You proved my point. The Consensus of the area determines vulgarity. Witnessess just makes it hard, if vulgar, in the Arete roll and paradox in cases of botch. What I mean is that the wand won't be coincident because the mage is alone. It could be if he's in a reaity zone, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't my quote. Also, I pretty much agree with you in this case. Under most circumstances if it was coincidental without a sleeper it should be coincidental with one. There is the question of if an expert witness could see something that a typical witness would not. I believe that is left up to the ST though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:18:06-07:00","id":972221,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry. Must have confused with the CTRL+V in quoting. My appologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:36:37-07:00","id":972649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=972057#post972057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And what's this about the Etherite needing Matter for the Gravity Gun? What does Matter have to do with levitation? The gravity gun itself is an Instrument - a tool for other Effects. It does not need Matter just to exist, and the only reason you would apply Matter to it is in a separate Effect to strengthen the object itself. The manipulation of gravity doesn't require Matter at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for finally pointing this out. If M20 did one thing completely right it was taking the vague mushy-headed vagueness that was the whole idea of &quot;Paradigm&quot; and actually make a (decent if if imperfect) stab at getting those concepts identified and broken out by coming up with Focus.<br /> <br /> Of course HDYDT completely tossed the whole thing back into the bin repeatedly with massive Sphere-bloat largely in place of the new Focus rules, but, oh well, they're at least THERE now.<br /> <br /> Effect = Spheres used<br /> How Effect is Manifested = Instruments<br /> (Practice &amp; Belief = Why those Instruments do that for you and yours)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:02:43-07:00","id":972797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=971089#post971089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't suggest that it was normal or everyday. It <i>is</i> a desperation move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is exactly what I said before, which you disagreed with.<br /> <br /> Since you actually DO agree with me, then what's all the fuss about? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T01:02:20-07:00","id":972985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=972797#post972797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, which is exactly what I said before, which you disagreed with.<br /> <br /> Since you actually DO agree with me, then what's all the fuss about?</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970898#post970898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, on a purely technical interpretation of the rule mechanics, it is *possible* for mystic mages to &quot;wishcast&quot;, but I'm skeptical that the intent was to allow mystic mages a shortcut to arete enlightenment, as opposed to penalizing them for not having the correct foci or being unable to improvise something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what you said.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/966290-how-technomancers-see-magick?p=970903#post970903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a shortcut. It's insanely difficult for them. Gaining Arete lets you do so trivially, without lying to yourself, and just makes things easier when you do use a focus. Now, yes, it's also blatantly asymmetric, but they did that with the Arete enlightenment too, so that's not really a good reason that the developers wouldn't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I said. Notice the disagreeing part being explicitly with the &quot;shortcut&quot; bit? And not about... whatever part was supposed to relate to it being 'a desperation move', and how I did in fact say it was incredibly difficult, absent having high Arete?<br /> <br /> That was the disagreement. Well, that, and me being upset at you seeming to cast it as something I explicitly agreed with you on. If I misunderstood what you meant by that line... I'm sorry. Maybe I was just nitpicking too much without realizing it.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm tired and hurt, and I'd like to be done with this mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-20-2016, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}